{\b
{\qc
2: Professor Cozmo\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Knock, knock, knock.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The sound of a door being knocked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come in."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing the voice, Johan was a little surprised but responded nonetheless.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a soft "click," a middle-aged man, dressed in light brown archaeologist attire and wearing round glasses, walked in, looking somewhat haggard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Cozmo."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Upon seeing the visitor, Johan quickly recalled the man's name from his memories.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Cozmo, full name Cozmo Takao, was a researcher specializing in meteorites and rocks. He was also a history professor at Kanaz Pok\u233?mon University, with his office right next to Johan's Pok\u233?mon Psychology Consultation Room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Like Johan, Professor Cozmo's history class was one of those rarely sought-after courses, and his focus on meteorites and rocks was an even more niche topic than Pok\u233?mon psychology.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The difference was that Professor Cozmo was a genuine Ph.D.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan." Professor Cozmo forced a smile. "Could you make me a cup of coffee?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Watching Professor Cozmo slowly walk over to the table, pull out a chair, and sit down\u8212?especially noting the dark circles under his eyes\u8212?Johan asked in surprise, "Don't you dislike coffee?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Despite saying that, Johan still got up to prepare the coffee.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't mention it." Professor Cozmo shook his head wearily. "I haven't had a good night's sleep these past two days."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In no time, Johan skillfully brewed a cup of coffee and placed it in front of him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The rich aroma wafted through the room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It shows." Johan gestured toward Cozmo's thick dark circles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Cozmo chuckled bitterly, picked up the coffee, hesitated for a moment, then took a big gulp.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the next instant\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His entire face scrunched up like a crumpled piece of paper.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hiss, it's so bitter." Putting the cup down and frowning, he said, "I don't understand how you people can enjoy this stuff."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Soon after, his brow relaxed, and he seemed to regain a bit of energy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's all about the bitterness waking you up, isn't it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But it does help a little."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled silently.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Once you get used to it, you'll like it. You can apply to the administration for a coffee machine by then."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Cozmo shook his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Forget it. I'm rarely in the office anyway, so no need to waste resources."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan shrugged and changed the topic:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So, what's the new discovery that's kept you up for two days?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the mention of his discovery, Professor Cozmo's spirit lifted. He adjusted his glasses and said:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This time, we did indeed find an interesting rock\u8212?highly valuable for research. One of my students actually found it. But the lack of sleep isn't because of that."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After briefly describing the newly discovered stone, Professor Cozmo's enthusiasm quickly faded, and he slumped again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Scratching his hair, now resembling a bird's nest, he said in frustration:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I don't know what's going on. Ever since I got back, I've been having nightmare after nightmare for the past two days. I can't get a good night's sleep at all."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nightmares?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan paused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After glancing over Professor Cozmo, he spoke seriously, "You didn't happen to disturb something you shouldn't have, did you?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Something I shouldn't have disturbed?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Cozmo's face went pale instantly, and he stammered, "You, you mean\u8230? a ghost?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As an archaeologist who often dug into ancient sites, Professor Cozmo had heard many stories about people uncovering "ghosts," but he had never encountered one himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And in the world of Pok\u233?mon, "ghosts" weren't exactly rare.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan chuckled slightly, "Don't worry, it's more likely that some situation during your exploration caused anxiety or fear, triggering your subconscious to protect itself by manifesting those fears in dreams."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He continued to reassure him, "If there really was a ghost, it wouldn't just be showing up in your dreams, would it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Saying this, Johan stood up and walked toward the corner of the consultation room, where there was an extremely comfortable armchair.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was where he usually took his afternoon naps.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He patted the back of the chair. "How about I help you take a good rest?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Cozmo hesitated for a moment but quickly slapped his cheeks, then downed the rest of the coffee in one gulp. "Maybe later. Now that I feel a bit more awake, I need to finish my lesson plans before the semester starts."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing this, Johan let him be and lay down on the sofa himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Better hurry up, then."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His lesson plans were already finished.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There weren't that many, after all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Cozmo slapped his cheeks again and, after thanking Johan, strode out of the consultation room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Judging by his posture, it looked like another case of "one pen, one person, one night, one miracle."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rain softly tapped against the window, leaving specks of droplets like stars.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ugh..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan opened his groggy eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He realized, without noticing, that he had slept until evening, and the sky had already grown dim.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The once sunny afternoon had turned into a gray, misty scene. Raindrops danced in the air, casting a thin veil over the city, adding a touch of mystery.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, a low, raspy voice echoed faintly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Startled by the weak, eerie voice, Johan jolted awake and shouted, "Who's there?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's me, Cozmo."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only then did Johan see the figure standing in the dim light.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He exhaled in relief, rubbing the goosebumps on his arms as he slowly stood up. "Professor Cozmo, still not off work?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cozmo sighed. "I just finished. Even if I go home, I doubt I'll sleep. Since you're still here, I was hoping you could help me out."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Now?" Johan glanced outside. "Not heading home?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Got used to it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Johan stood up, Cozmo immediately laid down on the sofa.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, he was a bachelor, and to save time for research, he often slept at the university.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan rubbed his dry eyes, yawned, and pulled up a chair to sit beside him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Cozmo seemed ready, clasping his hands over his chest and closing his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"...Slowly, take a deep breath, hold it, and exhale... Now, you're relaxed. You're lying on a soft lawn, the warm sunshine..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's soothing, gentle voice, rich and calming, felt like a spring breeze brushing across the heart, helping the mind naturally relax.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was hypnosis.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Professor Cozmo's cooperation, it was fairly easy for Johan to lull him into a simple sleep-aid hypnosis.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In fact, according to the original owner's memories, this wasn't the first time he had helped Professor Cozmo fall asleep.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Soon enough, steady breathing came from Professor Cozmo.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rest well."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing Cozmo peacefully asleep, Johan stood up and carefully closed the door behind him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Time to clock out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, what Johan didn't know was that after he left, a faint red glow appeared on Professor Cozmo's chest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Next, tendrils of black smoke swirled and began to gather.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A pair of eyes emerged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They stared at the sleeping Professor Cozmo with displeasure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Soon, the look of displeasure gave way to curiosity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, the figure turned to gaze at the closed door, curiosity growing stronger in its eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
