{\qc
57: The Psychic Girl, Sabrina\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the game, evolving Kadabra into Alakazam is similar to evolving Haunter into Gengar, as both require a {\i
Trade Evolution}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Back before the introduction of the {\i
Link Cable} item, evolving Pok\u233?mon like Haunter into its final form was a hurdle single-player fans struggled to overcome.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, the situation is slightly different in the Pok\u233?mon world.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's because "trading" essentially replicates the special magnetic fields found in the wild, which are necessary to stimulate certain Pok\u233?mon to complete their evolution.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This explains why wild Alakazam, Gengar, and Golem are seen in the wild.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be honest, questions like these shouldn't be directed at someone like Johan, a Pok\u233?mon psychologist. Although not widely known, this is general knowledge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, after some thought, Johan decided to respond.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Grain in the Field]:} {\i
You could try using the Link Cable item or attempt Trade Evolution.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The response came faster than expected.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Psychic Girl]:} {\i
If that worked, why would I be asking you?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "??"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be honest, this was the first time he had encountered someone with such a short temper.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Birds of every feather, huh.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan patted his cheeks to snap himself out of his "keyboard warrior" mindset. He had a hunch that the person on the other end had quite a bad temper. If he butted heads with her...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Things could easily escalate into a "doctor-patient dispute."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, her words did make him think more deeply.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Typically, Pok\u233?mon like Kadabra or Haunter evolve immediately through the use of a Link Cable or Trade Evolution methods.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But from what she was saying, it seemed like she had already tried those methods without success.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since this world's reality can't follow game mechanics to the letter\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Grain in the Field]:} {\i
Can you describe Kadabra's current state or tell me what it usually does?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Psychic Girl]:} {\i
What else can it do? (eye-roll emoji) It just meditates, spaces out, and meditates again.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Grain in the Field]:} {\i
What about its eating and sleeping habits?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Psychic Girl]:} {\i
??? Do Psychic Pok\u233?mon need to sleep? Do you even know what you're talking about?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Taking a deep breath, Johan forced a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Grain in the Field]:} {\i
Well, I think you should try asking Kadabra what it wants. Even though it's a Psychic-type, it's not a machine. It has its own thoughts, routines, and preferences. It can't just be stuck meditating all the time.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Grain in the Field]:} {\i
Try adding some color to its life.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He wanted to add more, but noticed that the user had gone offline!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Ka-kah?"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gastly seemed to notice Johan's mood, floating over curiously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's nothing," Johan replied, waving it off with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Ka-kah~~"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gastly grinned and floated away to find Alolan Vulpix to play with.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
So, it's that whole "Psychic superiority complex" thing, huh?} Johan thought darkly. {\i
Maybe Mewtwo should give them all a reality check!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dangerous thoughts flickered in his eyes as he headed for the bathroom.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After splashing his face with cold water, Johan stared at his reflection in the mirror.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
My emotions are all over the place\u8230? It seems that taking in Vulpix has put an invisible strain on me.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This kind of mental state wasn't acceptable for a Pok\u233?mon psychologist and trainer. Not only could it impact himself, but it could also affect his Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Luckily, he realized it in time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Kanto Region\u8212?Saffron City}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the most prosperous city in Kanto, Saffron is home to the Pok\u233?mon world's corporate giant, Silph Co., as well as two powerful gyms.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Deep within the Psychic-type Gym lies a room cluttered with a multitude of plushies\u8212?some shaped like people and others resembling various Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seated among these plushies is a girl in her late teens, wearing a form-fitting red outfit and long, straight hair.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She is Sabrina, the Psychic-type Gym Leader.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Standing before her is her Kadabra.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Kadabra, do you need sleep?" Sabrina asked flatly, pressing a hand to her forehead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before Kadabra could answer, Sabrina's eyes began to glow with an eerie blue light.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In sync, Kadabra's eyes reflected the same blue glow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a slight shake of Sabrina's head, Kadabra awkwardly mirrored her movement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing this, Sabrina smiled softly and murmured:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"See? Psychic Pok\u233?mon don't need to sleep."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When the blue light in Sabrina's eyes faded, Kadabra returned to normal. A flicker of resistance crossed its eyes but quickly vanished.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Still\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina tilted her head slightly, as if reconsidering.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
