"Chu\u8212?Chu\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She'd found it while the Gym staff was cleaning up, tossed aside as garbage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They didn't want it\u8230? so it wasn't stealing, right?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All three Pok\u233?mon glanced over at Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing he was too busy with a tiny booklet to notice them, they let out a collective sigh of relief.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowu\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Probably not\u8230? Maybe it's\u8230? just recycling?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, this stone alone didn't have enough magnetism to trigger Haunter's evolution\u8212?Haunter had tried licking Nosepass directly before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the gesture still touched him deeply.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He gave Tinkatink a pat on the head, signaling her to keep it for herself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Chu?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Really?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tinkatink blinked her big lavender eyes in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Getting approval from both Haunter and Vulpix, she excitedly took out her tiny hammer and began tinkering with the stone, clinking and clanking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Phew\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed with relief, stretching his back.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The first draft of the midterm exam was done, and he'd add to it as ideas came to him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For now, it was a simple test. The questions were easy, covering only material from the book. As long as his students studied, they'd do just fine.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Man, I really am a nice teacher\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Turning around, he saw that the three Pok\u233?mon were behaving and not causing trouble, which improved his mood instantly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A peaceful day\u8230? this is nice."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He casually picked up his phone and started browsing comments online.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His popularity had dropped recently, so there weren't many new "clients" looking for advice, and the questions he got were all fairly simple.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But as he scrolled, one message caught his eye.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Who Am I]: How can I meet\u8230?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only half the message was there. Mewtwo's avatar was already grayed out, meaning he wasn't online.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meet\u8230? who?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meet a new friend? Or maybe Mewtwo No. 2?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had always kept an eye on Mewtwo, this "troubled case," in particular.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But now that it was clearly under Team Rocket's control, it probably wasn't easy for it to get online, let alone reach out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As Johan pondered ways to help Mewtwo learn to restrain its "Id," a new friend request popped up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[King of the Earth]: Accept.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Didn't this person try to add me before?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Once again, Johan hit "Decline."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His profile stated clearly that anyone wanting help should specify their Pok\u233?mon's condition.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He'd had plenty of random friend requests in the past, but they'd mostly stopped as his popularity dipped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This person was persistent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, at the Team Rocket HQ beneath Viridian City in Kanto\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Boss, we intercepted Mewtwo's communication, and we've managed to trace the other user's account," reported Matori, holding a tablet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her gaze lingered on the tray of carefully made Meowth-shaped cookies on Giovanni's desk, her eyes hopeful.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh? What cut it off?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni looked up from his files, noticing the cookies on his desk. He was feeling a bit peckish, so he grabbed one and bit down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He'd never been picky about food.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Matori's cheeks turned pink as she tightened her fists\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmm?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing she hadn't answered, Giovanni turned her way.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Snapping back, Matori stammered, "I-it was a power outage. Someone pulled the lab's main breaker."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni nodded thoughtfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So, it's that {\i
Grain in the Field} user?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Y-yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Give me the phone."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Taking the phone from Matori, Giovanni sent a friend request directly to "Grain in the Field."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seconds later, he laughed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He'd been declined.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thinking a moment, he sent another request.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This time, he was clear about who he was.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[King of the Earth]: I am Giovanni.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan stared at the friend request notification on his screen, mind blank.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
