[Little Growlithe]: Thank you!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The other person's profile icon quickly dimmed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though there wasn't much exchange, Johan felt that this person wasn't bad\u8212?if anything, they seemed a bit naive.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Putting away his phone, Johan heard a loud "clang, clang, clang" nearby.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tinkatink was swinging its hammer, sweating profusely in the sun.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yesterday, the rare metal he had requested from Steven had arrived. Although Tinkatink was hammering a piece of metal only about palm-sized, its weight was astonishing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to Steven, this metal was developed by Devon Corporation to mimic Aggron's armor. It had high density and was balanced in weight, hardness, and malleability.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Normally, Tinkatink could fuse any metal into its hammer in minutes, but today it had been at it all afternoon without success.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But seeing its enthusiasm, Johan decided not to intervene.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Let it keep hammering.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hopefully, it would fall asleep on the way home, giving him some peace.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The instructor's assessment brought a hint of excitement to an otherwise calm weekend.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But once the weekend was over, things seemed to return to the usual pace.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wednesday.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
