{\b
{\qc
127: The 12-Choose-3 Mode?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In an old, abandoned activity square in the town's historic district.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sitting in a row on an old iron pipe, panting, were Nidoqueen, Haunter, Vulpix, and Tinkatink\u8212?from biggest to smallest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah" (Not bad, big girl.) "Oowu" (Pretty tough.)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Chu" (Think this pipe might have any good metal if I smash it open?)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nidoqueen scratched her head and turned away with a soft huff.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Nido!" (Even if you all compliment me... I won't be happy about it!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But she couldn't hide the pleased smirk tugging at her mouth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter chuckled, producing a box from his mouth, which was full of Pok\u233?blocks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowu?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vulpix blinked, staring in disbelief.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No wonder Johan's supply kept running out! You've been hiding them, haven't you?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter passed Pok\u233?blocks around to the Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nidoqueen looked down at the Pok\u233?block, then back up at Haunter's mouth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Nido\u8230?" (Is it really okay to eat?)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~~" (Don't mind if I do.)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But as Haunter reached out to grab some, Nidoqueen reacted faster, stuffing them all into her mouth in one swift gulp.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Chu-chu."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tinkatink, cheeks full, chewed in quiet confusion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She jumped down from the pipe, gripping her hammer and starting to measure out her swing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A faint rocky glow started to wrap around her hammer as she concentrated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then she brought it crashing down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bam!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet\u8230? aside from a noticeable dent in the ground, nothing else seemed to happen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Nido, Nido."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Shaking her head, Nidoqueen stepped forward to take Tinkatink's hammer, but her expression shifted slightly as she felt its surprising weight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Impressed, she quickly handed it back, looking at Tinkatink with newfound respect.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Such a small Pok\u233?mon, but so strong\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Without making too much fuss, Nidoqueen cleared her throat and demonstrated a move.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her arm shot up, swathed in rock-type energy that coiled like a serpent around her fist before she drove it into the ground.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Crash!!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A massive stone spike erupted from the earth beneath her punch.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Johan had been there, he would have recognized the rock-type move\u8212?Stone Edge!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And he'd probably be shocked too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nidoqueen wasn't holding back at all, teaching a super high-difficulty move like Stone Edge right from the start. Could Tinkatink even learn it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And not only Tinkatink.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter and Vulpix, having finished their Pok\u233?blocks, soon had their own questions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now, Nidoqueen wasn't exactly dumb, but she wasn't the brightest, either. Just because she could learn something didn't mean she was particularly good at teaching it to others.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Scratching her head, she stood around awkwardly, clearly stumped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Nido\u8230?" (Guess it's not so easy after all\u8230?)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just then\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A Persian with a spring in its step wandered into their view, followed by a crowd of scrappy-looking stray Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's neighborhood was full of wild Pok\u233?mon like this\u8212?Vulpix had once been one of them, and her timid nature had often made her a target for bullying.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This Persian was the leader of the local strays, known for bullying weaker Pok\u233?mon and swiping food to survive.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It had come over with its gang to investigate the noise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the moment it locked eyes with the four "smiling" figures in front of it, Persian froze, struck by a bone-deep fear. A cold sweat prickled its fur as it forced an awkward grin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Meow, meow!" (S-sorry to intrude!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter and the others exchanged looks, their "smiles" widening as they waved Persian and its gang over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~ kah-kah" (No need to be scared. We're the good guys)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Night fell.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[King of the Earth]: How is Nidoqueen doing?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, feeling a bit like an empty-nester, sat alone on his new couch.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Looking over at his Pok\u233?mon playing cards on the living room floor\u8212?each one with a little slip of paper stuck to their forehead\u8212?he replied to Giovanni's message.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Grain in the Field]: She's doing well.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan couldn't help but wonder if he was a bit unnecessary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[King of the Earth]: Good to hear (Gengar breathing a sigh of relief emoji)}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The lively expression on the Gengar emoji made Johan pause.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni\u8230? did Lady Kikuko possess you?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[King of the Earth]: If you need any extra supplies, or if you're running low on anything, just let me know.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Grain in the Field]: Oh, not much. Just some extra Pok\u233?blocks, berries, Moomoo Milk, protein shakes, antidotes, potions, candy, some extra groceries...}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Giovanni took a second to process that long list.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[King of the Earth]: Did you start a war? Against the League?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Is it just me, or does Giovanni sound a little\u8230? excited?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[Grain in the Field]: Nah, we just beat up the local stray Pok\u233?mon gang, that's all.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
[King of the Earth]: Got it.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And with that, Giovanni's icon went dark.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8230? That's it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan pinched the bridge of his nose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Honestly, though, Nidoqueen was recovering faster than expected. With her face covered in sticky notes, she looked nothing like the sulking Pok\u233?mon who'd first arrived.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, Johan could sense that she hadn't fully moved on yet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A few more days of "Sweet Dream" therapy and some "motivational speeches" should be enough to help her heal.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Glancing over his detailed notes on the computer screen, Johan grinned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"With these notes, I could pass as a 'Pok\u233?mon Relationship Specialist.'"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Looks like I've found a new skill.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was late.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After guiding Nidoqueen into a peaceful sleep with a special lullaby from Vulpix, Johan finally crawled into bed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vulpix stretched luxuriously, snuggled under the blanket, and nestled herself happily around Johan's arm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tinkatink, meanwhile, stashed her hammer under the pillow and promptly started snoring, her whole body half-draped over the bed's headboard, head buried in the pillow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From time to time, her limbs would twitch, reaching out as if for an imaginary hammer, causing the pillow to slide over her nose and briefly block her breathing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter, as always, was semi-attached to the ceiling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If anyone had looked up, they might've thought Haunter was floating in a hot spring.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Haunter\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Barely awake, Johan mumbled as if talking in his sleep.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Should I get you a coffin? Can't have you sleeping on the ceiling forever\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah! \u931?(\u1076?lll)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter froze at the word "coffin," but relaxed upon hearing the rest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just as he was about to reply, he noticed Johan had already fallen asleep again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a moment of surprise, Haunter chuckled quietly and floated down to tuck Johan in, carefully moving Tinkatink's pillow to keep it from covering her nose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yawning, he stretched out comfortably.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Good night, Makka Pakka~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Sunday}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The quarterfinals for Rustboro Academy's Battle Department Instructor Tournament!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was an even bigger crowd than yesterday, judging from the number of cameras and media personnel on-site.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Banners and support signs were everywhere.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Magnemites outfitted with cameras floated above, capturing every angle of the arena.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan clutched Tinkatink tightly, wary that she might suddenly take a swing at one of the Magnemites.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They really make perfect little cameramen."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But of course, they weren't on the same level as a certain Legendary Pok\u233?mon from Johto who was in charge of cameras.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From a distance, he spotted Roxanne, Flannery, and Steven waving him over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Got any confidence, Professor?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As soon as Johan sat down, Flannery leaned in, eyes bright with excitement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The last remaining non-battle instructor in the top eight, Johan had all of them rooting for him to reach the semifinals.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And it wasn't just them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Everyone had that look of someone ready for a good show.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, the thought of a non-battle instructor making it to the top four was too fun to miss!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not really," Johan replied bluntly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The remaining battle formats included 3-on-3, 6-choose-4 doubles, 6-choose-3 singles rotation, 12-choose-3 rental rotation, and full 6-on-6.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If he drew the 6-choose-4 or the full 6-on-6, he wouldn't even bother trying. He simply didn't have enough Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
None of the other formats seemed to be in his favor, either.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before long, the teachers from the administration were out with the draw box and the box of match formats.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Martin, the head instructor, pulled out a slip of paper from the format box and smiled as he read it aloud:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The format for today is\u8212?12-Choose-3 Rental Rotation!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A buzz rippled through the crowd.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
12-choose-3 rental rotation?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If you asked which event was the hardest of all, the answer was undoubtedly 6-on-6.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But if you asked which format demanded the most from a teacher\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
's knowledge of tactics, Pok\u233?mon, moves, and abilities, it was definitely 12-choose-3 rental rotation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For any instructor in the Battle Department, it wasn't enough just to be a strong battler. Knowing your own Pok\u233?mon well was one thing, but knowing Pok\u233?mon as a whole was entirely different.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Being able to assess a student's Pok\u233?mon and utilize each one's unique strengths? That was the hallmark of a Battle Department instructor.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
You'd never see this format in a standard match.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But for Academy Instructor Evaluations, or in the Battle Frontier, it was a classic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As a wave of excitement swept through the crowd, Steven, Roxanne, and Flannery all broke into smiles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Roxanne: "This is Professor Johan's wheelhouse."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flannery: "When it comes to tactics and fundamentals, who can beat him?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven: "Professor Johan's got this in the bag."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With this format, all of them were confident in Johan's chances.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Especially Steven.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In his mind, Johan's strength wasn't so much his raw power but his tactical mastery.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Listening to their enthusiastic support, Johan rubbed his temples.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With all this confidence, I can't help but feel the pressure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
