{\b
{\qc
128: I Shall Call Him the \u8216?Master Tactician\u8217?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The faculty moved a large machine onto the battlefield. At first glance, it looked like a lottery machine, but inside were Pok\u233? Balls containing Pok\u233?mon used in the academy's training.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Each instructor would receive twelve random Pok\u233?mon. This randomness was considered the fairest method, as each Pok\u233?mon had subtle differences even if they shared the same moves and abilities.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah, ka-kah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowu, oowu~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Chu~ chu~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the stands, Haunter, Vulpix, and Tinkatink cheered for Johan, each waving a little pom-pom. They were a bit disappointed they couldn't join the battle, but if Johan won this round and made it to the semifinals, he'd earn the top-four prize\u8212?a rare Evolution Stone!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And if he made it to the semifinals, there would be no more rental matches, meaning they'd be up for battle again soon enough. Just the thought got them excited.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Out on the field, Johan received a tray with twelve Pok\u233? Balls and a sheet listing each Pok\u233?mon's name, ability, and moves. He was given ten minutes to review and select items for them, up to a maximum of six.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But as Johan read through the list of twelve Pok\u233?mon he'd received, he felt a headache coming on.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Raticate, Arbok, Feraligatr, Beautifly, Drifloon, Frosmoth\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
One Pok\u233?mon, however, did catch his eye.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dolliv!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A Grass/Normal Pok\u233?mon from Paldea, Dolliv was gentle-natured and excelled in special attack and special defense.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His ten minutes went by quickly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's opponent was Carl, the senior instructor for the second-year Battle Department Class 3. He was renowned for his impressive skills and experience.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The battlefield's main screen displayed both instructors' portraits along with three Pok\u233? Balls representing each chosen Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the referee's signal, the two stepped onto the field.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carl, tall and slender with glasses, wore a confident smile that seemed to say he was very sure of his choice of Pok\u233?mon and strategy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But out loud, he said, "Professor Johan, please go easy on me."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing Carl's smug attempt at humility, Johan thought of a perfect word to describe his opponent's attitude:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pretentious."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's reputation was established, especially for his tactical prowess. But Carl saw him as someone with a "hobby" challenging his own profession.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan might have tactical skill, but the 12-choose-3 rental mode required exceptional expertise. And Carl had gotten quite lucky, drawing Pok\u233?mon that played well to his strengths.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Carl's "humble" appeal met with Johan's smile, Johan simply replied, "Alright."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hm?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carl was taken aback and narrowed his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the referee announced the start, both trainers threw their Pok\u233? Balls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Go, Rapidash!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Go, Dolliv!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Both Pok\u233?mon appeared on the field at the same time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Grass against Fire? Johan might be in for a rough start."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Where did Dolliv even come from?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Carl is a specialist in Fire and Flying types, so this is a great start for him."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Luck is part of skill, after all."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Watching the two Pok\u233?mon appear, the spectators began discussing the match. For this high-stakes top-eight battle, professional commentators had also been provided.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dolliv is a Pok\u233?mon from the distant Paldea region! It seems Johan is well-versed in Pok\u233?mon even from far-off regions. Unfortunately, he's right up against Carl's specialty."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Some of you might not realize just how big an advantage Rapidash has here, so let me break it down\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rapidash was fast and had high attack power, while Dolliv specialized in special attack and defense but was extremely slow\u8212?not to mention the type disadvantage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After hearing the analysis, the crowd collectively sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was no way Johan could win this round.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rapidash, Flare Blitz!" Carl said confidently, sweeping his hand forward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In an instant, Rapidash's body was completely engulfed in flames, and it charged at Dolliv like a blazing comet. With Dolliv's low speed, there was no chance of dodging.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Johan's command surprised everyone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dolliv, use Leech Seed beneath you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dolliv dropped a few tiny seeds at its feet, but before it could do anything else, Rapidash crashed into it with full force.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Boom!!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dolliv was sent flying.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The referee raised his flag.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dolliv is unable to battle! It was taken down in one hit, as Carl's Rapidash was holding a Charcoal item!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
[Charcoal: Increases the power of Fire-type moves by 20%.]\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The crowd erupted in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A one-hit knockout right at the start?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan was done for.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or was he?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While being knocked back, Dolliv had shaken loose several seeds, which quickly sprouted and spread across the field.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dolliv's ability is Seed Sower, so the field has become Grassy Terrain!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And because Rapidash used Flare Blitz, it took recoil damage from the collision\u8230? wait! Dolliv was holding a Rocky Helmet, so the damage to Rapidash is even worse!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the field, Rapidash neighed in pain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
[Rocky Helmet: Inflicts damage on attackers who use contact moves.]\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wow, holding Rocky Helmet? Only Johan could think of something so devious!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Does that mean Johan planned to sacrifice Dolliv from the start?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And don't forget, Rapidash is entangled in Leech Seed too."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Keen-eyed viewers noticed that while Rapidash had defeated Dolliv, it had taken substantial recoil damage from Flare Blitz, the Rocky Helmet, and the Leech Seed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And now the field was Grassy Terrain, enhancing Grass-type moves and restoring a little HP each turn.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So\u8230? will Johan's next Pok\u233?mon be another Grass type?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Grass types still get roasted by Rapidash."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Recalling Dolliv, Johan smiled down at its Pok\u233? Ball and said, "You did great. Leave the rest to the others."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He threw out his next Pok\u233? Ball, surprising everyone again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Drifloon, the Ghost/Flying-type balloon Pok\u233?mon!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wow, Johan has some bad luck. None of his Pok\u233?mon seem to form any kind of strong lineup."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So what's the Grassy Terrain for? Passive healing?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Most of the crowd knew Drifloon was a high-HP but defensively weak Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In other words, a "punching bag."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Drifloon immediately revealed the purpose of Grassy Terrain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A small seed dropped from Drifloon's body\u8212?a Grassy Seed!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
[Grassy Seed: Boosts defense when Grassy Terrain is active.]\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But\u8230? is that it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Drifloon's ability is Unburden, so after using its item, its speed has doubled!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This answer from the commentators somewhat satisfied the crowd.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carl frowned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Rapidash used Flare Blitz again, it would knock itself out. But Drifloon's Unburden had made it faster than Rapidash, so it could easily dodge now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rapidash, Flame Charge!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rapidash's fiery hooves flared up as it sprinted around the field.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Johan was unfazed. "Drifloon, Minimize."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drifloon's size shrank significantly, increasing its evasiveness. Rapidash's Flame Charge sailed past without hitting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, Rapidash's speed increased.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Drifloon, Minimize again."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rapidash, another Flame Charge!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rapidash circled the field as Drifloon continued to shrink, its evasiveness growing each time. Rapidash's second Flame Charge also missed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This back-and-forth continued until finally, Rapidash connected.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet Johan only gave one command.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Minimize again."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the third use, Drifloon was now only the size of a fist.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A Minimize strategy?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Doesn't that fail if it gets hit by something like Body Slam?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"True, but Rapidash doesn't seem to know that move."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Rapidash sustaining itself on Grassy Terrain's healing, Carl changed tactics.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rapidash, Flamethrower! Cover the area!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While Rapidash had high attack, most Fire Pok\u233?mon could use both attack and special moves. Its Flamethrower covered half the field, blanketing Drifloon in flames.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet Johan's instructions took a new turn.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Drifloon, Calm Mind."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
[Calm Mind: Raises a Pok\u233?mon's Special Attack and Special Defense.]\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Calm Mind enhancing its defenses and Grassy Terrain's healing, Drifloon seemed unscathed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thanks to Leech Seed, recoil from Rapidash's moves, and Grassy Terrain's passive healing, Drifloon soon maxed out its Calm Mind stacks without losing much HP.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Eventually, Rapidash fainted from Leech Seed damage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carl's second Pok\u233?mon was Typhlosion!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While Typhlosion knew moves like Body Slam and Smokescreen, Drifloon's Calm Mind, Substitute, and speed advantage rendered them ineffective.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even when Typhlosion's Body Slam connected, Drifloon's durability and Grassy Terrain meant it survived without much trouble.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Once Drifloon maxed out its stats, Johan's strategy reached its true potential.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Drifloon, Baton Pass!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The crowd gasped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I thought he was going for a Minimize strategy, but it's a Baton Pass strategy!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A fully maxed Special Attack and Special Defense? Even if he Baton Passed to a [Little Growlithe], it'd still have ridiculous Special Attack!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Frosmoth? But it's four times weak to Fire!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Indeed, the recipient of the boosted stats was Frosmoth, an Ice/Bug type!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
as a result of Baton Pass, this Frosmoth now had full Special Attack and Special Defense!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
More importantly\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Frosmoth, use Light Screen!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh no!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The students need to know that Johan's Frosmoth has Ice Scales!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
[Ice Scales: Halves damage from special moves.]\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now fully boosted with maxed Special Defense, Ice Scales halving Special Attack damage, and Light Screen halving it again, Typhlosion's Fire-type moves were effectively nullified!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Even with Typhlosion's type advantage, it's like scratching an itch!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Finally, someone in the crowd realized Frosmoth's 125 Special Attack stat, enhanced by six Calm Mind boosts, translated to a 400% increase in power!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Now it's a sweep! Even if Carl had twelve Pok\u233?mon, they'd all be defeated at this point!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was the allure of the Baton Pass strategy: once the Baton Pass succeeded, the rest was smooth sailing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Frosmoth's item? Leftovers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its survivability was maxed out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Desperately, Carl tried his third Pok\u233?mon, Torkoal, with Clear Smog to remove Frosmoth's boosts. Yet the slow Torkoal was easily outspeeded, and even Clear Smog couldn't keep up with Frosmoth's Substitute.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the end, Johan won the battle with an overwhelmingly "tactical" victory!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And the entire match had been recorded and livestreamed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
----------\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
