{\qc
129: Only the Victorious Are Entitled to Define \u8216?Justice\u8217?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You ghosts, your tactics are always so dirty!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You hit me, but you can't actually hurt me\u8212?nah nah nah~~. Hey everyone, am I doing a good impression?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"My 40-foot broadsword almost couldn't stay put."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Um... I'm a student from the Orange/Grape Academy in Paldea, and this tactic... I think I can use it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"To the person above, I suggest you act like a decent human!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I propose we get Professor Johan to teach at our Orange/Grape Academy! @Clavell_Principal."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Johan belongs to Hoenn!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since this was just a routine instructor assessment for the academy's top-eight round, the livestream was only popular within Hoenn.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, as the battle progressed, interest skyrocketed\u8212?especially when the "Baton Pass" tactic took center stage. The hype grew exponentially, and many people had to watch the replay to see the full extent of the strategy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When they finished watching, they couldn't help but head to the bathroom to wash their faces and rinse their eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, dirt should be washed away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But there was one consensus across the internet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although there were previously videos of Johan's tactical gameplay, like his "Substitute and Toxic" Skarmory strategy or Lapras's "Perish Song" strategy, those battles weren't enough to earn him the title of "Tactical Master"\u8212?not even close.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This battle, however, left everyone completely convinced of Johan's strategic brilliance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In a random 12-to-3 Pok\u233?mon selection, with bad luck, his opponent had drawn a hand with type advantage, while Johan's choices were nearly all disadvantaged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Olive-doll Dolliv was doubly weak to Fire, and Frosmoth was four times weak to Fire.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet, despite such a massive disadvantage, he achieved a four-fold type resistance reversal with perfect strategy and insight!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was not the type of battle tactics that the average trainer possessed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
