Its usual insatiable appetite had noticeably changed. After consuming a portion of Koga's Weezing and a fragment of {\i
Black Sludge}, Haunter had grown significantly larger.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The materials, rich in toxicity, seemed to be taking longer to digest, marking Haunter's progress toward an evolutionary threshold.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Holding Haunter back from evolving wasn't ideal\u8212?it could hinder its growth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No matter how tight Johan's finances got, his Pok\u233?mon's well-being came first.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll go," Johan finally agreed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance nodded gratefully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thanks. You've already done so much for me."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance lay back on the grass, gazing at the endless blue sky.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan, do you think there'll ever be a time when humans and Pok\u233?mon live together as freely as the clouds?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan lay back as well, letting the tranquility of the moment wash over him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"There will be," he said softly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance's question reminded him of someone he hadn't seen in a long time\u8212?a certain {\i
Mathematical Magician.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
People like Lance, the magician, Cynthia, Red, and Ash made it seem less like a dream and more like an eventuality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I've submitted a request to take on a covert mission once Gyarados recovers."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's heart sank.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Covert mission?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Was Lance planning to infiltrate Team Rocket?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two days later, the Red Gyarados's condition had stabilized.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though still irritable, it had acknowledged Lance as its trainer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From here on, recovery would involve a regimen of soothing audio and gradual psychological rehabilitation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Gyarados in good hands, Johan boarded a plane from Blackthorn City to Saffron City, en route to Elm's lab at {\i
Bill's Lighthouse.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The location of Bill's research was notoriously ambiguous:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the anime, he resided at Bill's Lighthouse.In the games, he worked out of Sea Cottage in northeast Kanto.At times, he was based in Johto's Goldenrod City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Luckily, after some inquiries, Johan confirmed Bill was currently at the lighthouse.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Elsewhere in Saffron City...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A burst of flames illuminated a cozy apartment as a plume of fragrant smoke filled the air.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alakazam!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The mustachioed Psychic Pok\u233?mon used its powers to gather the smoke and waft it out an open window.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well done, Alakazam!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wearing an apron, a tall, sharp-eyed girl flipped food in a frying pan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She glanced at Alakazam, who scratched the back of its head bashfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not long ago, this girl had been a cold, aloof psychic prodigy, wielding her powers with terrifying recklessness.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But now, she seemed... almost human.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was Sabrina, Gym Leader of Saffron City and one of Team Rocket's top operatives.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alakazam, grab me a soda. Also, the movie's over\u8212?put on another."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Despite her newfound warmth, some of her arrogance lingered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, Alakazam couldn't complain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Compared to the tyrant she used to be, Sabrina now resembled an angel.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thanks!" Sabrina popped the soda open, downing it in one go.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her latest obsession was cooking\u8212?and making others eat her creations.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her father had recently taken to leaving the house early and coming home late to avoid her "experiments."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Alakazam had no such luck.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's tamarind and persim berry chicken wings! Try it!" Sabrina beamed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The dish looked... unrecognizable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alakazam felt its knees tremble.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before it could take a bite, both Sabrina and Alakazam froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Their psychic senses flared as they detected a presence approaching the city.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina's eyes narrowed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's go."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alakazam sighed in relief, grateful for the sudden distraction.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Saved... for now.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
