{\qc
156: Little Sabrina, Totally Handled!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Kanto Region, Saffron City}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Saffron City was the largest and most developed city in all of Kanto, and this was Johan's first visit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The moment he stepped out of the airport, he could feel the stark contrast between Saffron and Blackthorn City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't that Blackthorn was underdeveloped\u8212?it was just that, compared to Saffron, it felt like moving from a small town to a bustling metropolis.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Towering skyscrapers lined the skyline, and the streets were alive with cars, people, and Pok\u233?mon of all kinds.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233?mon were incredibly diverse\u8212?some native to Kanto, others from Johto, and even some from far-off regions like Hoenn, Sinnoh, Unova, and Kalos.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Carrying Vulpix in his arms and flanked by Haunter, Johan made his way toward {\i
White Cove}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Known as a romantic spot for couples, the cove was also a popular tourist destination.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowu~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Vulpix in Johan's arms stirred, rubbing its eyes and yawning softly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Awake now?" Johan teased, ruffling its fur affectionately.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowu! (#\u65344?\u30399?)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Annoyed at its now-messy fur, Vulpix growled, baring its little fangs.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which only prompted Johan to double down on ruffling its fur.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vulpix's soft, silky coat was becoming more and more addictive to touch, Johan mused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oddly enough, while he could sense Haunter reaching a point where evolution might soon happen, Vulpix seemed to be making no such progress.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Perhaps it was because Vulpix required a {\i
Fire Stone} to evolve. Or maybe it was because Haunter had been dormant for a millennium, accumulating much more energy than Vulpix.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As Johan pondered these things, absentmindedly petting Vulpix, a sharp, cold presence brushed against his senses.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Both Haunter and Vulpix reacted before Johan, turning their gazes toward a young woman standing not far away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She had long black hair, a form-fitting red outfit, and glossy black tights. A {\i
Kadabra} floated by her side, its spoon gleaming faintly with psychic energy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her confident smirk gave her identity away immediately:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Sabrina.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Saffron City's Gym Leader.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
One of Team Rocket's three executive officers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed inwardly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
First Koga. Then the Rocket trio. Then Matori.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Now Sabrina?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan couldn't help but wonder, {\i
What's Giovanni trying to pull here?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before Johan could say a word, Sabrina spoke.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Grain... in the Field?" she asked, her tone equal parts amused and curious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan blinked, startled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina seemed to take his silence as confirmation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I thought I recognized the signature of my {\i
Calm Mind} techniques lingering around Saffron. Turns out it's you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's mind clicked into place.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She wasn't here under Giovanni's orders\u8212?she knew him from {\i
somewhere else.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Testing his theory, Johan ventured cautiously: "Supernatural Girl?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the nickname, Sabrina's elegant expression cracked slightly, and her pale cheeks turned a soft pink.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The embarrassment in her eyes confirmed Johan's suspicion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Oh no.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni. Matori. Sabrina.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unknowingly, Johan had ended up connected with so many Rocket executives through his online consultations for Pok\u233?mon with psychological issues.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If he added Mewtwo to that mix...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
If Officer Jenny came knocking, I'd never explain my way out of this.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan resolved to meticulously audit his online friends' list when he got home. Surely it couldn't have {\i
more} Rocket members, right?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina's gaze flicked to the Pok\u233?mon at Johan's side\u8212?Haunter and Vulpix.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her eyebrows arched in faint surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These two weren't Psychic-types, but they had latent potential in psychic energy that outshone most true Psychic Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As an expert in the field, Sabrina's keen eyes quickly picked up on their hidden talents.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then she turned back to Johan, tilting her head slightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Here to challenge my gym?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan froze, unsure how to respond.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before he could open his mouth, Haunter stepped in, donning a pair of sunglasses and waving dismissively.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
No time today.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina narrowed her eyes, her psychic aura flaring faintly as her long hair began to float.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vulpix tensed, jumping onto Johan's head, its six tails fanning out as it prepared to counter the energy with its own latent psychic resonance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Beside Sabrina, Kadabra gripped its spoon tightly, a nervous glint in its eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kadabra muttered to itself, {\i
If this escalates, there's no way I'm walking away unscathed.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kadabra had a vested interest in keeping things civil. At home, Sabrina's cooking experiments were enough to terrify it. The last thing it wanted was more trouble.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan quickly stepped in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What are you all doing? Looking for a fight?" he barked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vulpix wilted under his scolding, its tails drooping as it licked his cheek apologetically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina blinked, startled by his sudden assertiveness, and let her psychic aura dissipate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kadabra froze, nearly dropping its spoon in shock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Uh-oh.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter snickered, seemingly amused by the tension.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed and waved a hand dismissively.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sorry, we're busy today. Maybe tomorrow or the day after, I'll swing by your gym."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina raised an eyebrow, about to retort.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll even teach you a recipe," Johan added casually.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kadabra, Haunter, and Vulpix all froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Recipe?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To their astonishment, Sabrina's frosty demeanor thawed almost instantly. Her nose wrinkled slightly, and she folded her arms.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"W-who needs your recipes? I'm already a great cook, okay?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though her words protested, the spark of interest in her eyes was unmistakable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?" Haunter scratched its head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What just happened?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kadabra, however, felt its heart sink.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Great. I guess we're eating another 'culinary masterpiece' soon.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a moment of sulking, Sabrina muttered, "Fine. Teach me the hardest one you know."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Deal," Johan said with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her mood brightened considerably.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sabrina hesitated, then added, "I don't want to owe you, so... how about I teach your Haunter how to use psychic energy in return?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Both Johan and Haunter blinked in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Psychic energy?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Satisfied with herself, Sabrina turned to Kadabra.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kadabra groaned inwardly, but with a resigned sigh, activated {\i
Teleport}, whisking Sabrina away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before disappearing, Kadabra shot Johan a look that he didn't quite understand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
You're our only hope.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the pair vanished, Johan let out a breath he hadn't realized he was holding.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Turning to his Pok\u233?mon, he said sternly:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The next time this happens, keep calm. No rushing into fights. Be like me\u8212?stay composed and prioritize peace."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter blinked, then floated over and poked Johan's back.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
You're drenched in sweat!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oowu!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vulpix burst out laughing, its tails wagging with delight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter joined in, cackling uncontrollably.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a moment, Vulpix spoke softly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowu..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
I don't think she really wanted to fight. I didn't feel any malice from her or Kadabra.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Haunter nodded in agreement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
True. It did seem that way.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Really?" Johan asked, skeptical.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a brief pause, Haunter voiced another question.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
But how did you know one dish would win her over?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan chuckled knowingly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Every time I post a picture of my cooking, the same few people always give it the most likes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He ticked off names on his fingers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Cynthia, Matori, Sabrina, Diantha, Lorelei, Steven...}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia and Diantha were foodies, but Matori and Sabrina? They just wanted to learn.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, Johan had once taught Sabrina to use cooking as a way to bond with Kadabra.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Little Sabrina... totally handled.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then again... now that Johan thought about it, hadn't nearly every Rocket member\u8212?Giovanni included\u8212?attempted cooking under his advice at some point?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The warm sun, salty breeze, and rhythmic crash of waves made {\i
White Cove} a scenic paradise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Named for its pristine, white sand, the cove was a haven for both humans and Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan kicked off his shoes, enjoying the soft sand beneath his feet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dratini would probably love this," he mused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He released Dratini and Tinkatuff from their Pok\u233?balls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As soon as it emerged, Dratini happily rolled around in the sand, eyes closed in bliss.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Tink!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tinkatuff, meanwhile, hefted its hammer and set off on an enthusiastic treasure hunt.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not far off, Haunter spotted a wild Krabby and floated over mischievously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Wanna play rock-paper-scissors? If I lose, I'll give you a berry. If you lose, I get a claw.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Krab? Krab krab?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Krabby tilted its head, utterly baffled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smacked his forehead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You do realize Krabby can only throw scissors, right?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
