For now, it was enough that there was no Pryce-like figure here.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Masked Man's power was absurd, his Pok\u233?mon lineup terrifying\u8212?be it the Delibird, a Swinub that refused to evolve, or the legendary Ho-Oh he had captured.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Shrugging off these thoughts, Johan turned his attention to the small metallic case in his hand\u8212?a gift Giovanni had handed him before he left.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was what Giovanni had promised when Gengar jokingly asked about "rewards" before the battle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A piece of {\b
Metal Coat}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Useful for evolving Onix into Steelix or Scyther into Scizor.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While the {\b
Earthquake} TM was a great prize, this Metal Coat was of greater immediate value to Johan. He could already imagine Tinkatuff's excitement upon seeing it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This particular Metal Coat wasn't naturally occurring but artificially compressed, rich in high-grade steel-type minerals. It was rare and highly valuable, likely worth upwards of five million Pok\u233?dollars.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is the kind of benefit Team Rocket offers\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No wonder so many people were devoted to them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The car traveled steadily through Viridian Forest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Matori had offered to arrange a helicopter, but Johan thought it too ostentatious and opted for a car ride instead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Finally, they arrived at {\b
Pallet Town}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The small, peaceful village brimmed with Blueery, quiet roads, and sparkling rivers where Magikarp and Poliwag frolicked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Stepping out of the car, Johan breathed in the fresh air, feeling a surge of energy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
By the roadside, a few children were having what could generously be called a Pok\u233?mon battle. Their high-pitched voices might have left one questioning how their Pok\u233?mon even understood them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Johan didn't underestimate them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was {\b
Pallet Town}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Who knew which of these kids might grow into a legendary "Super Pallet Trainer," a League Champion, or even the famed "Five-Minute Champion"?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What if he bumped into young Red? Should he teach him or prank him?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And if it were young Ash\u8230? Perhaps he'd prepare him for the harsh realities of the world before his inevitable misadventures.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Letting his Pok\u233?mon out of their balls\u8212?Gengar, Vulpix, Tinkatuff, and Dratini\u8212?Johan watched as, apart from Gengar, the others fit seamlessly into the playful atmosphere with the children's Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Could it be\u8230? I have potential to be a Pallet Town local too?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a chuckle, he turned his sights to Professor Oak's Laboratory, a prominent building with a windmill atop a hill.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As he climbed the path to the lab, Gengar's antics began as expected.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!" it shouted, startling a flock of Pidgey into flight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
