Blue led Johan past bustling researchers in the chaotic lab, through a side door, and into\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's jaw dropped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A vast expanse of plains, rolling hills, and shimmering lakes stretched out before him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "???"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was the "backyard"?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blue scratched his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"There's no helping it. This place houses over three thousand Pok\u233?mon, not counting the wild ones or the ones my grandfather raises himself."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Three thousand?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan nodded mechanically. No wonder Blue was later dubbed the "Breeder," with unparalleled expertise in raising Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Raising the Pok\u233?mon in this "backyard" alone was an impossible task for most.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Grandfather is probably near the Kangaskhan. It's not far, so no need for the jeep."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan glanced at the row of jeeps parked nearby, his eye twitching.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A backyard that required jeeps. Wonderful.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Following Blue on foot, Johan soon saw a white-coated elderly man crouched on the ground, magnifying glass in hand, observing a feeding Kangaskhan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Looks like the little one's teething\u8230? No wonder it's weaning," Professor Oak muttered as he lifted the baby Kangaskhan from its mother's pouch.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But before he could examine further\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gaaaaroo!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Kangaskhan roared, snatched her baby back, and swatted Oak aside with her tail.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak soared through the air in a graceful arc before crashing into the grass.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "\u8230?."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blue, unfazed, continued forward. Clearly, he'd seen this routine far too many times.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Grandpa!" Blue called out. "Johan is here!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak looked up, spotting Johan, and his eyes lit up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah, Johan! Birch mentioned you were coming. Thanks for going out of your way."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The two had met during the Mt. Coronet Pok\u233?mon Researcher Summit, so they weren't strangers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's no trouble," Johan replied with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He turned to his shadow and called, "Gengar."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The shadow remained still.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Overhead, a few Murkrow cawed ominously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Kaaw\u8212?Kaaw\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak and Blue: "?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sweat formed on Johan's brow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Where had Gengar gone?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This backyard housed over three thousand Pok\u233?mon\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, Gengar emerged from Oak's shadow, pulling a spooky face at the professor.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan exhaled in relief.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thankfully\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Oak's expression turned complicated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In Gengar's confused gaze, the professor gently patted its head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thank you, Gengar," Oak said softly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar tilted its head, utterly baffled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thank me? For what?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And why didn't my scare work?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Blue seemed puzzled by Oak's reaction.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Johan had a faint understanding.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak's words weren't meant for Gengar\u8230? but for someone it reminded him of.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar sidled up to Johan, pointing at its head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Is this old guy okay in the head?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
