He'd write scripts and collect royalties\u8212?Matori could handle the rest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Matori launched into an update, detailing production plans and schedules.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her professionalism was evident.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
No wonder she's Giovanni's secretary.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If anyone could rival her, it might be Macro Cosmos's secretary, Oleana.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though Matori lacked Oleana's imposing presence and refined wardrobe...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Well, close enough.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Matori's thoroughness reassured Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
With someone like her in charge, I can relax.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His original goal had been to delegate everything beyond scriptwriting, and that plan remained unchanged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan, there's just one last thing," Matori said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's that?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Casting."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Casting?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The success of {\i
The Adventures of Meowth and Pichu} hinged entirely on its two leads.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If it were to surpass {\i
Bubble Cyndaquil's Adventures}, the casting had to be perfect.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"For Meowth, we're scouting in Galar. But we already have a candidate for Pichu. Would you like to see it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan raised an eyebrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You've been busy."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's Rocket efficiency," Matori replied, beaming through the phone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll arrange a flight for you to meet the candidate!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait\u8212?where am I flying to?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Vermilion City. We've... cultivated some connections there."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Lt. Surge's Electric Army, no doubt.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A sense of foreboding crept over Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At home, Johan gathered his Pok\u233?mon and the Rocket trio.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He announced his upcoming trip to Kanto, where he'd be gone for a few days.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His Pok\u233?mon were thrilled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Another adventure!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe they'd even challenge some gyms for fun.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Rocket trio, on the other hand, looked anxious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The question on their minds:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Who would be the next "Acting Manager"?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's answer dashed their hopes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wobbuffet, the caf\u233? is safest in your hands."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wobbaaa~~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tears streamed down Wobbuffet's face. He saluted solemnly, vowing to defend the caf\u233? with his life.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The trio slumped in defeat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is so unfair!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He couldn't trust any of them to lead without bickering. Wobbuffet's neutrality avoided unnecessary conflict.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, watching them sulk, a new idea struck him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Maybe they should join the production team.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
James's meticulousness would suit managing cast and crew.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meowth could choreograph actions, even take Meowth's role if needed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for Jessie?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She'd always dreamed of stardom. The role of "Mrs. Two-Shoes" was practically made for her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Come to think of it, didn't they produce a film in the anime?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The only remaining problem:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What about the caf\u233??}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
