{\qc
201: Vermilion Gym, Lt. Surge!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Kanto, Vermilion City.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The whistle of a departing ship echoed as a massive cruise liner slowly left the bustling harbor.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vermilion, the largest port city in Kanto, thrived on international connections. People from all over the world arrived and departed on cruise ships, bringing with them diversity and vitality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A burly man leaned casually against a railing near the port. Dressed in green camouflage, his short blond hair gleamed in the sunlight. His powerful physique gave off an imposing aura.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Tssssk.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He cracked open a beer can and took a long sip.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, from the shadows, something shot toward him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge's expression shifted. His reflexes were lightning-quick\u8212?his large hand darted out and caught the object midair.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When he opened his palm, he found a badge\u8212?{\b
Fuchsia Gym's Pink Badge!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge smirked, balancing the badge on his fingertips.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Ding!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He flicked it, sending it spinning into the air before catching it deftly again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, well," he muttered, glancing toward the shadows.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There, a man in ninja attire emerged from the darkness\u8212?a middle-aged figure with an aura as sharp as a blade.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're awfully free these days, Koga," Surge said, taking another swig of his beer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The figure, Fuchsia Gym Leader {\b
Koga}, replied in his deep, muffled voice:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I have a mission in Johto. I need you to handle something for me."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And here I thought you were always busy."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Koga's gaze narrowed beneath his mask.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You seem quite relaxed yourself."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge grinned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"When the boss halts all activities, things get pretty dull. I'm even stuck helping someone pick Pok\u233?mon for a TV show. Doesn't get much more boring than that."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You doubt the boss's orders?" Koga asked coolly, his piercing eyes focused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge's expression turned serious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course not."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He caught the Pink Badge again and examined it idly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But I am curious... What kind of person could make {\i
you} go out of your way?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Koga's voice lowered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"{\b
Johan.}"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge frowned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan again? What's his deal?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You don't know Johan?" Koga seemed surprised.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Should I?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge wasn't one to spend time online or keep up with buzz about individuals outside his military or Rocket circles. To him, Johan was just a name\u8212?one that seemed to be popping up more often lately.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Koga explained briefly, summarizing the key points he'd heard about Johan from his daughter Janine and online chatter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Surge merely scoffed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Being good at tactics doesn't make him good at actual combat."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For a man like Surge, once a soldier, combat meant survival in life-and-death situations. Pok\u233?mon battles governed by League rules? Child's play.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even as Vermilion Gym Leader, he found it dull. That's why he was infamous for being a tough and ruthless opponent. Trainers who challenged him often found themselves limping to the Pok\u233?mon Center.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Just deliver the badge," Koga instructed curtly, disappearing back into the shadows.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge sighed, crushing the empty beer can in one hand before tossing it aside.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His eyes glinted dangerously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'd like to see what this Johan guy is really made of."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
At the Vermilion coast.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Waves glittered under the sunlight as they lapped against the shore.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah\u8212?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar cupped his hands around his mouth and shouted at the sea, his voice brimming with excitement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Today, I'm eating ten bowls!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed, feeling his wallet cringe.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Woo~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vulpix, perched on Johan's shoulder, pointed toward a departing ship.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What a big boat!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's the S.S. Aqua, a luxury cruise ship."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, Tinkatuff had its sights set on something grander\u8212?the enormous and opulent {\b
S.S. Anne}, docked at the port.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Chu!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
That one's even bigger!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan rolled his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Yeah, sure. Let's see you try hammering that into your club.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's the S.S. Anne," he explained. "It's a super-luxury liner that can carry thousands of passengers at once. They even hold major competitions onboard during each voyage. But tickets..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He trailed off, recalling a detail from the Pok\u233?mon Adventures manga.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If memory served, Lt. Surge wasn't just Vermilion's Gym Leader and a Rocket Executive\u8212?he was also the {\b
captain} of the S.S. Anne.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Honestly, these League-appointed roles are tough.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Gym Leaders had it rough, juggling their duties with various side gigs. Surge had to manage his gym, command an electric Pok\u233?mon army, and captain a cruise liner.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even the Cerulean Gym Sisters turned their facility into a water performance stage just to make ends meet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Driii..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dratini gazed at the open sea, a longing stirring deep within her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Should we go sailing?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Next time," Johan promised.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, a rugged off-road vehicle pulled up beside them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A young woman with short white hair, tanned skin, and a pink headband stood atop the vehicle. Her muscular frame exuded strength and confidence.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her boisterous voice startled everyone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm Visquez, Lt. Surge's deputy!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan remembered hearing of her\u8212?a former soldier and vice-captain of Surge's squad.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Surge was busy captaining the S.S. Anne or handling Rocket affairs, Visquez took over as Gym Leader.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He also recalled a fun fact: she ranked {\b
2109th} in the World Coronation Series.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Respectable, but not exactly top-tier.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Nice to meet you," Johan greeted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lt. Surge sent me to pick you up," she said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thanks."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan climbed into the vehicle, knowing he'd soon meet the infamous Electric Army and pick out a Pichu for the show.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Visquez stomped the gas pedal, sending the jeep roaring forward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As she drove, she sized Johan up through the rearview mirror.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
He's handsome, I'll give him that,} she thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
But a guy who hugs a cute Vulpix?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She wrinkled her nose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What a pretty boy.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her judgment was cut short when a shadow appeared in the passenger seat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Gengar, grinning menacingly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Did you just call my trainer a pretty boy?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Visquez nearly swerved in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Where did you\u8212??!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar pointed to the steering wheel.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Can I drive?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moments later, Johan noticed something amiss.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gengar! What are you\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Too late.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Visquez had fainted, slumped over the wheel, while the jeep's horn blared obnoxiously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan groaned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're the vice-captain of a military squad, and you faint from a ghost prank?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar cackled, donning sunglasses and gripping the wheel.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Time for Gengar's road trip!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gengar," Johan muttered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Do you even know where Vermilion Gym is?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Good point.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
At Vermilion Gym.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge led his trainees and staff on a morning jog around the facility\u8212?a daily ritual that reflected his military roots.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sir!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
One of his subordinates, Tony, pointed toward the road.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Deputy Visquez's jeep!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge frowned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
She's late. Two hours late.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The delay had already made him extend the jog unnecessarily.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The jeep finally appeared\u8212?but instead of stopping, it sped past the gym.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge's scowl deepened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It reversed moments later.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When the door opened, Johan stepped out, visibly awkward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Uh... Sorry. She's just... sleeping."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lt. Surge cracked his knuckles, his lips curling into a menacing grin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Looks like we're gonna have to settle this..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
