{\qc
202: Johan's First Unrestricted Battle!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
As expected.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan revealed an expression that seemed to say, {\i
"Of course this was going to happen."}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The moment he set out for Vermilion City to meet Lt. Surge, he'd figured this would be unavoidable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, with three Gym Badges already in hand, he had accepted the situation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some things just can't be dodged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
If it's a battle he wants, it's a battle he'll get.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Whether he could earn a badge or how many badges he could collect\u8212?he would leave it all to fate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If he did manage to gather all eight badges, entering the League Conference wouldn't be so bad. After all, Gengar and the others had yet to experience a Pok\u233?mon League tournament.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had read about Lt. Surge's reputation before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alongside {\b
Koga} and {\b
Sabrina}, Surge was one of Team Rocket's three main Executives.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unlike the others, Surge had quickly turned a new leaf after Team Rocket disbanded, even aiding Red and others in major incidents.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge's outward appearance\u8212?a brawny, rough, temperamental man\u8212?often gave the impression of a simple-minded brute.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But how many people achieve the rank of {\b
Major} in the military without some measure of intellect?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His "on-paper" strength might have been the weakest among the Rocket Executives.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But that only made it more apparent that his position wasn't solely based on raw power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Lt. Surge specialized in no-holds-barred combat\u8212?the kind of fight where lives were on the line.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the Pok\u233?mon Special manga, he had once forced Red into a desperate situation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That infamous "insulated gloves trick" Red used during his final battle with Giovanni? The gloves were stolen from Lt. Surge during their showdown.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge was also known for making {\b
Raikou}, one of the three Legendary Beasts, {\b
charge a maglev train}\u8212?effectively using it as a battery.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was likely the first and only person to ever think of something so audacious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In addition to Raikou, Surge had also commanded Zapdos, one of the Legendary Birds.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A man who had wielded both a Legendary Bird and a Legendary Beast was not to be taken lightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now, standing face-to-face with such a figure, Johan was ready.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If this battle was unavoidable, why hesitate?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'd be honored, Lt. Surge."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge was slightly taken aback.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He glanced at Johan, who appeared calm and composed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His earlier opinion of Johan\u8212?a delicate-looking man with a cute Vulpix\u8212?began to shift.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge smirked, crossing his arms.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"In that case, let's make it an {\b
unrestricted battle}."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan froze for a moment before quickly understanding.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was very much in line with Surge's personality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar tilted his head, looking confused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What's an unrestricted battle? Never heard of it.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A man with a sausage-shaped nose\u8212?Tony\u8212?stepped forward to explain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Unrestricted battles are like regulated street fights. They were popular in earlier Gym matches and tournaments, though they're less common nowadays."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He continued,\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The rules are simple: both Trainers and their Pok\u233?mon fight on the field together. Pok\u233?mon can be swapped in and out anytime. The first to incapacitate an opponent's Pok\u233?mon wins."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I understand. The Pok\u233?mon can't attack Trainers directly, but anything else on the battlefield\u8212?be it environmental hazards or collateral damage\u8212?is fair game."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tony seemed surprised but impressed by Johan's knowledge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unrestricted battles were indeed rare now, but they weren't unheard of.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233?mon League tournaments depicted in the {\i
Pok\u233?mon Special} manga? Those were unrestricted battles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Red's showdown with Giovanni? Same rules.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These battles favored "wandering Trainers" over "academic Trainers" because they required practical experience.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The rules had faded into obscurity partly due to escalating tensions between these two groups.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some veterans even believed the League's declining influence was tied to the disappearance of unrestricted battles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar's eyes widened in realization.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ohhh! So that's why the fights on those old videos look so wild!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He remembered watching footage of battles led by an elderly Trainer and now understood the difference.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge chuckled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, if you're familiar with the rules, we don't need to waste time explaining."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's start!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The excitement in Surge's voice was palpable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
How long had it been since his last unrestricted battle?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As word spread, Gym trainers and staff gathered to watch. Even Bisques, who had just woken up, joined the crowd.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
The Vermilion Gym battlefield.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge and Johan placed three Pok\u233? Balls each on the central pedestal.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Per the rules, the balls were locked to prevent premature release.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Trainers stepped back to the arena's edges.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tony raised two flags.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The first phase required both Trainers to sprint to the pedestal and retrieve their Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't uncommon for Trainers to sabotage each other's Pok\u233? Balls during this phase.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Battle..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tony slashed the flag downward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Begin!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge launched forward like a bullet, his muscles coiled like springs.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, though quick, was no match for Surge's raw speed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surge smirked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Typical. A twiggy Trainer like you doesn't stand a chance.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He reached the pedestal first, grabbing one of his Pok\u233? Balls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the same time, Surge flung a small knife toward Johan's side of the pedestal, aiming to knock away one of his Pok\u233? Balls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Go, {\b
Magneton!}"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the metallic trio emerged from its ball, Surge barked an order:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"{\b
Discharge! Blanket the field!}"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But something unexpected happened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan stopped mid-sprint.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What's he doing?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233? Ball that Surge had knocked away...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
clicked open by itself.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar burst forth, already holding a massive {\b
Shadow Ball} over his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
