"I'm getting increasingly annoyed with the idea of trading Pok\u233?mon," Johan muttered, eliciting a collective nod of agreement from his Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the Pok\u233?mon world, trading Pok\u233?mon wasn't uncommon and was considered a fairly normal practice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some people treated Pok\u233?mon as toys and found it natural to swap them out when bored.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Others were passionate about battles and used trading to fill gaps in their team.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A smaller group sought to find a more suitable trainer for their Pok\u233?mon to help them grow, resulting in trades for the Pok\u233?mon's betterment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For example, in the original story, Ash and Dawn traded their Aipom and Buizel because Aipom preferred contests and suited Dawn better, while Buizel loved battling and was better off with Ash.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, even in these cases, the Pok\u233?mon's own opinions were sought first.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From Johan's perspective, if a Pok\u233?mon liked battling, nurture it for battles. If it enjoyed contests, train it for that. If it liked neither, let it do what it wants.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Isn't it a trainer's responsibility to cater to their Pok\u233?mon's preferences and talents?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If you're not capable, don't catch them recklessly. If you do, you must take responsibility.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Anyway, let's not dwell on this. What do you guys feel like eating? How about grilled eel over rice?" Johan asked with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His Pok\u233?mon cheered enthusiastically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After wandering around and buying a variety of snacks and treats, Johan felt a bit tired. He found a relatively quiet beach, spread out a picnic blanket, and laid out all the food he'd bought, along with MooMoo Milk, berries, and Pok\u233?blocks he always carried with him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Now it's\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Picnic time!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After dinner, his Pok\u233?mon began playing on the beach.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Vulpix and Tinkatuff built sandcastles together.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar, on the other hand, had somehow procured a pair of goggles. After putting them on, it stood by the shore, taking deep breaths with exaggerated gusto before leaping into the water with a splash. The kids nearby burst into laughter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan looked at Dratini, who was still by his side.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're not going to join them?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Driii~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dratini whimpered softly, looking a little lost in thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed softly, realizing that the fisherman's earlier words might have affected the little Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As he gently stroked Dratini's head, he said quietly, "Why don't you talk to me about it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dratini's round, shiny eyes gazed deeply at Johan before shaking its head and muttering softly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Driii~ Driii~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't sure how to express itself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It just felt like it was the weakest and least useful among Johan's four Pok\u233?mon\u8212?and lately, it had even put on some weight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan chuckled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Pulling Dratini into his arms, he whispered into its ear, "Do you know why that annoying man only wanted to trade for you and not for Gengar or the others?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Driii?" Dratini blinked in confusion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled warmly and whispered, half-jokingly, "Because you're the one with the most potential. That annoying man has a good eye for spotting the best\u8212?my Dratini."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dratini looked skeptical.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan laughed heartily.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Okay, okay, all of you have great potential. But I wasn't lying\u8212?his judgment was accurate."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He then muttered, as if to himself, "I'm just worried that when my Dratini grows up, it won't want to stick around with a 'weak' trainer like me~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Driii!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Never!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dratini suddenly coiled tightly around Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hahaha!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan laughed again, patting the little one on the head. "Alright, alright, I was just joking."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Driii~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dratini looked up, its eyes filled with determination.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It only wanted to stay with Johan forever\u8212?always and always!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the distance, the lights of Vermilion City shone brightly, casting their glow onto the beach. The waves, crashing rhythmically, left white foam on the shore.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, even the sea breeze seemed to soften.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Buzz\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To Johan's surprise, Dratini's body began to emit a dazzling white light, attracting the attention of others on the beach.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A little girl holding a pinwheel tugged on her mother's sleeve, her voice innocent and sweet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Mommy, look! That big brother is evolving!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Because Dratini was wrapped around Johan, the evolving glow enveloped him as well.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Vulpix, Tinkatuff, and Gengar all noticed the commotion and rushed over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Chu Chu?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Did Johan\u8230? evolve?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tinkatuff's eyes widened in disbelief.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar snickered mischievously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yeah, he evolved. Up next, we've got Johan-mon!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
