218: Johan, Please Teach Me!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're... Johan, the teacher?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint scrutinized Johan's features carefully before recognition dawned upon him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan looked puzzled, but Flint grinned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah, I forgot to introduce myself! I'm Flint, the Pewter Gym Leader. My son, Brock, mentioned you to me once."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
The Pewter Gym Leader?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's expression remained neutral, but his Pok\u233?mon\u8212?Gengar and the rest of his team\u8212?immediately perked up. Their eyes gleamed with a mixture of mischief and anticipation as they fixated on Flint like predators spotting prey.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
One of the last two Gym Leaders in the Kanto region!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To Gengar and company, Flint wasn't just Flint; he was a {\i
walking six million Pok\u233?dollars!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint: {\i
\u8230?!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Feeling the weight of their intense gazes, Flint's back suddenly grew cold.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's going on here..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan quickly stepped in front of his team, blocking their line of sight. He diverted Flint's attention, saying with a smile, "Flint, your reputation precedes you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hahaha!" Flint scratched the back of his head, laughing loudly. "You flatter me, Johan!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan nodded seriously. "Father to ten children, raising them while contributing so much to the Pok\u233?mon League. Truly admirable!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint froze mid-laugh, visibly startled by Johan's remark.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Everyone knew Flint's claim to fame: {\i
Pok\u233?mon World's Top Breeder\u8212?of Humans.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His eldest son, Brock, was the "Judge of All Pok\u233?mon." As for his younger sons\u8212?Jiro, Saburo, Goro\u8212?they didn't even merit individual names.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had often wondered if Flint carried some kind of "super-breeder" gene. How else could he explain such prolific parenting?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint wasn't just the "Breeder of Men"\u8212?his wife, Miyuki, deserved that title more. If anything, Flint was merely the {\i
"Planter of Seeds."}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for Brock's obsession with women? That was almost certainly an inherited trait.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Brushing aside the awkward praise, Flint waved his hand modestly. "You could do it too, Johan!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: {\i
\u8230?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Ten kids?} If every one of them wanted to become a trainer, the costs alone... no wonder Brock was such a jack-of-all-trades. Besides being a trainer and breeder, he seemed to have picked up every odd skill just to help keep the family afloat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Anyway... what brings you here, Flint?" Johan asked, steering the conversation elsewhere.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He'd come to this remote mountain because of Gengar, but why was Flint here? Shouldn't he be running the Pewter Gym?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At Johan's question, Flint straightened his posture and responded solemnly: "I'm here to train!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan raised an eyebrow, skeptical.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As a fellow man, Johan's intuition told him the real reason probably involved Flint's wife, Miyuki.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was no secret: Flint was notoriously henpecked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He adored Miyuki but couldn't deny that he was no match for her\u8212?both figuratively and literally.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As a Rock-type specialist, Flint was utterly countered by Miyuki's Water-type expertise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, seeing Johan's dubious expression, Flint quickly added another explanation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"To be honest, running Gym battles is really expensive. Going on a training journey lets me close the Gym for a while... it saves on repair costs."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Uh..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan was momentarily taken aback before realization dawned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gym battles were, indeed, costly\u8212?especially for Rock, Ground, or Steel-type Gyms, where the facilities needed frequent repairs.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Combine that with Flint's responsibility of raising ten children, and it all added up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Life's not easy, huh," Johan murmured, sympathetic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint turned his head away, tilting it skyward as he discreetly wiped at his eyes. "Finally, someone understands me!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"By the way," Flint said, his tone lightening, "what was that massive Gengar all about earlier?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, just an ancient Pok\u233?mon," Johan replied nonchalantly. "I've already reported it to Officer Jenny."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He gave Flint a brief rundown of the events, but the Gym Leader seemed fixated on only one detail: {\i
"Officer Jenny."}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In a flash, Flint darted to the lakeshore. Cupping water in his hands, he slicked back his hair, turned to Johan with a dazzling smile, and asked, "How do I look, Johan?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: {\i
\u8230?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If you hadn't said anything, I'd have mistaken you for Wallace.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not bad," Johan deadpanned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Really?" Flint eagerly checked his reflection in the water.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But just as he leaned closer, a mischievous Gengar emerged silently from the lake, its wide, toothy grin mere inches from Flint's face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For three whole seconds, Flint and Gengar locked eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint: {\i
\u8230?!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Gym Leader leapt nearly three meters into the air, his face pale as a ghost.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No matter how tough a man is, everyone's got something they're scared of.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
---\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The sound of a helicopter approaching interrupted their banter. Within moments, Officer Jenny arrived with two police officers and a pair of archaeologists in tow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Upon spotting her, Flint immediately perked up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a theatrical flourish, he knelt on one knee before Jenny, his face radiating admiration.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Officer Jenny, I'm Flint of Pewt\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Jenny didn't even glance his way. Instead, she briskly walked past him and approached Johan with bright eyes and a rosy complexion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Johan!" she exclaimed, practically glowing like a fangirl meeting her idol.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Crack.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint froze mid-motion, his hopes dashed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
She ignored me...}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thanks to Johan's prominence among the Officer Jenny clan\u8212?owing to his work on the "Anti-Theft Brigade" initiative and occasional online lectures\u8212?his reputation within their ranks was stellar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Add to that Johan's striking looks, rivaling even the likes of Steven Stone, and it wasn't hard to see why Jenny was starstruck.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan greeted her with a polite smile. "Thank you for coming, Officer Jenny."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's no trouble at all\u8212?this is my duty!" Jenny replied earnestly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After Johan explained the situation, he emphasized the importance of safeguarding the ancient Pok\u233?mon artifacts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If possible," he suggested, "store them alongside the bell from the altar. That bell contains the sleeping Giant Jigglypuff. Should the Giant Gengar or Alakazam act up again, Jigglypuff can pacify them."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Jenny nodded, promising to report Johan's contributions to the League for appropriate recognition.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan waved her off modestly. "It's not about the rewards. I'm just curious to see what the League is willing to do with this much ancient power."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Truthfully, while the ancient Pok\u233?mon were powerful, they weren't exactly {\i
useful.} Communication with them was virtually impossible, and taming them seemed out of reach.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Besides," Johan added dryly, "I already have my hands full with one Gengar. I can't imagine taking care of a giant one."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As Jenny's team departed with the artifacts, she turned back with a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Say hi to your cousin in Rustboro for me, Professor Johan!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Watching the helicopter disappear into the distance, Johan sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Johan!" Flint's sudden shout startled him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
THUD!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint dropped to his knees before Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Flint?! What are you doing?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I, uh... slipped," Flint mumbled, quickly rising and brushing himself off. Then, with uncharacteristic solemnity, he declared: "Johan, please teach me! No\u8212?teach my 'friend!'"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Teach what?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leaning in conspiratorially, Flint whispered, "How do you get beautiful women to approach you so easily?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan shot him a sidelong glare.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Excuse me, sir. Aren't you married?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a resigned sigh, Johan replied, "That's not something you can learn, Flint."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint's expression hardened. "My... my friend can endure hardship!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a moment's thought, Johan nodded slowly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, to start..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes?" Flint leaned in eagerly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You need a very handsome face."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint: {\i
\u931?(\u65439?\u1044?\u65439?lll)}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
---\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the two men sat by the lake chatting, Johan couldn't help but notice how Flint, despite his easygoing demeanor, carried the weight of his responsibilities.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For all his flaws, Flint deeply loved his children\u8212?he just didn't always show it the right way.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan listened patiently as Flint vented about his struggles, nodding empathetically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thank you for listening, Johan," Flint said sincerely.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan shrugged. "Every family has its challenges."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, Gengar floated back, gleefully presenting Johan with a Cheri Berry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Accepting it without hesitation, Johan took a bite, much to Flint's astonishment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan, your bond with your Pok\u233?mon is truly admirable," Flint said with genuine admiration.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled faintly. "We've been through a lot together."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Standing abruptly, Flint clenched his fists. "Johan, how about a battle?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I hear you're aiming for the Indigo League. My Pewter Gym badge might come in handy for you. Think of it as my thanks for today!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Wait, isn't a badge supposed to be earned through official means?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed internally.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Once again, it seemed Erika had been spreading his plans around.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
