{\qc
222: A Rainy Night Routine\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Secrets of the Earth} could easily be called Giovanni's magnum opus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was said that Giovanni earned the title {\i
"As long as I stand upon the earth, I shall not be defeated"}, thus gaining the moniker {\b
Giovanni of the Earth}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the {\i
Pok\u233?mon Adventures} manga, the only time Giovanni lost to Red was due to a {\i
cheap shot} involving insulated gloves and a decisive finishing move.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Later, when Green acquired Giovanni's {\i
Secrets of the Earth}, he built a formidable team in under a year.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This demonstrated that {\i
Secrets of the Earth} wasn't just about training Ground-type Pok\u233?mon or teaching Ground-type moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It contained Giovanni's lifetime of experience in raising Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His unparalleled strength, combined with the magnanimity to share his wisdom with others, was what gave Giovanni the aura of a true master.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No wonder Gengar was so engrossed in it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even it seemed to absorb some strategies and methods from the book.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Strictly speaking, without its {\i
Levitate} ability, Gengar could also be considered a Pok\u233?mon "standing upon the earth."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some methods in the book were a little too... destructive.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not for the Pok\u233?mon\u8212?but for Johan's {\b
house}!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing Gengar's serious expression, Johan massaged his temples and sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"All right, all right. That's enough for now. I still have a meeting at school today. I'll be late if we don't leave soon."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar reluctantly ejected the USB drive and swallowed it into its stomach.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the school, the end-of-term faculty meeting was as important as ever.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For Johan, though, participation was more symbolic than anything else.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Originally, he'd planned to attend the meeting today and fly to Kalos tomorrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To avoid arriving unexpectedly, he decided to call Professor Sycamore ahead of time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Surprisingly, Sycamore didn't answer. Instead, a young voice picked up the phone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sorry, Mr. Johan. Professor Sycamore is out on an errand right now..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The voice sounded a bit youthful but clear and articulate\u8212?probably one of Sycamore's assistants.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I see," Johan replied, slightly surprised but relieved.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Good thing I didn't just fly straight to Kalos\u8212?would've been awkward to find no one there.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't unusual for professors to be out in the field, so Johan wasn't too concerned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well then, when Professor Sycamore returns, could you have him give me a call? Thanks."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course! That's no problem at all."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"By the way... who am I speaking with?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alan. Mr. Johan, my name's Alan. I'm Professor Sycamore's assistant."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alan?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The name sparked an image in Johan's mind\u8212?a stoic, cool-looking teenager.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Alan}, the {\i
Water-Absorb Charizard} Trainer!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ash's inability to win the Kalos League was a sore spot for many Pok\u233?mon fans.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And his greatest rival? Alan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although Ash later claimed victory in Alola, that league wasn't exactly fully developed yet, making the victory feel somewhat {\i
provincial}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, it couldn't be denied that "Water-Absorb Charizard" memes aside, Alan was incredibly strong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had single-handedly defeated ten opponents and had the backing of Fire-type Elite Four member Malva.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But right now, Alan was just a research assistant for Professor Sycamore\u8212?far from the powerhouse he'd become.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"All right, Alan. Thanks again."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After hanging up, Johan paused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar tilted its head, sensing Johan's hesitation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, I guess I'm not going to Kalos anytime soon. That means... I'm free for now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, the sky darkened, and light rain began to fall. Johan hurried to take shelter under the gatehouse.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Does this mean... I'm going to have to write exam papers for the kids?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The term exams were still a ways off, and writing tests this early would only give the students nightmares.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Failing too many students wouldn't look good either.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Guess I'll save that for the last minute, like always."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Watching the rain grow heavier, Johan smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This weather's perfect for staying indoors."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, they were low on groceries at home.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan released his Pok\u233?mon, lining them up in a neat row with Gengar at the lead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Holding up his phone, he said, "You have three seconds to call out what you want to eat."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!" (Fried pork cutlet!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowu!" (Vanilla ice cream!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Chu!" (Mapo tofu!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa!" (Sashimi!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Excellent!" Johan nodded approvingly. "Then tonight... we'll have dumplings!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233?mon: ???\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
You called us out here just to ignore us?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!" (Get him!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar growled menacingly, rallying the others.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonair prepared to bind him, Gengar readied {\i
Paralysis}, and Vulpix froze the right flank with {\i
Ice Beam}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Thud.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tinkatuff set its hammer on the ground with a heavy clang, smiling mischievously as it dragged the hammer toward Johan step by step...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Kalos, Lumiose City.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In a quiet caf\u233?, two men sat across from each other.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The red-haired man exuded an aura of authority\u8212?{\b
Lysandre}, leader of Team Flare and representative of the Lysandre Labs.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Opposite him was a scruffy man in his thirties, wearing a dark blue shirt\u8212?{\b
Professor Sycamore}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though they belonged to different research organizations, the two were close friends.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Any progress lately?" Lysandre asked, passing Sycamore a cup of coffee.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sycamore smiled. "Same as always."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lysandre wasn't surprised. Instead, he slid a small slip of paper across the table.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's this?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A ruin. You'll find what you're looking for there."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sycamore hesitated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He didn't need to ask\u8212?Lysandre clearly meant {\i
Mega Stones} and {\i
Key Stones}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, instead of taking the paper immediately, Sycamore stirred his coffee thoughtfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lysandre."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmm?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sycamore studied Lysandre's eyes for a long moment before sighing, his tone filled with quiet disappointment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sometimes, I feel like you've changed\u8212?become someone I don't recognize. But other times..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I feel like you're still the same person you used to be."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lysandre chuckled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I haven't changed."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The smile faded from his face as he turned to look out the window, staring at the bustling streets of Lumiose City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's changed... is this world."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Or rather, what needs to change... is this world!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For a fleeting moment, his face twisted into an expression of rage and madness.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sycamore caught it, his heart sinking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But he quickly regained his composure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Taking the slip of paper, he stood up. "When I get back, I'll introduce you to a friend."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A friend?" Lysandre raised an eyebrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sycamore's circle of friends was notoriously small.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Smiling cryptically, Sycamore left the caf\u233?.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Looking up at the overcast sky, he sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I need to find him a good psychologist. Lysandre's mindset is growing increasingly extreme..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hopefully, Johan can help him."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Hoenn, Rustboro City. Caf\u233?, Second Floor.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Condensation misted the windows as warm air filled the room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonair used its tail to draw crooked doodles on the foggy glass, smiling contentedly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rubbing his face, Johan walked over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The fat blob is Gengar. The six tails are Vulpix. The one with the hammer is Tinkatuff. And the one flying... is you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Turning to Dragonair, he deadpanned, "So tell me, what's this lump on the ground?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa" (You guess)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan rolled his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Guess whether I'll guess or not."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gathering his Pok\u233?mon around the table, he sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Can you guys stop taking things so seriously? I was just teasing you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233?mon were now behaving, though Johan knew they had him wrapped around their little paws.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"All right. I'll teach you how to knead dough and roll dumpling wrappers."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Making dumplings was a family affair.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Besides, this way he could keep an eye on Gengar\u8212?he didn't want it sneaking into the kitchen while he was distracted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar excelled at kneading dough, thanks to its "ball-rolling" expertise. Vulpix's six tails made it the most efficient wrapper of all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for Tinkatuff...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its raw strength made it perfect for chopping the filling. Johan handed it two plastic knives and assigned it the new task of dicing vegetables.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonair, lacking hands, had its tail repurposed as a rolling pin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Make only what we can eat," Johan said as he worked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He glanced over to see Gengar with a mountain of dumpling wrappers piled next to it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hot dumplings, golden-fried pork cutlets, vanilla ice cream, spicy mapo tofu, and fresh sashimi soon filled the table.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cheers!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan clinked his soda can with his Pok\u233?mon's drinks\u8212?Moomoo Milk, fruit juice, and sodas of their choice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's eat!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The table descended into chaos.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gengar, don't dump the entire plate into your mouth! And no using {\i
Double Team}!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah! \u931?(\u1076?lll)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As laughter echoed through the warm, light-filled room, the camera slowly pulled away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Outside, the rain continued to fall softly against the windows.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowu?" (Who made this ugly dumpling?)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Must be Gengar!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!" (It's clearly yours!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Was it Tinkatuff?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Chu!" (This masterpiece is mine!)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then it's Dragonair!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa?" (Me?)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, who cares? It's delicious... I was just trying to make a Vulpix, but it fell apart halfway through."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
More laughter rang out, spreading warmth into the rainy night.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
