269: Let\u8217?s Play It Safe This Time\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
5 bonus chapter's coming out at 11 AM EST. So I ask that you save you're powerstones until then.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
-----------\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the evening, Johan dined with Steven, Flannery, Roxanne, and Professor Oak's group at a hotel near Indigo Plateau.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a casual gathering to chat and enjoy the lively atmosphere, but it also served as a small celebration of Johan making it to the quarterfinals.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though celebrating this early might seem premature, advancing to the top eight was indeed a big milestone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For most trainers, especially first-time competitors, reaching the top eight was a major achievement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From this stage onward, all matches would be held in the main arena and broadcast live across all platforms by the league.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unlike the preliminary rounds, where matches in different arenas split viewership, the main arena only had one channel for live coverage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In other words, the viewership would at least quadruple!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, having lived in a world where "traffic is king," understood better than anyone what such exposure could bring.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even something as simple as endorsing a product, like Leon did, could yield massive profits.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With increased fame and supporters, opportunities to participate in minor tournaments or exhibition matches would also roll in, bringing in considerable funds.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Many champions like Cynthia, Diantha, and Lorelei derived a significant portion of their income from such events.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But more importantly, from the top eight onward, all matches would be full 6v6 battles. The difficulty would spike dramatically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some trainers who shone in 3v3 battles might struggle in 6v6, simply because of the greater number of Pok\u233?mon they needed to train and rotate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to Johan's research, only one other top-eight finalist was a first-time league participant besides him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That trainer wasn't highly regarded by most people.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, however, was an exception.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some people had previously speculated that his Kubfu and Dragonair were his strongest Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But after witnessing his Tinkaton's sheer destructive power during its "one-hammer sweep," those doubts vanished.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In fact, many now believed that Tinkaton was stronger than Dragonair, and certainly stronger than Kubfu.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Naturally, this led people to speculate how powerful Johan's Ninetales and Gengar might be.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Given the circumstances, a small celebration seemed fitting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Lorelei, who had just wrapped up an exam, came to join them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And as for who would pick up the bill...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No one needed to.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The hotel belonged to Steven's family.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan, can you teach me how to train my Pok\u233?mon?" Ash asked, his face smeared with cake, eyes sparkling with excitement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Already passionate about becoming a Pok\u233?mon Master, Ash's desire grew even stronger after watching Johan's matches.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He dreamed of commanding his Pok\u233?mon with the same calm confidence, achieving those effortless sweeps.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmm..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan clicked his tongue, pondering how to respond to Ash's request.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After some thought, he said:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ash, as someone who's been through this, let me give you a few pieces of advice."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ash nodded eagerly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"First, never release your Pok\u233?mon without a good reason."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ash tilted his head in confusion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Why would he release his Pok\u233?mon for no reason?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Who would be bored enough to do that?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Second, if you leave a Pok\u233?mon somewhere and promise to pick it up later, do it as soon as possible."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course! I wouldn't want to be apart from my Pok\u233?mon for too long!" Ash clenched his fists with determination.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan chuckled and continued.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Third, if you have the chance to step in yourself, don't always rely on your Pok\u233?mon to do the fighting."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ash scratched his head, utterly perplexed by Johan's advice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What kind of suggestions were these?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, he trusted Johan's strength and wisdom, so he nodded in agreement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Most people present took Johan's words as a joke.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only Professor Oak seemed to be deep in thought, casting a curious glance at Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Had Johan noticed something special about Ash?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After dinner, Professor Oak called Johan out to the balcony.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan, did you sense something unique about Ash?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sense?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Did he need to sense it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Everyone from Pallet Town was practically superhuman!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Especially Ash.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had been resurrected multiple times\u8212?once even by Ho-Oh.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And considering Ho-Oh's legendary connection to the creation of the three Legendary Beasts...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Ho-Oh revived Ash, then logically speaking...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ash = Three Legendary Beasts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No, I just think..." Johan smiled faintly before continuing, "That kid has the potential to be incredible."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Oak chuckled softly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Funny you should say that. There were two people in whom I once saw reflections of my younger self."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Red and Ash?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Red would be starting his journey soon, while Ash probably had another two years to go.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak nodded. "Yes. But now, I've found a third."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan felt a chill run down his spine.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Please don't say my name.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The people you "see yourself in" always end up enduring insane trials!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Red was frozen in ice for years, and Ash? He died and came back to life countless times.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, curiosity got the better of him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Green?" he guessed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak shook his head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Green is a fine boy, but perhaps because he spends so much time helping me, he's a bit... too rational."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Great.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now rationality was a bad thing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thinking about it, though, it made sense. Pok\u233?mon often performed better when their trainers could inspire them with raw emotion rather than cold logic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
People like Red and Ash, with their emotionally driven personalities, were particularly good at triggering those "comeback" moments.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wait a minute.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I'm pretty rational, too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan frowned, wondering what Oak was getting at.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The professor gave him a serious look.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You remind me a lot of myself when I was young."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Me?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No way!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I'd never be such a heartbreaker!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"In fact, I'd say you're even more talented than I was back then." Oak smiled warmly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan clutched his chest dramatically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ugh, my heart!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Feeling a bit unsettled, he quickly changed the subject.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"By the way, Professor Oak, I ran into Chrysa recently."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak froze for a moment, his expression turning complicated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His lips parted slightly before he carefully asked, "How... how is she doing?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan shot him a sideways glance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"She asked me to pass on a message."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak forced a wry smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let me guess... it was a curse or a hex aimed at me?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smirked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No. She said... you should cut back on smoking."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oak's entire body stiffened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He stood frozen in place.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Satisfied, Johan took a deep breath and headed back inside, leaving one final remark.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Maybe you should visit her sometime."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As he walked back inside, Johan's face broke into a mischievous grin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ah, revenge feels sweet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alone on the balcony, Oak slowly pulled out a cigarette from his pocket.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lighting it, he took a deep drag.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The soft glow illuminated his conflicted expression.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Puff... sigh..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The fifth day of the Indigo League Tournament.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The schedule was intense, with one round completed almost every day\u8212?a real test of both trainers' and Pok\u233?mon's endurance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Today marked the semifinals.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The venue had moved to the main stadium, where the sacred flames of Moltres burned brightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The crowd's enthusiasm was at an all-time high.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Today, we have some very special guests joining us!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The announcer hyped up the audience and viewers alike.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Please welcome the esteemed Professor Oak, a leading figure in Pok\u233?mon research!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Next, the Fighting-type Elite Four member from Kanto, Bruno!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And finally, the Gym Leader from Ecruteak City in Johto, Morty!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Each name was met with roaring applause.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At first glance, Morty seemed the least notable of the three.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, those in the know understood his strength.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
