{\b
{\qc
302: The \u8220?Rule Maker\u8221?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait, what's this? A surprise stream?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Didn't he already finish the Battle Tower? Why is there another stream? How's my Gengar? Has it recovered?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Two Battle Frontier facilities in one day? What's next on the list?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hold up, did I see that right? Johan is challenging the Battle Pike?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is he planning on streaming nonstop for an entire month?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The moment Scott's stream, titled {\b
"Johan Teaches You How to Conquer the Battle Frontier"}, went live, viewers flooded in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some were well-versed in the rules of each facility, but most weren't.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To help, Scott thoughtfully pinned a detailed explanation of the Battle Pike's rules to the livestream.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait... 140 rooms of pure luck? Johan is seriously daring!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I heard someone once got stuck inside for an entire month."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Who's been feeding Johan lies about his good luck?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The chat erupted into chaos.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan stood at the ominous entrance to the Battle Pike, designed like a giant Seviper's open maw. He wasn't paying attention to the livestream chat but could easily imagine what they were saying.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Smirking, he muttered, "Hmph. Time for you all to witness the true power of the Johan family's luck!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With confident strides, he entered the facility.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The first room was empty, save for three doors ahead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the Pok\u233?mon Adventures manga, Emerald was notoriously unlucky in the Battle Pike, exploring 139 rooms before finally reaching the Frontier Brain in the 140th.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hakuryu, I'm leaving this to you," Johan said to his Dragonair. "No overthinking. Just pick a door by instinct."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonair tilted its head quizzically but obediently waved its tail to point at a door.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, however, didn't walk toward the chosen door.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Instead, he stroked his chin thoughtfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Good. That eliminates one wrong choice."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonair: ???\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Turning to Jirachi, he communicated through his Aura powers:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Jirachi, it's your turn. Two doors left. Pick whichever feels right."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Jirachi's eyes sparkled with excitement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"This one! Johan, this one!"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Without hesitation, Johan opened the door Jirachi had chosen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The room beyond was completely empty \u8212? no traps, no trainers, and no Pok\u233?mon guards.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The livestream chat exploded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Excuse me?! Did he just blatantly cheat?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is this even allowed? Using Dragonair to 'filter' the bad choices?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, technically, the rules don't say you can't use your Pok\u233?mon's abilities. It's dirty, but fair."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I can't believe what I'm seeing..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan couldn't care less about the outrage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is nothing," he muttered. "If I wanted, I could just have Gengar phase through walls to find the Frontier Brain directly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, he decided against it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While using Gengar would make this much faster, Johan figured someone else might try the same trick in the future. It was better to address this loophole now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Turning toward the camera for the first time, Johan said, "Let me show you another method. But don't follow my example."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gesturing to his shadow, he called, "Gengar."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar emerged, yawning and rubbing its eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Check out the next room. Let me know if it's safe."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar's eyes lit up mischievously. It cackled, then phased into the adjacent room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moments later, Gengar reappeared, holding a Potion in its hand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
There's someone in there, but I grabbed this while they weren't looking.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The smug grin on its face was unmistakable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The livestream chat erupted in disbelief.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"??????"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Did he just... send Gengar to rob someone?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not gonna lie, that's hilarious."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Teacher Johan, are you serious right now?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan turned to a dumbfounded Scott and said with a grin, "Of course, I wouldn't recommend this method. Right, Mr. Scott?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Scott's expression froze, and after a brief pause, he nodded stiffly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll... update the rules immediately."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The chat went wild again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You've got to be kidding! He's changing the rules mid-stream?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan's officially the biggest troll ever!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why does this feel less like cheating and more like... education?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While the audience hurled playful insults, Johan gained a new nickname: {\b
The Rule Maker}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Steven, Flannery, and Roxanne couldn't help but laugh.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's so like Johan," Flannery remarked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Perhaps it's his down-to-earth, unpretentious nature that makes him so likable," Roxanne added.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Deep within the Battle Pike, the Frontier Brain Lucy \u8212? or as fans called her, the Queen of the Pipes \u8212? watched the livestream with a bemused expression.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
This guy is something else,} she thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Dragonair and Jirachi as his guides, Johan progressed through the Battle Pike with remarkable ease.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not only did he avoid any major obstacles, but he also collected a variety of items \u8212? like Potions and Berries \u8212? originally meant to help struggling trainers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For most challengers, the Battle Pike required meticulous preparation and endurance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For Johan, it was a casual stroll.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In less than an hour, he reached the final room, where Lucy awaited.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucy was a quiet and reserved woman, not one for idle chatter. Seeing Johan enter, she simply stated:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If you want the symbol, you'll have to beat me first."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan knew Lucy specialized in status-based strategies, particularly using moves like Substitute and Toxic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Viewers familiar with Lucy's tactics chimed in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Substitute-Toxic strategy? Pfft. Does she know who she's up against?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan's about to teach everyone how to counter that nonsense."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pipe Queen Lucy? More like Pipe Dream Lucy. She's doomed."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the referee signaled the start of the battle, both trainers released their Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucy's choice was Shuckle \u8212? a small, unassuming Pok\u233?mon with a red, hollow shell dotted with holes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Shuckle, the Mold Pok\u233?mon. A Bug- and Rock-type known for fermenting berries into juice within its shell, often underestimated due to its appearance," Rotom Dex explained.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, however, wasn't fooled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
