{\qc
323: Bell Tower, The Sacred Wood of Ho-Oh\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Johto Region, Ecruteak City.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Nighttime.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan and Morty, along with their Pok\u233?mon, visited the Ecruteak Dance Theater to watch the Kimono Girls perform.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To say the least, the Eevees were absolutely dazzling. They were stunningly white and unbelievably cute.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Dance Theater was most famous for the five Kimono Sisters of Ecruteak, each owning a different evolution of Eevee: Flareon, Vaporeon, Jolteon, Umbreon, and Espeon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The performances were clearly reminiscent of Pok\u233?mon Contests in their elegance and style.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After the dances concluded, the theater invited audience members onstage for battles with the Kimono Sisters, allowing them to choose one of the Eeveelutions to challenge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Whether they won or lost, participants would receive small prizes from the theater\u8212?a tradition that had become one of its most iconic attractions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, however, was not particularly interested.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If the prizes were evolution stones, he would've been more enthusiastic, but clearly, giving out evolution stones every time would bankrupt the theater.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Occasionally offering them as special rewards was enough to draw in large audiences.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This, Johan thought, was yet another reminder of how much Pok\u233?mon battles pervaded this world. Even a dance theater had to include Pok\u233?mon battles to keep the crowds coming.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After the show, Johan returned to the Pok\u233?mon Center in Ecruteak City with his companions to rest for the night.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
The next morning.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan groggily opened his eyes, then quickly shut them again, mumbling,\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rotom, what time is it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's 6:30 a.m., Rotom!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hovering mid-air, the Rotom Pok\u233?dex cheerfully continued,\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Today's weather in Ecruteak City is sunny, with a mild east wind at Level 3. It's a great day for sightseeing, Rotom!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"6:30, huh..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan rubbed his eyes, burying his face into Ice Ninetales' soft fur. The cool sensation instantly jolted him awake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He couldn't deny it\u8212?after evolving, Ice Ninetales had not only grown stronger in its Ice-type abilities but had also gained greater control over its powers. The uncontrollable chill it used to emit had been significantly reduced.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowoo~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The little one puffed up its cheeks, clearly displeased at having its sleep interrupted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan chuckled. "Rotom, play a song."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Right away, Rotom!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Soon, an intense rock song boomed from the Rotom Pok\u233?dex, with electrifying vocals and sharp rhythms energizing the team in no time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowoo~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ice Ninetales stretched gracefully, its sleek body and nine elegant tails unfurling as it rose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After everyone freshened up and started their morning routines, Johan noticed something odd.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The normally peppy little Pok\u233?mon seemed... melancholic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hold on, Rotom," Johan called. "Whose song are you playing?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom displayed a photo of a rock band on its screen: a lead singer alongside four Pok\u233?mon bandmates.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pok\u233?mon were: a drummer Rillaboom, a guitarist Toxtricity (Amped Form), a bassist Toxtricity (Low Key Form), and a co-vocalist Obstagoon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's the Galar Region's Spikemuth Band, Rotom! The lead singer is the 'Melancholy Nessa,' Rotom!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No wonder. A rock band singing emo songs? That tracks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You know," Johan mused, "if anyone can sing, it's Meowth."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He hummed a bit. "Aoh-ee, Aoh-ee..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wasn't that how it went?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Maybe we should get Meowth to go solo again," Johan joked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Singing, acting in movies and TV shows...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Hmmm. Meowth might just become a triple-threat celebrity.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan shook his head and filed the idea away for later.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
After breakfast}, Johan took his Pok\u233?mon to the free training grounds behind the Pok\u233?mon Center for some light practice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Later, he met up with Morty, and the two set off together for Bell Tower.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
On the way to Bell Tower.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To reach Bell Tower, they first had to walk through {\b
Chime Path}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lined with trees that glowed a permanent autumnal gold, Chime Path was home to many lively wild Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The warm hues of the leaves created a serene and uplifting atmosphere, making it a popular spot for tourists visiting Ecruteak City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, the real draw of Chime Path was its end: the sacred Bell Tower.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ordinary people couldn't enter Bell Tower, but Johan and Morty were on a special mission.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
At Bell Tower's base.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A monk in gray-and-white robes was sweeping the steps leading to the tower. When he saw the two Trainers, he paused, bowed respectfully, but said nothing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan couldn't help but give the monk a second glance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As everyone knows, the person sweeping the entrance of a major temple or shrine is never an ordinary individual.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar, meanwhile, found the monk's actions amusing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar mimicked the monk's bow, folding one hand in front of itself and bending slightly at the waist.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The monk paused, clearly caught off guard. Though his rigorous training typically kept him composed, he couldn't suppress a faint smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Your Pok\u233?mon has a strong connection to the Buddha," the monk said with a serene nod.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan raised an eyebrow. {\i
A ghost like Gengar, connected to the Buddha? That's a strange image.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar, on the other hand, was loving the attention. It bowed again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~" {\i
Why, thank you!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
No one was actually praising you!} Johan thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Inside Bell Tower.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Bell Tower was much larger than Johan had expected. Even the first floor felt vast and open.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thanks to Morty's connections, Johan\u8212?acknowledged as someone who had earned Entei's favor\u8212?was granted access to the upper floors after a brief check of his identity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As they climbed the creaky wooden stairs, they passed monks on every level.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some were meditating, others studying ancient texts, yet none seemed to pay the visitors much mind.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wild Pok\u233?mon roamed freely throughout the tower as well, which Morty explained was by design.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Bell Tower, like the Burned Tower, had been built to celebrate the harmony between humans and Pok\u233?mon. It welcomed wild Pok\u233?mon to come and go as they pleased.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Reaching the top floors.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the staircase between the ninth and tenth floors, Johan and Morty came across a large wooden carving.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It depicted none other than the legendary Pok\u233?mon, {\b
Ho-Oh}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar pointed at the carving excitedly. {\i
The one holding the camera!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Morty: "???"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed, rubbing his temples.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan-sensei, have you seen Ho-Oh before?" Morty asked, finally catching on.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Morty's family had worshipped Ho-Oh for generations, which was one reason he was allowed access to Bell Tower. Yet even his ancestors hadn't seen Ho-Oh since it had left the tower.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"We encountered it once in Pallet Town," Johan explained.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Morty's eyes lit up in understanding.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
No wonder.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
No wonder Entei sought him out and granted him its blessing.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And the 'camera' thing?" Morty asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan coughed awkwardly. "Uh, don't worry about it." He quickly moved on.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
The top floor.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On a large cushion sat an elderly monk with snow-white eyebrows cascading down to his shoulders.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two strong, muscular young monks stood at his sides, exuding an air of discipline.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Honored Elder," Morty greeted with a respectful bow, and Johan followed suit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar, too, mimicked the motion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The elder smiled warmly, his gaze lingering on Gengar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This little one is deeply connected to the Buddha," he said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah, ka-kaah~~" Gengar puffed up with pride, giving Johan a smug look.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
See? Even the old master says I'm great!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan resisted the urge to roll his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Morty explained Johan's request, and after hearing the story, the elder nodded toward one of the younger monks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The monk returned moments later, carrying a large, sturdy log.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Thud!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He placed it on the ground with a heavy thump.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This wood," the elder said, "comes from the very perch where Ho-Oh once rested. It is exactly what you seek."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before Johan could respond, the elder added, "May I see the {\b
Rainbow Feather}?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan and Morty both froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Morty was stunned that Johan had the Rainbow Feather.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, on the other hand, wondered how the elder even knew about it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, he retrieved the shimmering, multicolored feather from his pocket.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing it, the elder nodded knowingly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So vibrant, so full of life... You are truly someone who has earned Ho-Oh's recognition."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Rainbow Feather pulsed faintly, as if in agreement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The elder chuckled. "Even the Rainbow Feather seems pleased with you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan laughed nervously, tucking the feather back into his pocket.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The elder continued, "This wood is yours. It once supported Ho-Oh itself and should serve your needs well."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan was surprised. {\i
That easy? No strings attached?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had been prepared to fight\u8212?or at least negotiate. Instead, they'd just handed him the wood.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Gengar looked confused, scratching its head. {\i
No battle?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The elder smiled knowingly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had heard about the destruction at Ecruteak Gym the day before. Someone capable of clashing with Entei and earning its blessing wasn't someone he wanted testing the tower's durability.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Go on," the elder said, dismissing them with a wave.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As they left, Johan glanced at the massive log in Tinkaton's hands.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
If Ho-Oh ever returns and finds part of its tower missing...}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Well, that would be a problem for future Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
