{\b
{\qc
324: Picnic at the Lake of Rage\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
That's it?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan was surprised by how smoothly things had gone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leaving Bell Tower with the sacred wood in hand, he couldn't help but feel like the elder monk might have laid some kind of trap.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But as it turned out, Johan was simply overthinking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Initially, he had expected to spend three or four days in Ecruteak City. Instead, everything was resolved in just two days.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Should I... stop by Mahogany Town?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Oak had asked Johan during the Indigo League to check in on Pryce and see if he could offer any help.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan hadn't forgotten, but he hadn't had the chance to visit Johto until now. With Mahogany Town just east of Ecruteak City and accessible by maglev train, it seemed like a good time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Having made up his mind, Johan expressed his gratitude to Morty once again before leaving.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Morty was polite enough to personally escort them to the station.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Johto Region, Mahogany Town.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mahogany Town was a quaint, tranquil settlement. Its population was small, and the slow pace of life made it quite comfortable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Were it not for Pryce's Mahogany Gym and the Lake of Rage, this town might not have drawn much attention at all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Team Rocket having vacated the lake and the infamous red Gyarados captured by Lance, Mahogany Town had recently regained some vitality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So this is Mahogany Town," Johan remarked as he and his Pok\u233?mon stepped out of the maglev station.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He couldn't help but think about Pryce's situation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a complicated matter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For starters, Johan couldn't be certain whether this world's Pryce mirrored his animated counterpart, who had shut himself off emotionally after losing his Piloswine.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or if Pryce's trauma was instead related to the death of his Lapras.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
One thing was clear: this Pryce likely wasn't the "Masked Man" from the Pok\u233?mon Adventures manga.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or rather, this world probably didn't have a character as ridiculously overpowered as the Masked Man.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Just showing up and offering to 'help' would probably get me turned away," Johan mused, pulling out his phone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He decided to call Professor Oak for more information, at least to determine whether Pryce's change in personality was due to Piloswine or Lapras.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hello, Johan!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Professor Oak's cheerful voice came through the phone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Oak, I'm in Mahogany Town right now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Mahogany Town? Are you planning to challenge Pryce's gym?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Didn't you ask me to check on Pryce when I had the chance?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I did? Oh..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, right! Yes, I think I did!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: {\i
...}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ahahaha! Sorry, I've been swamped with work at the lab, so I forgot!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suppressing the urge to roll his eyes, Johan asked for more details about Pryce's situation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unfortunately, Professor Oak's response was less than helpful.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I don't know much, actually. After I gave up being a Trainer to focus on research, Pryce and I didn't talk for a long time. By the time I saw him again, he was already like that."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As expected, Professor Oak wasn't exactly reliable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hanging up, Johan briefly considered calling Karen of the Elite Four for insight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But he quickly dismissed the idea.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"One headache at a time. Getting two of them involved at once would be a duet of ice and ghosts."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowoo?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar and Ice Ninetales both turned to him quizzically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed. "I wasn't talking about you two."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Without wasting more time, he made his way toward the Mahogany Gym.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Johan arrived at the gym, he found the doors shut and a sign hanging on them that read:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Gym Leader is out. Gym temporarily closed."}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Tch." Johan clicked his tongue. "Classic Pryce. Shuts down the gym whenever he feels like it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While other gym leaders worried about meeting "performance" requirements and passing League evaluations, Pryce seemed entirely unconcerned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If the League threatened to fire him, Pryce's likely response would be: {\i
Fine. Fire me.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The man hadn't even wanted to be an Elite Four member, let alone a mere gym leader.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What now?} Gengar gestured.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan adjusted his glasses. "Nothing to do. Either it's bad luck for us or bad timing for Pryce. Fate is fate."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar rolled its eyes. {\i
And you call me dramatic? You just left Bell Tower and started talking like this.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What a waste of time.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's not a waste," Johan replied, shaking his head. "Let's go have a picnic by the Lake of Rage."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A picnic? Gengar and Ice Ninetales instantly perked up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Picnic time!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
The Lake of Rage.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Situated north of Mahogany Town, the Lake of Rage wasn't far. Johan and his Pok\u233?mon took their time enjoying the scenery as they strolled toward the lake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When they arrived, the view was breathtaking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
What a massive lake!} Gengar exclaimed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The clear sky reflected on the shimmering water. The gentle rustling of trees in the wind and the occasional splash of a Magikarp leaping from the lake created a serene atmosphere.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Lake of Rage was Johto's largest freshwater lake, teeming with resources\u8212?primarily Magikarp.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Legend had it that the lake was once a volcanic crater. After the volcano went dormant, a group of Gyarados brought torrential rain, turning the crater into a lake where they eventually settled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Fishermen working on the lake needed to tread carefully. Provoking an angry Gyarados\u8212?or worse, a group of them\u8212?was no joke.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan found a shaded patch of grass near the lake, perfect for their picnic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He spread out a picnic blanket and released all his Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ku~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kubfu took a deep breath.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Nature... it's so vast!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~!" Gengar stretched theatrically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
The Lake of Rage... it's all water!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
You two are a perfect pair.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The happiest of the bunch was Dragonair, who immediately dove into the water and swam gleefully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar, not wanting to be left out, donned its goggles, took a deep breath, and leapt in with a splash.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It began swimming in a flamboyant display\u8212?backstroke, breaststroke, butterfly stroke.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the shore, Johan chuckled while watching Gengar, then turned to his other Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Charcadet, heat some water for me."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Goka~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ninetales, chill the milk."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowoo~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nearby, Tinkaton sat quietly with a scroll in hand, while Kubfu dozed off after a few punches.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The soft warmth of the winter sun was truly relaxing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan prepped snacks and desserts, placing seven energy cubes on the picnic blanket. He then made himself a cup of coffee, settling into his folding chair to bask in the sun.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
This is the life,} Johan thought as he lazily sipped his coffee, admiring the distant mountain range that stretched across the horizon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In his mind, this was how Trainers and Pok\u233?mon should live: eating, lounging, and eating again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Someday, when I don't have to worry about money anymore, I'll pull a Master Roshi\u8212?buy an island, find a nice lady, and live quietly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After some time, Johan noticed something amiss.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Where's Gengar?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He scanned the lake and realized the mischievous ghost was nowhere to be seen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan wasn't worried about Gengar's safety. The cheeky Pok\u233?mon was smart enough to run if things got dangerous.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What concerned Johan were the wild Pok\u233?mon of the lake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Charcadet pointed toward the shoreline.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There, a soaked Gengar waddled out of the water, happily removing its goggles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Beside it stood a plump, pale-blue Pok\u233?mon with tiny eyes and a blank expression that rivaled a Slowpoke's.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a {\b
Quagsire.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Quagsire, the Water Fish Pok\u233?mon. A Water- and Ground-type, known for its easygoing and carefree nature, Rotom!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom Dex snapped a picture, though Quagsire's shadow didn't appear in the photo.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan raised an eyebrow. "What's with the Quagsire?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Woopa~ (O.)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Quagsire waved at Johan and his Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan hesitated for a moment before inviting it over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why not? Join us for lunch. I made plenty."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~" Gengar guided the clumsy Quagsire to the picnic area.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The other Pok\u233?mon were initially curious but quickly warmed up to their new guest, happily sharing food and energy cubes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Woopa~! (\u9661?.)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Quagsire's face lit up as it savored the curry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eat as much as you like," Johan said with a smile. "There's more if you're still hungry."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blushing slightly, Quagsire nodded and continued eating, clearly enjoying itself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the group dined, a calm yet icy voice interrupted them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So this is where you've wandered off to."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan turned to see an elderly man in a wheelchair, pushed by a Jynx.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The man had white hair, a scarf around his neck, and a stern expression.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was none other than {\b
Pryce, the Mahogany Gym Leader!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
