{\b
In the Oreburgh Mines.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Aerodactyl flew restlessly through the not-so-spacious cavern, but it showed no intention of leaving the mine.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In ancient times, this had been its domain. As the ruler of its territory, it was unwilling to leave the mine.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was precisely the tricky part.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If a large-scale battle occurred, it could cause irreparable damage to the Oreburgh Mine. A collapse would disrupt the mine's operations and have significant consequences for the entire Oreburgh City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet the Aerodactyl couldn't simply be left unchecked. Its presence was halting all work in the mine, and it made further exploration into the cavern containing the stone tablets impossible.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia could easily subdue the Aerodactyl if needed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The real issue, however, was what came afterward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
