{\qc
416: Do You Understand the Value of a \u8216?Tactical Master\u8217??\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You did well, Stonjourner."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gordie spoke to the Pok\u233? Ball as he recalled his Pok\u233?mon, then immediately took out his third Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Without any hesitation, he tossed it forward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His confidence remained unwavering\u8212?if anything, he looked even more confident than before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As if the previous battle hadn't affected him at all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Go, Coalossal!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was Gordie's signature Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It resembled a massive, bipedal dinosaur, its entire body composed of hardened, jet-black stone. On its back, it carried a coal mound, glowing with a deep red heat, constantly emitting waves of white-hot steam.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Coalossal, the Coal Pok\u233?mon, was a Rock/Fire-type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But truthfully, this wasn't the most ideal typing\u8212?it had double weaknesses to both Ground and Water and an additional weakness to Rock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, if used correctly\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Stonjourner left behind its stones on the field!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, the announcer pointed out something most of the audience had overlooked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As Coalossal entered the field, the scattered Stonjourner's Rocks from earlier began to glow faintly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait\u8230? is he activating Power Spot like this?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Holy crap\u8212?so this is how you trigger Power Spot in singles?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Learned it! Learned it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The crowd erupted in shock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clearly, this was Gordie's exclusive strategy\u8212?something most trainers wouldn't even think of. Even if they tried to mimic it, they'd likely fail.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, who had already noticed this earlier, twitched the corner of his mouth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yeah. Figures."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So we're just outright breaking the game now, huh?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was basically a 2v1.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Stonjourner's Rocks remained on the field, activating Power Spot, massively boosting Coalossal's attack power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And yet\u8230? Gordie wasn't done.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Adjusting his glasses, he confidently waved his hand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Coalossal\u8212?Steam Engine, activate!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garrr!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The coal on Coalossal's back glowed an intense crimson, and thick white steam gushed out like a raging furnace.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under this steam boost, Coalossal's entire body became blindingly fast!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its Steam Engine ability had triggered!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steam Engine: When hit by a Water- or Fire-type attack, Speed is maximized!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maximized.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That meant it instantly jumped up by SIX stages!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait\u8212?Coalossal hasn't even been attacked yet?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yeah! How did Steam Engine activate?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The audience was confused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's the water!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the sharp-eyed announcer noticed something most had missed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The lingering water from Rotom's Hydro Pumps earlier\u8212?Coalossal had absorbed it!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Coalossal had landed right inside a crater left by Stonjourner's Earthquake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That crater was flooded with leftover water from Rotom's repeated attacks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
