{\qc
422: You Won\u8217?t Even Call Me \u8216?Teacher\u8217?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan, don't hold back\u8212?crush him!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Among everyone, Flint was undoubtedly the most excited about Johan facing Guzma.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Early in the morning, he banged on Johan's door, fully displaying the unyielding spirit of a Fire-type Trainer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gengar, put him back to sleep."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, rubbing his temples and yawning, was already covered in exhaustion lines.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yesterday, helping Urshifu evolve had drained a lot of his Aura energy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since his match was scheduled for the afternoon, he had planned to sleep in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But then this idiot Flint\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar cackled and suddenly popped up in front of Flint.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint's face drained of color. "Wait, no\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
BAM\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He collapsed onto the floor, fast asleep.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Luckily, Gengar knew its limits and only used a standard Hypnosis, not a nightmare.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, Gengar casually tapped the Pok\u233? Ball on Flint's waist.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a flash of red light, Infernape emerged, yawning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It looked at Gengar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then at Flint's unconscious body.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And instantly understood.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Without hesitation, Infernape picked up Flint, yawned again, waved at Gengar, and carried him back to his room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The whole sequence was so smooth and practiced that it was heartbreaking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all that noise, Johan was fully awake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His Gallade and the others had already left for work, so he could only make himself a cup of coffee, grab a chair, and sit in the courtyard reading.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lately, he had been focused on reading "The Secrets of the Earth", occasionally imparting some knowledge to Larvitar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, among his Pok\u233?mon, the only Ground-type move they really used was Dig.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8230?Well, not exactly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was one Pok\u233?mon that knew Ground-type moves\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Giovanni ever found out that Johan's "Secrets of the Earth" had been studied the most by a Flying-type Pok\u233?mon, he might just show up at his door.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the courtyard, Dragonite and Larvitar\u8212?two Pok\u233?mon with the biggest height difference\u8212?were having a training session.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite raised its foot, about to stomp down, when it noticed Johan watching.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It chuckled awkwardly and gently set its foot down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was Earthquake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar scratched the small horn on its head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, Dragonite raised its foot again and lightly stomped down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was Stomp.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji? (O_O)?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar's tiny head filled with question marks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Was there even a difference?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just pay attention.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite gently patted Larvitar on the head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar chewed on its finger, looked at its tiny feet, and wobbled them a little.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Forget it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was all just stomping anyway.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Oh, right\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had said to "feel the pulse and breath of the earth."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So, Larvitar mimicked Dragonite, slowly raised its foot\u8230? and stomped down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
BOOM!!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A thunderous crash erupted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's head snapped up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The other Pok\u233?mon all turned to look.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And then\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From Larvitar's foot, a thin crack spread outward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The farther it went, the larger the fissure became.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It extended all the way to the house\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
and collapsed an entire section of the building.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "???"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No way.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all the precautions he took against Gengar and the others\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Larvitar who got the first demolition?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Who would have thought that a Pok\u233?mon that just hatched days ago could cause such destruction?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the same time, in Johan's Pok\u233?dex, Larvitar's move list updated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A new move appeared\u8212?High Horsepower!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
??\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now Johan was completely confused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had been watching Dragonite teach Larvitar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had even warned Dragonite not to destroy anything.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Dragonite only knew Earthquake and Stomp.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So how did Larvitar learn High Horsepower?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar flashed a cute smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's frustration melted away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
How was he supposed to be mad at that?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At least\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's a player village house."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe the Sinnoh League would cover the damage?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan snapped out of his thoughts just in time to see Larvitar happily running toward the collapsed house.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What are you doing?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Don't waste it, duh!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That afternoon, the sky was slightly overcast.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since he had nowhere to go, Johan spent the morning lounging at Cynthia's place.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to the news, Tobias had already made it to the finals\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
with zero suspense.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His opponent had been lucky just to make it to the semifinals.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Their bragging rights would probably be more valuable than an actual championship.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8230?Though, of course, not as valuable as Guderian's runner-up title from the Indigo Conference.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now, the second semifinal match was about to begin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The massive main stadium was packed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even outside, the square was overflowing with people watching the giant screen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The cheers never stopped\u8212?and Johan was by far the crowd favorite.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan's popularity keeps growing\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Lucian couldn't help but comment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Among their entire group, only Cynthia might be able to compete with that level of fame.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Only one spot in the finals remains. Who will claim it? Let's find out!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The host's voice echoed throughout the stadium.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan and Guzma walked onto the field.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The two were stark contrasts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan yawned loudly, adjusted his glasses, and looked half-asleep.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma, hands shoved into his pockets, walked with a slouch.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His messy white hair and skull-patterned clothes made him look as delinquent as ever.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Guzma saw Johan's sleepy look, he frowned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Was this a provocation?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled at every other opponent, but against him, he was constantly yawning?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Did he think Guzma wasn't even a threat?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As soon as they reached their positions, Guzma spoke first.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So you're Johan, huh?" He gave a disdainful glare.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmm? Mm."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan yawned again and mentally cursed Flint one more time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Their "grudge" was only getting deeper.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma's face darkened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He scoffed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So you're the 'teacher' Kukui keeps praising? I'm going to crush you today."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma's history with Kukui was\u8230? complicated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To put it simply\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was the classic shonen protagonist vs. edgy rival dynamic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If you wanted a reference, Naruto and Sasuke wouldn't be too far off.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, okay." Johan nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His forehead twitched.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan yawned again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Finally, as the referee stepped forward, Johan pushed up his glasses and looked at Guzma.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His tone was calm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So\u8230? Guzma, right?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yeah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You won't even call me 'Teacher'?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now this\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was personal.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230??"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before Guzma could respond, the referee cleared his throat and raised his flag.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Both trainers, send out your Pok\u233?mon!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan tossed his Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're up, Dragonite."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A beam of red light shot out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A chubby orange figure flapped its tiny wings, stretched its neck, and let out a deep roar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~! (\u714?\u715?)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It looked harmless.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But everyone knew\u8212?this was a pseudo-legendary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma smirked when he saw Dragonite.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Going all out from the start, huh? Fine by me."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He grabbed a Pok\u233? Ball and tossed it forward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rain Moth, let's put it in its place."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a flash of red light, Masquerain appeared on the battlefield.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It had two pairs of wings, but what stood out were the large, eye-patterned antennae, giving it the eerie appearance of a floating face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Masquerain, the Eyeball Pok\u233?mon. A Bug/Flying-type that uses the eye patterns on its feelers to intimidate foes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The longer you stare at it, the creepier it gets.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Intimidate Ability, activated!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was the only Bug-type Pok\u233?mon with the Intimidate Ability.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
One of the "Big Three" intimidators in competitive battles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite flinched slightly, caught off guard by Masquerain's unsettling gaze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Had the battle already started, it might have had time to counter the effect.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the pre-battle activation meant it lost one stage of Attack.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was also why Guzma smirked in satisfaction.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had clearly expected him to lead with Golisopod, the Pok\u233?mon he usually used to overwhelm opponents.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Instead, he threw out Masquerain first\u8212?a Pok\u233?mon he hadn't used in the tournament before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's pre-match strategy had been disrupted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And Guzma loved catching opponents off guard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Battle, begin!" The referee dropped his flag.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The entire stadium fell silent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma wore his usual cocky grin and stayed quiet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was confident in his ability to read opponents, so he wanted Johan to move first.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Against Lana's Primarina back in {\i
Sun & Moon}, he had used this same strategy, forcing opponents to attack first while he countered with devastating precision.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But against Johan\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled slightly and said, "Dragon Dance."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma's smirk froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Crap.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had just handed Johan a free setup.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite flapped its wings, power surging through its body.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its Attack and Speed both increased!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He realized something very stupid.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trying psychological warfare against a trained psychologist was\u8230? not the smartest move.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Masquerain, U-turn!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From the very first move of the battle, Guzma had already decided to switch out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This caught the audience off guard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait, the battle just started, and he's already U-turning?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite, despite its round, chubby body, was remarkably agile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It smoothly dodged Masquerain's attack as the Bug-type retreated into its Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan rubbed his face to wake up a little.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was close.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He nearly fell behind right away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Guzma hadn't overthought things, this opening would have been a lot rougher.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or, as Gengar would put it\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're actually kind of nice, huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guzma: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
----------\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
