{\qc
474: Mt. Pyre and the Rare Candy\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hoenn, Slateport City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was early spring, and the southern city of Slateport was renowned for its flowers and ocean.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The deep blue sky was dotted with drifting clouds. A flock of Taillow soared overhead, leaving fleeting trails in their wake. Swarms of Beautifly fluttered among the flowerbeds, drinking nectar. A Rhyhorn lay beneath the morning sun, dozing amidst the dewdrops and floral scents.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The golden sunlight bathed the scene. A Beautifly gently flapped its wings and perched atop Rhyhorn's rugged horn.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A small group of people walked along a narrow path through the flower fields, their presence barely disturbing the sleeping Rhyhorn or the resting Beautifly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The weather is quite nice today."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, dressed in his signature suit, adjusted his monocle with a pleasant smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be honest\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
