{\qc
482: Solar Beam? No, Solar Blade!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A sailboat cruised across the endless ocean. Compared to the vast sea, the once seemingly large vessel now appeared rather small.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sat on the deck at the bow, a sunshade umbrella propped up as he fished.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Baby Lugia and Larvitar had tired themselves out from playing and were now napping beside his chair, basking in the warm sun, completely at ease.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Especially Baby Lugia\u8212?after growing close to Johan, it had completely forgotten that it had been "kidnapped." With Larvitar keeping it company, it hadn't thought about Lugia at all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Splash\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Water splattered as Cynthia lifted her fishing rod, reeling in a Remoraid that flailed, splashing droplets into the bucket beside her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing this, Johan glanced at his own bucket on the other side\u8212?completely empty except for seawater. His eye twitched.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That didn't make sense.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Stop looking. You haven't caught a single one."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Across from Cynthia, Caitlin smirked in amusement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You say that like you've caught a ton."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cynthia has three, I have one, even Gengar caught two. What about you?" Caitlin shot him a sidelong glance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar grinned, licking its tongue\u8212?it had never been this successful at fishing before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All thanks to Johan "helping" by doing worse.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"My bait must be expired."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Huh?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As soon as he said it, Johan froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Why did that sound familiar?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia stretched lazily, her black trench coat draped over her chair. Now, in just a sleeveless top, her slender figure was elegantly outlined as she stood up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan snapped his head around.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to "how this scene plays out," wasn't he supposed to get hit in the back of the head by a rock right about now?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmm?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just as she walked behind him, Cynthia was startled by his sudden movement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"N-Nothing." Johan coughed into his fist.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He wasn't trying to play some double-role narrative\u8212?he was just overthinking things.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Where are you going?" he quickly changed the subject.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's too hot. I'm going to change." Cynthia casually tucked her hair behind her ear.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait for me, Cynthia! I'm coming too!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing this, Caitlin immediately dropped her fishing rod and ran after her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Change\u8230? clothes?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sunlight, the ocean, fishing\u8230? put those together\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A certain image flashed through Johan's mind.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, he felt a slight warmth in his nose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cough.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar seemed to have caught on to something, sidling up with a wicked grin, fishing rod in hand, raising its eyebrows at Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"W-What?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan snapped out of it. "Watch this\u8212?today I'm catching a big one. I'll make fish head soup for lunch!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~ (\u1076?.)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar looked doubtful, leaning in so close its cool purple face almost touched Johan's.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji\u8230? (\u949?`)" Larvitar smacked its lips.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hehe, fish head soup!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Bwooo\u8230? (\u949?`)" Baby Lugia murmured.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As long as it's not roast pigeon, it's fine.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Keep staring, and you're not getting any!" Johan growled at Gengar, feeling a bit guilty.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar immediately raised its hands in surrender.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But its teasing gaze made it clear\u8212?it had seen right through him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Huh?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan felt a heavy tug on his rod. His eyes lit up. Finally, a bite!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a sharp pull, he reeled it in. The translucent fishing line sparkled in the sunlight as a bright orange Magikarp arced through the air.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It flopped onto the deck, staring blankly while thrashing about.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar pointed at the dull-eyed Magikarp and burst out laughing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's so funny?!" Johan gritted his teeth. "Fish head soup needs Magikarp!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar suddenly gasped, jerking its own fishing rod\u8212?it had a bite too!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And then\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two Magikarp flopped side by side on the deck, flapping in unison as if slapping Johan and Gengar across the face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan & Gengar: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Another Magikarp swarm?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wait, why did he think {\i
another}?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not that it matters\u8212?they're all inedible anyway."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Whether it was Magikarp or Cynthia's Remoraid, they couldn't be eaten. He was aiming for normal sea fish.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Keep going\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cha~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under the watchful eyes of Cynthia and Caitlin's Pok\u233?mon, Ceruledge twisted the dial on its chest\u8212?transforming into Armarouge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garrr?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lu-ka?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Garchomp and Lucario tilted their heads, question marks forming above them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What's going on?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cha~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Armarouge's focus was entirely on Roserade.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Roserade raised its rose-like hands, gathering tiny motes of light under the sunlight. The glowing particles coalesced into a shimmering sphere.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, with both flowers aimed at the sea\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Buzz\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A brilliant white beam shot forward, slicing through the distance in an instant. The surface of the ocean erupted in a spectacular burst, spraying rainbow-colored mist into the air.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Solar Beam!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Every movement had been slow and deliberate, as if demonstrating each step for Armarouge to observe.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cha\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Armarouge's eyes glowed with understanding.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clack!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its armored arms locked together, forming a golden cannon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garrr\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Garchomp and Lucario's eyes gleamed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even they had to admit\u8212?that looked cool.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Buzz\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sunlight streamed down, gathering into the cannon's barrel, forming a searing golden sphere.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As soon as enough energy had built up, it scattered before taking shape.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A failure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But this was Armarouge's first attempt at Solar Beam. Given the complexity of the move and the fact that it wasn't a Grass-type, failing on the first try was expected.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yet Armarouge seemed to have realized something.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It twisted its chest dial again\u8212?transforming back into Ceruledge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lu-ka\u8230?" Lucario murmured.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That transformation\u8230? didn't add up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clang!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ceruledge crossed its twin blades over its chest. Tiny golden sparks of sunlight gathered once more.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This time, instead of forming a light sphere, the energy fused into its twin swords.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Instead of dispersing, the golden glow became more solid.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clang!!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The two blades gleamed, transformed into twin golden swords.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Solar Blade!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Huh?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, watching from afar, had a strange expression.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was supposed to be Solar Beam\u8212?how did it turn into Solar Blade?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Was this\u8230? {\i
creative learning}?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Well, in a way.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For both Ceruledge and Armarouge, Solar Beam wasn't something they could naturally learn.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They could only acquire it through TMs or special training.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Solar Blade was different\u8212?it was a move Ceruledge could already learn.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All it had lacked was the right opportunity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since it had now figured out how to gather solar energy, it instinctively used Solar Blade instead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lu-ka!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucario gestured for a spar. With a focused breath, it extended a glowing blue Bone Rush staff.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ceruledge didn't hesitate. It already knew Lucario's strength well.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It charged forward, twin golden blades flashing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clang! Clang\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Golden swords clashed with the blue staff, sparks flying with each impact.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a final collision, the two Pok\u233?mon retreated simultaneously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucario nodded in approval, dismissing its weapon while shaking its hands\u8212?not bad.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For a first attempt, Ceruledge had done well.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, Ceruledge stood still, deep in thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was analyzing its own technique, refining every movement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't wreck the deck," Johan, who had now caught seven Magikarp, reminded them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garrr\u8212?!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Garchomp growled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
You dare tell me how to fight?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan just sighed\u8212?he was used to Garchomp's attitude by now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the side, Cynthia\u8212?now in a light blue short-sleeved shirt\u8212?sat gracefully, fishing with a small smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clearly, despite the sun, sea, and fishing, neither she nor Caitlin had changed into swimsuits this early in the season.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Commander Johan, a group of Pok\u233?mon is approaching." In the captain's cabin, the handsome guy spotted something unusual on the radar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wild Pok\u233?mon?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan squinted toward the horizon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That is\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar reacted first, leaning over the railing in a classic "Monkey King lookout" pose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A swarm of Frillish!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Frillish?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They're Frillish, Roto!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom activated its zoom function, focusing on the misty, cloud-like cluster of Pok\u233?mon drifting toward them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Frillish, the Floating Pok\u233?mon. Water/Ghost type. Males are blue, females are pink. They are drawn to life energy and are known for attacking cruise ships, Roto!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"An irregular formation\u8230? Looks like they're coming for you, Gengar."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah! \u931?(\u1076?lll)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I may not be smart, but don't try to fool me!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blue and pink bodies bobbed as they pulsed through the water, their eerie red eyes fixated on the ship, drawing closer with each undulating motion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Veteran sailors often said that encountering Gyarados or Sharpedo at sea wasn't as terrifying as running into a school of Frillish. These ghostly creatures could silently sap the strength from both people and Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be fair, their round, floating bodies, glowing red eyes, and Ghost-type aura {\i
did} bear a resemblance to Gengar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No wonder Gengar almost believed it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, watching Gengar's "panic," smirked slightly, neither confirming nor denying anything. Instead, he tapped his chin thoughtfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Life energy\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Many Ghost-type Pok\u233?mon were drawn to life energy, like Chandelure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There were even old rumors claiming that Chandelure could quietly drain a Trainer's life force.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had encountered many Chandelure owners before, but he had never seen anything to suggest they were secretly energy vampires.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, life energy was a mysterious force in the Pok\u233?mon world.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright, we've got work to do, little ones."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though there were many Frillish, they weren't enough to pose a serious threat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garrr~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roar~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before Johan could give the order, Dragonite and Garchomp had already charged forward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dragonite, Garchomp\u8212?Dragon Rush!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garrr!! (\u9660?\u30399?\u9660?)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Don't order me around!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Despite its grumble, Garchomp still cloaked itself in draconic energy, lunging forward alongside Dragonite.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The battle had begun.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
