485: Temple of the Sea, Samiya!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The moon was bright and stars sparse, the rolling waves of the ocean settling into stillness.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A single sailboat glided across the calm sea, as if following the moon's silver path reflected on the water.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're not resting?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the cockpit, Johan leaned against the doorframe, watching the handsome man at the helm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You all slept when we landed on Slowking Island." The man grinned, looking energetic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While Johan and the others explored, he'd taken stock of the cabin and snuck in a nap himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing his good condition, Johan smiled and said no more.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Their current location, marked on both their sea chart and the Rotom navigator, was closing in on one of the moving coordinates.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That coordinate had suddenly accelerated during dinner\u8212?not quite Lugia-speed, but definitely faster than an ordinary Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So it had to be Lugia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Probably.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They might even encounter it by midnight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But since they didn't know Lugia's state or intentions\u8212?if it would be hostile\u8212?Johan had Cynthia and Caitlin rest to conserve energy while he kept watch.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Relying on the man alone in a crisis would be a disaster. He'd probably only react once the boat was flipped and everyone was swimming.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan crouched down and beckoned to the Croagunk wearing a captain's hat, who stood stiffly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ku."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Croagunk hesitated briefly, glanced at the man, then trotted to Johan and took an energy cube from his hand, tossing it into its mouth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing it sneak glances at the man, Johan chuckled. Clearly, Croagunk cared a lot about how the man felt.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He patted Croagunk's shoulder, his eyes gleaming with aura.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Croagunk, let me teach you something."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ku?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If you ever sense real danger, don't listen to that guy. Poison Jab him into unconsciousness and carry him off."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan grinned, picturing Brock's Croagunk dragging him away by the leg after knocking him out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ku?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Croagunk looked even more confused, but there was a hint of curiosity in its eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You know how reckless he is. If he gets himself into danger, don't follow his orders."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sure, that might lead to mission failure\u8212?but the man never followed protocol anyway.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"As a Superintendent Inspector of the International Police, I hereby secretly appoint you as 'Chief Patrol Officer.' That makes you his superior. He has to listen to you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Chief Patrol Officer?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Croagunk's eyes lit up. It straightened its back, shot a sideways glance at the man, and got a puzzled look in return.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Only for extreme situations, okay?" Johan added.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ku!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Croagunk nodded solemnly. Protecting the man had always been its mission.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It just never had a legitimate reason\u8212?until now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now it was in charge!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled and gave it another handful of energy cubes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Protecting the man meant protecting Croagunk too. He didn't want to revisit a future where all that remained was Croagunk's photo in mourning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From Johan's shadow, Gengar peeked out, puzzled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Was Johan... mimicking his sneaky ways?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Johan, sir!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, the man's voice rang out, tense.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The coordinate changed direction! And its speed\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan looked at Rotom and saw that the coordinate previously headed toward them had turned, moving in a completely different pattern.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What's going on?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thinking fast, Johan made a decision. "Catch up to it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The turn wasn't a retreat\u8212?there was still a chance to close in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Got it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The man had the same idea. He cranked the sailboat's turbines to max. The boat jolted with a burst of speed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tyrunt and the baby Lugia rolled from foot to headboard in their sleep, but just snuggled closer together without waking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In their rooms, Ninetales, Urshifu, and Ceruledge opened their eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In Cynthia and Caitlin's room, Garchomp and Lucario also stirred, but upon confirming the girls were still asleep, made no sound.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rotom, help out," Johan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roto~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom crackled with electricity and dove into the boat's turbine, supercharging it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With extra power from Magnezone and two Chinchou, the boat accelerated again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The man pressed a button, and Croagunk ran to the deck to help furl the sails.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moonlight shimmered on the water as waves rippled beneath them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a while\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"According to this direction\u8230?" the man said in surprise, "That coordinate is moving toward another one!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan noticed too\u8212?both coordinates were converging. What's happening?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
First it came toward them, now it veered to another spot?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And now they were getting close to both?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Captain, someone's chasing us!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In a massive submarine, a Ghost Pirate Crew member spotted blips on radar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The burly man in command narrowed his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eliminate them!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two mini-subs launched from the main sub, spiraling toward the sailboat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From the subs, six Sharpedo, four Crawdaunt, two Cloyster, and a swarm of Remoraid swam out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar perched atop the mast, scanning the sea with glowing red eyes, and cried out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Submarines!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The radar in the cockpit lit up with the two mini-subs and their Pok\u233?mon swarm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan narrowed his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So... we guessed wrong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That coordinate wasn't Lugia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was... likely Manaphy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or rather, Manaphy's egg.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It floated with the current.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blame Slowking for being vague\u8212?the two coordinates it gave included Manaphy too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The stationary one had to be Lugia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which hadn't moved. Why?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The pirates' target was the Temple of the Sea\u8212?likely aiming for Manaphy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But then how did the man rescue the baby Lugia?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Did they catch it first? Was it a side goal?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Too many questions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Some clues were new, some were half-remembered from a movie Johan had once seen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But nothing quite fit together yet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, one thing was clear:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The enemy made the first move.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which meant\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Time to strike first!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Pok\u233?mon hunters either way\u8212?they were going down!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan strode onto the deck.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The boat rocked as waves churned from water-type attacks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Johan stood firm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His aura training, combined with martial arts lessons from Bruno, kept him steady.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowoo~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ninetales appeared beside him, sensing the urgency.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan patted its snowy white fur.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Without words, it raised its head and howled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowoo\u8212?!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Snow began to fall, temperature plummeting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dragonite, Urshifu!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garruu~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The attackers were underwater\u8212?targeting the boat's hull.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only Dragonite and Urshifu had real underwater combat capability.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Splash\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite dove in. Urshifu took a deep breath and followed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar, now in goggles, volunteered for underwater duty.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled and waved it on.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Air, land, sea... underwater's where we're weakest," Johan mused, closing his eyes and using aura.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The underwater scene painted itself in his mind like sonar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The sea churned violently. Dozens of water-types used Whirlpool.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Any normal boat would've been shredded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the whirlpool began to slow\u8230? and freeze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thanks, Ninetales!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even if Johan's team lacked true sea fighters, they could still control the ocean.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite wasn't fast underwater, but far faster than the enemy Sharpedo and Crawdaunt.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And the Remoraid? No chance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Bwooooom\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Golden lightning exploded from Dragonite's body.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thunderbolt!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only Dragonite\u8212?with its uncanny luck\u8212?would dare use Thunderbolt underwater.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Remoraid floated to the surface, stunned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, Urshifu dove deeper.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even ten meters out, it struck a pose, fists moving.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Water slowed most Fighting-types\u8212?not Urshifu.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With its Water typing and mastery of flowing strikes, it felt right at home.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It punched.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Splash\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Water became its weapon, flowing, compounding. It surged toward the Sharpedo.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Boom!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two Sharpedo went down immediately.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And that was just the start.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A whiplike leg strike sliced the water like a blade.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then a sweeping punch sent layered waves crashing forward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Didn't expect Urshifu to be this good underwater," Johan admitted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even the pirates were stunned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This... this strong?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fall back! Report to the captain!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But before they could move\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
One looked to his side and screamed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar had already appeared beside him, arm draped around his shoulder.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before he could react\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hypnosis.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When he opened his eyes again, he was on a sunny beach.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Vacation?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He sighed in bliss and lay back.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only for Gengar to reappear beside him, grinning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The sea calmed again, as if nothing had happened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only the fast-sailing boat remained.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan stood at the bow, sea breeze cooling his face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~ Ka-kaah~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar sat nearby, reciting intel it gathered:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Manaphy, Lugia, ghost pirates, Pok\u233?mon Hunter J.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Piece by piece, the picture became clearer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lugia was J's target.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Manaphy was the ghost pirates'.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They were working together!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The approaching coordinate had been Manaphy's egg.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The stationary one\u8212?Lugia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And its silence? Possibly caused by the petrification gun\u8212?J's signature weapon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It could even petrify the lake guardians.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If they hit Lugia with it... that explained everything.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In any case, they had to catch up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The egg was still showing up on Rotom's map.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now was the best time to strike the pirates.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan could almost hear it\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Want the treasure? I hid it all in the sub. If you want it, come find it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two major Pok\u233?mon hunter crews...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's up?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia, now in a windcoat, and Caitlin, yawning, joined him on deck.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Battle sounds woke us up," Caitlin muttered, frowning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Interrupting sleep... how rude!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her hair lifted as her psychic aura stirred.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan quickly explained.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Both understood.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar pointed to the sea ahead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Beneath the surface, among swirling fish, a grand, ancient structure shimmered within a glowing barrier.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A powerful aura of history washed over them. Cynthia's eyes sparkled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Temple of the Sea\u8212?Samiya," Johan answered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The coordinates overlapped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lugia... seemed to be inside.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gaaaaarrrrgh!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A pained cry echoed from the depths.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Inside the cabin, baby Lugia trembled, suddenly waking, tears in its eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Bwooo..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A massive shadow flickered past the glowing temple deep below.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
