{\qc
502: The Incident Brought by Porygon-Z\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rustboro City, Caf\u233?.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was Johan's first time seeing such a complicated expression on Gengar's face\u8212?confused, bashful, nervous, and shy all at once.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He couldn't help but laugh.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Who could relate to this painless fatherhood? Only fellow Pok\u233?-dads could understand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the same time, Porygon-Z was sitting on the table, happily munching on Pok\u233?blocks like it had never eaten anything before\u8212?utterly amazed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Could it be that Porygon-Z didn't need to eat?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's thoughts stirred.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Was this his destined Pok\u233?mon?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Porygon-Z clarified that it wasn't that it didn't eat\u8212?in the lab, it had its own nutrient fluid, similar to the treatment given to Mewtwo.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That made sense to Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rocket's nutrient formula wasn't ordinary stuff\u8212?it could even nourish a legendary Pok\u233?mon like Mewtwo.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, Gengar was standing beside the table with a tray of Pok\u233?blocks, looking like a nervous waiter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Those Pok\u233?blocks? Gengar's personal stash.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Pure Pok\u233?-dad vibes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And the others weren't missing the fun\u8212?his Pok\u233?mon all sat around, munching on seeds, enjoying the show.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just then, Johan's phone rang again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This time, it was a call\u8212?not a message.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And the caller? None other than the head of Team Rocket, Gym Leader of Viridian City in Kanto\u8212?Giovanni!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Leader Giovanni," Johan answered, having fully expected this call.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Advisor Johan."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni's calm and magnetic voice came through the phone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"He's with me," Johan said, smiling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He knew exactly why Giovanni was calling\u8212?of course, it was about Porygon-Z.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was likely the first Porygon-Z in the Pok\u233?mon world, and in terms of practical application, it could rival an entire IT company.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I know."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And Giovanni wouldn't be calling unless he was certain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They understood each other.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"There's something else," Giovanni added.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni didn't bother being subtle. "Your method for evolving Porygon into Porygon2 and Porygon-Z."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Evolving into Porygon2 was already valuable, but the leap to Porygon-Z had Rocket's researchers witnessing true artificial intelligence.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rocket had dozens of Porygon. Naturally, Giovanni wanted them all upgraded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With that, they'd surpass even the League in cyber power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I've got a rough idea for evolving to Porygon2, but as for Porygon-Z\u8230? that was more of a coincidence," Johan admitted honestly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It had involved Deoxys' space virus, which wasn't exactly something you could replicate on demand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not to mention Mewtwo's psychic power played a role.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I see."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni's tone didn't change much, but he nodded slightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If there's a chance, help evolve some Porygon into Porygon2."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He paused, then added with a chuckle, "I'll pay per unit."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No problem!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had expected Giovanni to try and buy the method outright\u8212?but instead, he chose the long-term, profit-sharing route.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In truth, Johan had already begun theorizing other ways to evolve Porygon into Porygon-Z. Maybe Deoxys wasn't strictly necessary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"One more thing."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni said, "When Porygon-Z left, it left a backdoor in the network\u8212?some Porygon followed and escaped."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Huh?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan was startled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Porygon escaped into the internet?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was going to be tough to get them back.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan still didn't know whether the League even had any Porygon. If they didn't, how were they countering Rocket?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Either way\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
By now, the League probably had at least one.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And once they had one, breeding more would be easy given their current capabilities.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So... writing a thesis on Porygon was starting to look worthwhile?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Would that offend Giovanni though?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He still pretended not to know Giovanni's true identity, and if Rocket was planning a rebrand, there was no reason to panic. Everyone's cybersecurity would just become equally impenetrable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Otherwise, Giovanni wouldn't be speaking so calmly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I have something to bring up too," Johan suddenly said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Go on."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I wonder\u8230? do you know about Dark Balls?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Back at Rocket HQ, Giovanni raised an eyebrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Marauder?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hadn't they both agreed not to dig too deeply into that matter?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Giovanni didn't answer, Johan continued.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A while ago\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He chose his words carefully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230?during the capture of Hunter J, she had a Dark Ball in her possession."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni might not know about the incident with the Temple of the Sea and Lugia, but he'd definitely heard of Hunter J's arrest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan figured it was worth mentioning since Giovanni had already called.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni was silent for a while, then finally asked:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Marauder?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"As far as I know\u8230? no," Johan replied.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"\u8230??"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giovanni, now leaning forward in his chair, narrowed his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I see."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He didn't question Johan's information. If needed, he had ways to reach Hunter J in prison.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And he didn't press for more\u8212?smart people knew when to stop.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In truth, Giovanni already had a few suspects in mind.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll have Matori transfer the intelligence fee to your account."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a beat, he added:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Do well in the Youth Masters."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And with that, the call ended.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So even Giovanni is watching the Youth Masters\u8230?" Johan muttered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moments later, he received a bank notification\u8212?3,000,000 Pok\u233?dollars deposited!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Big boss Giovanni didn't mess around!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, a call from Matori came through.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Johan, what intel did you give? Even we didn't know about it!" she asked, full of curiosity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Kids shouldn't ask."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm not that\u8212? wait\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, in the League's Information Department:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Someone's attacking our firewall?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The department housed the League's top cybersecurity experts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even major corporations like Devon had their own top talent here.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, in the modern Pok\u233?mon world, data was everything.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, one analyst noticed something.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They hadn't been attacked in ages\u8212?this was exciting!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Until they saw\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is that\u8230? a Pok\u233?mon?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The staffer stared, dumbfounded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A Pok\u233?mon living in cyberspace?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its "attack" wasn't aggressive. More like\u8230? knocking politely?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When did Pok\u233?mon start living in the internet?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then again, with Pok\u233?mon living in space now, maybe this wasn't so strange.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Report\u8212?right, I need to report this!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Because of the League's emphasis on cybersecurity, this department was overseen by none other than Elite Four member Bertha!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Once informed, she summoned the League's top IT experts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Among them? Johan's old acquaintance\u8212?Bill.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bill, a Pok\u233?mon researcher and tech genius, was quickly informed and spread the word among his peers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, after getting its fill, Porygon-Z didn't linger long. It returned to Rocket HQ.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though it was reluctant to part from Gengar, as Mewtwo's mouthpiece, it had to go.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But before leaving, it handed Rotom the coordinates of the Pok\u233?mon needing help\u8212?and even helped track down the escaped Porygon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It seemed to care deeply about them, maybe even saw them as kin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Truth was, Porygon didn't have self-awareness. They simply followed instructions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Porygon-Z hadn't guided them out, they wouldn't have moved at all\u8212?even if the firewall was open.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So rather than escaping, they were {\i
freed}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And by giving their locations to Johan, Porygon-Z was asking him to help.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just like he helped others.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not that Rocket treated them poorly\u8212?but Porygon-Z's data analysis suggested: don't put all your eggs in one basket.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Porygon line would only thrive if spread out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan agreed to help.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The more Porygon there were, the more valuable his research into their evolution would become.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Also, another reason:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now that Rocket had a Porygon-Z, if they hadn't reformed, the League would've been unable to resist their cyber capabilities.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A stable Pok\u233?mon world was a better Pok\u233?mon world.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To maintain that stability, both sides needed the tech.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm the ultimate fence-sitter, aren't I?" Johan chuckled to himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Later that night, he spotted forum threads popping up on a researcher site\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The League was already buzzing about Porygon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They're fast\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
