504: Testing Cadres with a "Champion"?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unova Region, Opelucid City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As one of the major cities in the Unova region, Opelucid had a distinct charm of its own.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The entire city was split down the middle by the location of the Opelucid Gym, dividing it into two completely different styles: modern on the west side and classical on the east.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The western part of the city had asphalt roads, gridded blue lights on the ground, and blue light-trimmed eaves on buildings, all with a futuristic, sci-fi aesthetic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In contrast, the eastern side had more greenery, stone-paved streets with uneven levels, and stone reliefs decorating the walls\u8212?a more traditional, classical atmosphere.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This contrast was a hallmark of Opelucid City, representing the residents' different attitudes toward life.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
People in the west preferred innovation, while those in the east favored the depth of tradition.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though it appeared to be a divided city, the residents embraced the duality with open arms.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't that classical enthusiasts couldn't accept modernity, or vice versa. They just had different lifestyles\u8212?and mutual respect for each other's choices.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
