He explained: the academy was stifling her spirit. She wasn't thriving there. Her growth was being suppressed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was the classic clash between academic and experiential learning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Academia prized knowledge and tactics.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Field trainers valued bonds and instincts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iris clearly fit the latter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Still," Johan said, "isn't pushing her out like this going to hurt her?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Might she feel like a failure? Like she was being rejected?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was exactly the emotional weight Iris carried when she returned years later with Ash.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But that could become her motivation," Drayden insisted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
To prove everyone wrong\u8230?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clich\u233? revenge plot vibes?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan bit his tongue.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"She's just a kid. What if she can't handle it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drayden fell silent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Eventually, he muttered, "I believe in her."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He trusted her potential.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Johan had a different philosophy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If someone was better suited to another path, just tell them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Encourage them. Support them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Why choose painful rejection over uplifting guidance?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He always tailored training to his Pok\u233?mon's personalities and strengths\u8212?even letting Gengar punch things instead of using special attacks, because Gengar liked it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe not optimal\u8212?but it made Gengar happy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drayden and Johan had clearly different teaching ideologies.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which suited Opelucid's dual-natured identity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To his credit, Drayden wasn't rigid. He saw Johan's point.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"How about that lesson?" he asked again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This wasn't a challenge\u8212?it was an opportunity to compare philosophies.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan adjusted his glasses. "Alright."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
How would they compare?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Simple:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
A battle.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nothing showed philosophy more clearly than a Pok\u233?mon battle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And for a Pok\u233?mon academy?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was no better way to teach than by showing them a real match.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was their unspoken agreement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Back in the car, Alder woke up and blinked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan vs. Drayden?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Now {\i
that} got him excited.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's go! I gotta see this!" he shouted, startling Officer Jenny.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But truthfully?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She was intrigued too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drayden wasn't just any Gym Leader.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
