508: The Awakening of Truth and Ideals\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unova Region, Opelucid City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In a narrow alley outside the Opelucid Gym.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Staring up at the twin dragon heads atop the gym, N lowered the brim of his cap, his eyes gleaming beneath its shadow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had followed someone all the way here, but stopped outside, captivated by the statues above the building.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The twin dragons of truth and ideals from the 'Founding Legend'..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Skritch, skritch...}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A faint rustling sound caught his attention. He turned toward the noise and spotted a scrawny Rattata clawing its way out from the corner of the wall.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its trembling limbs and malnourished body revealed just how rough life had been for the little wanderer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
N knelt down gently, picking it up and offering bits of cake he had packed earlier from a caf\u233?.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The little Rattata, sensing N's kindness, looked up as if to memorize the face of this gentle, handsome human, while devouring the food with desperate gratitude.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was the best thing it had ever tasted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But at that moment, shadows stirred at the end of the alley. Three figures appeared suddenly and silently flanked N in a triangular formation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
N wasn't surprised. He recognized them instantly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They were the Dark Triad of Team Plasma\u8212?silent, white-haired men with ghastly metal masks\u8212?servants of his foster father, Ghetsis. They obeyed only Ghetsis and N himself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Their presence meant Ghetsis already knew N had returned to Opelucid.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, N calmly continued feeding the Rattata. Only after ensuring the little one had eaten its fill did he gently set it down and slowly stand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Dark Triad remained silent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, black mist engulfed them all. In an instant\u8212?just like a teleport\u8212?they vanished from the alley, leaving the bewildered Rattata alone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Inside Opelucid Gym.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is the Legend Badge, and a TM for the move 'Wide Slash'."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drayden handed the items to Johan without hesitation, having accepted his defeat and gained new clarity about Johan's strength.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The badge didn't mean much to Johan, now that his Trainer level was Master\u8212?he couldn't participate in Unova's League Conference anymore, even with eight badges.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the move {\i
Wide Slash}, a Dragon-type technique that damages enemies and lowers their Attack, was quite valuable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
During the battle earlier, had Dragonite not made Haxorus flinch with Air Slash, Drayden might not have had to use Outrage to counter, and the match might've gone on longer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar moved faster than Johan, happily snatching up the items and admiring the Legend Badge. It looked pretty good\u8212?better than most badges Johan had collected, actually.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drayden raised an eyebrow at Gengar's confident movements.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thank you, Mr. Drayden," Johan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drayden shook his head slightly. "No, I should be thanking you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not only had Johan delivered an important item, but he'd also taught a public battle class to the Opelucid Academy students\u8212?a clash of ideals and techniques that ultimately had a shared goal: the students' growth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Can I trouble you one more time?" Drayden asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan paused, adjusted his monocle, then smiled. "Is it about Iris?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drayden nodded, sighing lightly. "Feels like... you might understand her better than I do."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even after just one meeting...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a moment's thought, Johan nodded. "Sure."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As Johan left, Drayden crossed his arms again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He's someone who perfectly blends the strengths of the academy and the journeying trainer...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drayden glanced at Alder, now surrounded by enthusiastic students.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What are you waiting for? Keep him here!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Night fell.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The eastern part of Opelucid City stood tall and modern, streets carving the landscape into tidy squares.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The western half was tranquil\u8212?low, quaint buildings, gardens everywhere. A peaceful harbor in everyone's hearts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iris sat in a noodle shop, staring into her bowl, eyes slowly losing focus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, someone sat across from her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Three bowls of seafood udon, please," said the man.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Coming right up!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iris blinked and looked up. Her eyes widened in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Johan?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This place looked promising." Johan smiled as he prepared his chopsticks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar wrung its hands, tongue out, clearly eager to eat. Larvitar kicked its tiny legs on the seat, waving at the Mr. Mime preparing the noodles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Y-yeah..." Iris managed a smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She admired Johan deeply\u8212?he had just defeated her invincible Grandpa Drayden\u8212?and yet, her mood was complicated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No matter who won or lost... she had to leave Opelucid Academy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She loved the freedom\u8212?but not like this.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll take you somewhere after this," Johan said, ignoring her gloomy expression and digging into the steaming udon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Go somewhere?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After eating, they stepped outside.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan summoned Dragonite.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing the massive Dragonite made Iris's eyes sparkle. Her spirits lifted immediately.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan fitted its saddle armor, mounted, then waved her up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Without hesitation, Iris clambered aboard, eager and unafraid.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's Dragonite stood nearly three meters tall\u8212?plenty of room for the small girl.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a beat of its wings, they soared into the air.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wow\u8212?!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iris's shout was filled with pure joy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Johan, is this what it's like to fly on a Dragon-type? This is amazing!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan held his hat with one hand, gripping the harness with the other.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why the armor? This is totally safe!" Iris asked, clinging to Dragonite's neck with ease.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thankfully, their destination wasn't far.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They landed atop Opelucid's tallest structure\u8212?the Radio Tower.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From here, the entire city stretched beneath them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iris had been here once before\u8212?back when Officer Jenny caught her and Drayden scolded her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan stood at the center of the tower, silently berating himself. Why was he showing off like this?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kah!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar cupped his hands and shouted into the city below\u8212?Woohoo! This is wild!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Y-Yoji..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar clung to Johan's leg, face pale. It seemed to have a fear of heights.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Iris?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She mimicked Gengar, hands like a megaphone, and shouted into the city.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"AAAAH!!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her voice echoed\u8212?a cathartic scream.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan exhaled slowly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Iris... where is the Village of Dragons?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"There!" she pointed instantly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I can't see it\u8212?but I can smell it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's how certain she was.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Do you want to go back?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She nodded\u8212?then hesitated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yes... but not like this. Not like I'm being kicked out...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan placed a hand gently on her head. His voice softened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Drayden wants you to return too."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She lowered her head. "I-I know. I just... I didn't do well enough... I couldn't learn properly, I\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan cut her off, walking to the edge of the platform and looking down with a shiver.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dammit, why do I do this to myself?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, he continued.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Drayden and I both believe that Opelucid Academy, while excellent, is limiting you. The best place for you isn't a school\u8212?it's the wild."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iris blinked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She looked up at him, hope dawning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Really?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He nodded. "Absolutely."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To her, his smile was like a warm spring breeze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So... I'm not being abandoned?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But I can't learn things like the others... I'm just different\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Look at the city, Iris," Johan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"City?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"East side is modern, west is classical. Which is better?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I... I don't know."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Which do you prefer?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Classical."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then what about academy learning vs. travel experience?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her eyes widened.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're saying... it's not about which is better\u8212?it's about what fits best?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Smart girl."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Ash had gone to a traditional school, he might still be chasing badges twenty years later\u8212?never competing with Steven or Cynthia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Iris, like Ash, was meant for something different.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's your dream?" he asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"To become a Dragon Master!" Her voice was resolute, her eyes firm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then chase it. You've got what it takes." He ruffled her hair.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No wonder Axew snuck into her hair one day. It's practically a cozy forest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dreams are goals. Reality is the path. If you don't understand your starting point, you'll never reach the dream.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Me too!" Iris grinned wide.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Confidence-wise, she and Ash were equals.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"When you come back, amaze Drayden. Make him proud."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Her eyes sparkled like stars.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yeah!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's how motivation is born\u8212?not from revenge, but from hope.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That night...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A young girl planted the seed of her dream. With effort as its water, and reality as its soil, it would bloom.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Elsewhere in Unova...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A pure white orb glowed faintly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And far away, in the deep night sky, a black beast stirred\u8212?mechanical thunder humming from within.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Truth and Ideals... were awakening.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The next day.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan bid farewell to Drayden, Iris, and Alder. He set out for Lacunosa Town in southern Unova.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Partly to visit Professor Juniper, and partly because of coordinates given by Porygon-Z.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Instead of heading straight south, he traveled east to Village Bridge, planning to sail downstream.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Village Bridge, older than the League, was built over two centuries ago to stop floods\u8212?now a famous battle landmark.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Young Trainers loved to duel near it\u8212?some even chasing long win streaks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan wasn't interested in that.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the scenic waterfalls on Route 11 did make him and his Pok\u233?mon pause to admire the view.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At that moment, his phone rang.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're in Unova?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia's voice came through. And Caitlin's.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You didn't even tell us?! I ought to give you a nice 'welcome'..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The way Caitlin stressed {\i
welcome} made it clear\u8212?this wasn't good news.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was {\i
her} turf.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan ignored her and answered, "Yeah. Just delivering something for the old headmaster. Also got a few errands."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I thought you were headed to Blueberry Academy," Cynthia said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blueberry Academy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A newly founded school built atop an underwater resource development facility, off Unova's coast.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Like Kanaz Academy, it was elite\u8212?and tightly connected with Paldea's Naranja Academy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its rise was rapid.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not only did it host students with Champion potential\u8212?but it also developed a way to control {\b
Tera} mechanics!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
You could Terastallize Pok\u233?mon at Blueberry Academy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This skyrocketed the school's popularity and drew swarms of students.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had heard Martin mention it several times.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its creators were brilliant\u8212?not only mastering Terastal mechanics, but also building four artificial biomes: Grassland, Coastal, Polar, and Canyon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I wouldn't mind checking it out."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The thought intrigued Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Terastallization...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was very curious how they replicated it without Terapagos, the "Crystal Turtle."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe Terastal mechanics would go mainstream someday.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then battles would get... very interesting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Normal-type Champion Lance returning to the spotlight?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
