509: The Island Not Found on Any Map\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji~~" Another boat ride~~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yoji the Larvitar sat on a deck chair, watching the passing scenery on both sides, swinging its little legs.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The tune from "Roaring Dragon, Oowoo~ Little Windmill, Big West Jiji, Aba Aba" popped into Johan's head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He shook his head, trying to purge the earworm from his brain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rotom, where do we go from here?" Johan asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roto!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom-Dex stopped taking photos and pulled up the navigation screen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Calculating optimal route, Roto..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Route lines began flashing across the digital map\u8212?if one didn't work, another replaced it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Turn left after 10 kilometers, Roto!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan frowned at the path on the map. "There's no road there. If we turn left, it's straight into the sea."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes, Roto!" Rotom replied with certainty. "The coordinates are in the sea, Roto."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"In the sea?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There's internet in the sea?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though confused, Johan figured they might as well check it out. If the coordinates were wrong, they could ask Porygon-Z what the deal was.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Once they reached the indicated point, Johan retrieved the Rotom Bike from Gengar's mouth. Rotom entered the bike's system.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To the astonishment of nearby tourists, Johan launched himself off the deck with the bike.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is that guy nuts? He just jumped into the sea!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"On a bike?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Maybe he's had a mental breakdown?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just as some tourists were about to call for help or report to Officer Jenny...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Look!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A sheet of ice spread across the sea surface. Johan's bike rolled smoothly along it, heading east. Gengar floated behind him, while a graceful Ice-type Ninetales glided beside him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You can do that with Ice-types?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's... actually really cool."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I need to catch an Ice-type now!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But it wasn't so simple. Not every Ice-type could freeze the sea fast enough to support a speeding bike, especially for long stretches.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"How long do we have to ride, Rotom?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thirty kilometers, Roto!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Good thing it's a Rotom Bike, or this would be a serious workout.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Turbo boost, Rotom!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roger that, Roto!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Zzzzt\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Electric sparks flared, and the bike shot forward without Johan pedaling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That turbine engine glowed gold... and a thought popped into Johan's mind:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Zekrom, the Dragon of Ideals, also had a turbine. If combined with Rotom...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Would that become the transforming robot Rotom dreamed of?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"R-Roto..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom shuddered as if it sensed an ominous gaze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With the boost engaged, the island came into view ahead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wait a second..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan blinked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That spot on Rotom's updated League map was supposed to be open sea. So why was there an island?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Could it be the League hadn't discovered it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As they neared the lush island, the sea suddenly churned, and aggressive-looking fish Pok\u233?mon surged into view\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bruxish. At least thirty to forty of them!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These were red-striped Bruxish\u8212?brutal, vicious, and territorial. Only tough Pok\u233?mon like Carvanha or Crawdaunt could survive in their waters.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unlike the red and blue-striped ones, white-striped Bruxish\u8212?now nearly extinct\u8212?were gentler and could evolve into Dragalisk. The others could not.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The red-striped ones swarmed toward Johan, enraged by his intrusion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan remained calm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ninetales."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oowoo~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a graceful flourish of her tails, Ninetales released a soft breath of cold air.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In seconds, half the sea froze over. Even the water-dwellers couldn't escape\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Freeze-Dry!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Super-effective against Water-types.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Crack, crack-crack\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But the ice began to splinter. One by one, the Bruxish broke free.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan and Ninetales were both surprised.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ninetales was no joke\u8212?her "Eternal Ice Wall" and Four Heavenly Kings-tier strength made her a terror on the field. No wild Pok\u233?mon should've broken free.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There were only two explanations:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These Bruxish were unusually strong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They had resistance to Ice-type moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
...Or both.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which meant two things:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Either there was some rare resource beneath the island boosting wild Pok\u233?mon levels...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or someone deliberately raised these Bruxish to guard the island.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Given the numbers, the latter seemed more likely.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rotom!" Johan called out. "Discharge!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Zzzzz\u8212?!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lightning burst across the sea, electrocuting the area.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If they weren't in the Bruxish's waters, this would've been considered unethical. But here? No problem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Despite Rotom's dislike of battling, under Johan's tough-love training, powered by top-tier Pok\u233?blocks and a special Raikou Thunderstone...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom was cracked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ninetales, Freeze-Dry again."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With the fish half-cooked, Ninetales froze the sea once more.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This time, the Bruxish couldn't break free.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If they could still jump out, Johan might consider bringing them home for... ahem... study.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar called out from ahead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
More were coming\u8212?a school of blue-striped Bruxish.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This confirmed it: someone had released them here on purpose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Landfall!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan declared, heading toward the island.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Beneath the thick forest lay a hidden facility, mostly underground.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At its deepest point...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A tall, slender researcher in a white lab coat, glasses gleaming, worked intently at a tablet filled with complex data.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was none other than Colress\u8212?the "Mad Scientist" of Team Plasma.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A Pok\u233?mon that can pass data through firewalls into my lab... how fascinating."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He crossed his legs, intrigued by the trace data left behind.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What kind of Pok\u233?mon could move through the network like that?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had to find out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just then, a Team Plasma grunt burst in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lord Colress! Intruder alert!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh?" Colress didn't seem upset\u8212?in fact, he looked excited.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Right after a data breach, and now an intruder?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Coincidence? Not likely.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Out by the island's edge, the Bruxish became aggressive, and our surveillance devices were fried by electricity. It looks like the intruder came prepared!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmm..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Colress stroked his chin, then raised a finger with a sudden idea.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Perfect. Let's test my latest experiment."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The grunt trembled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Y-You mean... use that?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmm?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Colress turned, smiling innocently. "Did you say something?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"N-No, sir! I'll take care of it right away!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Good."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Colress waved him off.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was always so pleasant. Why did everyone fear him?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Perhaps... fear of the unknown?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, one more thing." He added, "Bring the intruder alive. I want to meet him."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If the intruder had a link to that mysterious data-traveling Pok\u233?mon, it was worth investigating.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the grunt rushed off, Colress returned to his tablet, hunting for more digital traces.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had no idea...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That the Pok\u233?mon in question was far beyond his league.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
