Now it was unsure if it could do anything at all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Guilt toward Cobalion and the others\u8230? fear of Kyurem\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The mix of emotions swirled inside it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just as Keldeo started to sink again, Yoji\u8212?the little Larvitar\u8212?tapped its side, as if trying to say something.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What is it?" Keldeo asked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yoji pointed at Keldeo's back, then at himself, rubbing his hands together sheepishly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Can I ride on your back?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Keldeo: "???"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Excuse me, I thought we were friends, and you're trying to\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji~ Yoji~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u127926? Riding on my beloved little donkey~ I'll never be caught in traffic~ \u127926?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And so, Yoji climbed onto Keldeo's back, gripping its fluffy red mane with a contented hum.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Keldeo was dazed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Why had it agreed to that?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A dignified "Sword of Justice," turned into a mount\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Am I really a "Sword of Justice"?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or just a useless burden, always protected by others\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Keldeo realized the reason it agreed\u8212?because, in its eyes, Yoji was the weakest of Johan's Pok\u233?mon. Like itself, Yoji was sheltered, watched over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
