522: Pok\u233?mon Sanctuary\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unova Region, Nimbasa City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After parting ways with the Swords of Justice and Keldeo, Johan arrived in one of Unova's major cities\u8212?Nimbasa City.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Modeled after New York City in America, Nimbasa's architecture was nearly a carbon copy in many places. Especially its central park\u8212?the Pok\u233?mon Sanctuary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This man-made Pok\u233?mon paradise in the heart of a bustling city was lush with vegetation, shaded by green trees, and surrounded by flowing water where Pok\u233?mon frolicked freely.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Johan had to admit, building such a sanctuary amidst a jungle of steel and glass was a real blessing for wild Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was also the very location the Genesects tried to reclaim as their new home in the movie {\i
Genesect and the Legend Awakened}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not just because of the Pok\u233?mon Sanctuary itself, but because in the flowing waters of the park bloomed a lotus-like flower known as {\b
Aurus}\u8212?said to be the oldest flower species on Earth, with origins tracing back some 300 million years.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's why the Genesects chose this spot.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Aurus reminded them of home.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan wasn't sure where the Genesects had gone\u8212?but he figured they might be searching for traces of their ancient homeland, guided by memory.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, after 300 million years of tectonic shifts and time, that home no longer existed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So if they ended up here at the Sanctuary, it wouldn't be surprising.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When Johan arrived, though, he didn't see the Genesects. Nor did he see many people\u8212?since the sanctuary was still under reconstruction. It was currently closed off to the public. Johan was allowed in only due to his status as an international police inspector.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Accompanying him as a volunteer tour guide was Nurse Joy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Mr. Johan, this is the Pok\u233?mon Sanctuary. Construction isn't quite finished, but Pok\u233?mon have already started living here," Nurse Joy said cheerfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If they haven't returned, and there's no trace of them, then odds are they've found another place to build their home."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which\u8212?honestly\u8212?was a good thing for both Johan and the Genesects.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Living far from humans, building a new home, surviving peacefully... what more could anyone ask for?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Come on out."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Standing by a lake at the front of the Sanctuary, Johan called out his team.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
