{\qc
540: Meloetta\u8217?s Gift of Gratitude\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Damn it! You can't even keep track of one person?! Find him\u8212?find him!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Inside Team Plasma's Castle, Ghetsis was in a furious rage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Honestly, this was the first time Team Plasma members had seen him so angry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All because their "King," N, had vanished again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Last time he disappeared, Ghetsis hadn't reacted this strongly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But what they didn't know was that this time, N's disappearance had an entirely different implication for Team Plasma.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They had planned to use N as their scapegoat, and now\u8212?he was gone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was only because Team Plasma had recently gone underground and the "Junior Masters World Championship" was drawing near that they had a little breathing room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But if they couldn't produce someone to take the fall before the championship ended...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then they'd face an even more intense manhunt from the entire Unova League!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes, sir!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Team Plasma members quickly obeyed and dispersed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
None of them doubted they could find their "King."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, to most of the rank-and-file, N was still the true leader of Team Plasma.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You can't hang everything on one tree\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Once they had left, Ghetsis knew he couldn't bet everything on N alone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He needed another way to make the Unova League hesitate\u8212?to make them think twice before striking at Team Plasma with full force.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His gaze turned to Colress.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Colress, immersed in his research, slowly lifted his head, smiling faintly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I happen to have a new research lead."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He turned his tablet toward Ghetsis, revealing digitized ancient texts recovered during the Nacrene Museum raid.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These texts described... the Abyssal Ruins\u8212?and the Reveal Glass!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
An artifact capable of transforming and controlling the Forces of Nature of Unova. It might even aid his research in strengthening and controlling Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Ka-kaah!! (\u9660?\u8895?\u9660?)"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar stood proudly on the beach, donning a Squirtle swim cap and triangle-shaped goggles, hands on hips, ready to dive in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Beside it stood Urshifu with goggles, a taut and graceful Milotic, and a lazy-looking Gastrodon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, dressed in Alolan-style beachwear, raised a hand beside them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Go!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Johan's shout, Gengar dove into the ocean first.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wearing a "Squirtle swim cap," how could it not win?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Splash splash splash\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Urshifu used textbook freestyle form, slicing through the water and quickly overtaking Gengar, even raising an eyebrow mockingly as it passed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unforgivable!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar was fuming.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But just as it was about to go all out, the water ahead parted\u8212?Milotic elegantly burst from the surface, shimmering with droplets as it formed a dazzling arc through the air.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
So fast?!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Well\u8230? at least I'm faster than Gastrodon\u8230? Gengar comforted itself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Splash\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Waves surged again, but this time from behind. Cynthia's Gastrodon rode a wave, overtaking Gengar and even flipping it in the water.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It surfaced, ripping off its Squirtle swim cap in frustration.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lies! All lies!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The vendor {\i
said} this cap would give it Squirtle-level speed!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Fine. I'll do it my way.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar's eyes spun craftily\u8212?this wasn't over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the beach, Cynthia and Caitlin reclined under a parasol, grinning at the aquatic showdown.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's expression was\u8230? exasperated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seriously, Gengar challenging three Water-types to a swimming race?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meloetta, now fully recovered, was even more excited than Gengar, cheering from the shore.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji yoji~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yoji (Larvitar) joined in, too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gengar looks like it's going to lose~~" Caitlin teased.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan glanced at her, unimpressed. "You're underestimating Gengar."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You think it can outswim Milotic or Gastrodon?" Caitlin raised an eyebrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garrr~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Garchomp, sunbathing in shades, snorted twice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No way Gengar was faster\u8212?but it had tricks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Garchomp knew what kind of Pok\u233?mon Gengar was.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the water, Milotic and Gastrodon were neck-and-neck, with Urshifu trailing slightly. Gengar was nowhere to be seen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Ka-kaah!!"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar suddenly burst from the waves near the finish, standing triumphantly on the reef, laughing maniacally.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh?" Caitlin blinked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia smiled. "It used Shadow Sneak."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cheating!" Caitlin huffed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No one said you couldn't use moves," Johan mimicked her earlier tone mockingly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gastrodon had used Surf, hadn't it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Caitlin was furious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Garchomp had a "called it" look\u8212?thank goodness it didn't join the race. How do you win when someone cheats?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Melo!!"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Yoji!!"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meloetta and Larvitar cheered loudly for Gengar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These fun antics happened a lot during their days in Undella Town.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With Gengar around, joy was inevitable\u8212?alongside frequent absurdity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, Johan didn't mind.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He always valued his Pok\u233?mon's interests more than just forcing them to train. Their joy often brought unexpected growth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for Meloetta\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After recovering, it hadn't left immediately. Perhaps it stayed out of gratitude\u8212?or maybe it simply enjoyed the fun.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But to show its thanks, Meloetta had quietly disappeared for half a day.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When it returned, it held an ancient-looking box, covered in dirt.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even its own face and body were smudged.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You went digging?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's Larvitar's favorite hobby.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yoji tilted its head\u8212?"Why didn't you invite me?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Melo~~"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meloetta danced through the air, beaming, and handed Johan the box.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What is it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan opened it with curiosity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The material was strange\u8212?wooden or stone?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Inside was something that made Larvitar's eyes go wide.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Y-Yoji\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It didn't know what it was\u8212?just that it smelled {\i
amazing}. It gulped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar peeked in too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"These markings\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia noticed the patterns and brushed off the dust, making them clearer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You recognize them?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As a scholar of mythology, Cynthia didn't just know Sinnoh lore\u8212?she'd studied Unova as well, even recently borrowing Shaga's {\b
DNA Splicers} for research.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmm\u8230?" She nodded slowly, then said, "They seem to signify a ritual for honoring the earth."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Honoring the earth?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's expression shifted as he looked at Meloetta.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Others might not know its past, but Johan did. Meloetta was deeply linked to the Forces of Nature.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It wasn't just connected to the Reveal Glass, which changed their forms\u8212?but also one of the few Pok\u233?mon able to calm them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tornadus and Thundurus fought on sight. Landorus usually mediated\u8212?but sometimes they all clashed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meloetta's song could soothe them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So this "earth ritual" box\u8230? could it be an offering left by ancient people to Landorus?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or maybe\u8230? something that {\i
belonged} to Landorus?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Melo~ Melo~~"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meloetta nodded eagerly and motioned that the gift was for Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for who could use it\u8212?well, that was obvious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar was already bouncing, eyes sparkling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I can feel the earth energy," Caitlin murmured, eyes closed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No doubt about it\u8212?a legendary artifact linked to Landorus!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And now, Meloetta had gifted it away.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Landorus\u8212?nicknamed "World's Strongest Bug"\u8212?despite being Ground/Flying, often carried the Bug-type move U-turn in battle for Intimidate support.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thus the meme.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's suspicion deepened. Giovanni's original "Storm Plan" had aimed for Landorus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A Ground-type matching "Earthbound Giovanni." A Bug-move user, fitting his ace\u8212?Beedrill.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ahem, back to the story.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Will it cause problems?" Johan asked cautiously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Melo~ Melo~~"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meloetta leaned in, resting her hands on Johan's cheeks and nuzzling him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Well then.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With such a heartfelt gift, how could he say no?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under Larvitar's eager gaze, Johan handed it the earthy, sand-like relic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Yoji!!"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar squealed with joy, kicking its little feet excitedly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan, however, felt a tinge of nervousness.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It already had a shard of the Earth Plate. Now it held Landorus's relic\u8212?the {\b
Land Stone}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Would it one day stomp and flatten a mountain?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Watching it stomp the sand, Johan half-expected a crater to form.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thankfully, it didn't.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But he made a firm decision.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Never} let Larvitar use any moves indoors\u8212?{\b
not one!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for now\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If something collapses, oh well\u8212?Caitlin's loaded anyway.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Larvitar's final evolution, Tyranitar, is Dark/Rock\u8230? but I feel like its Ground-type moves will be {\i
devastating} someday."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As long as it stands on solid ground\u8212?it will never fall!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, it's now the Pok\u233?mon of a man with both an Earth Plate shard {\i
and} the Land Stone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still\u8230? it's just a Larvitar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Eating at this level already? Johan had a headache.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Should he rush its evolution? Then it'll eat {\i
more}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But if he delays? It'll stockpile strength and still eat {\i
more}.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trapped either way.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the end, Johan decided to go with the flow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Worst case\u8230? he'd use all his championship prize money to feed Larvitar!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His hunger for the prize money just grew a little stronger.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
