{\qc
548: "Cold-Blooded" Boss Teacher Johan\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Different trainers have different battling styles\u8212?this applies to most trainers in the Pok\u233?mon world.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Take Flint, for example\u8212?classic case. If you're being nice, you'd call it a hot-blooded style; if you're being blunt, it's the reckless bruiser style. He specializes in dragging down the opponent's IQ to match his own, then relies on experience to win.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia, on the other hand, doesn't specialize in a single type, making her adaptable. Her key tactic is level suppression\u8212?many of her battles can be summed up in one phrase: "Garchomp steamroll."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She's not alone. Leon does the same. His whole tactical system revolves around one thing: "Max Charizard."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven represents the blend of academic tactics and traveler bonds, while Wallace leans toward flashy battling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In short, as a trainer's system of Pok\u233?mon grows, so does the style solidify.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These were the notes recorded by a League staffer responsible for compiling data during the "Youth Master World Championship."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When it came to Johan, this staffer hit a wall.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What exactly {\i
was} Teacher Johan's specialty?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He's dubbed a "Tactical Master" online and credited with developing and popularizing several well-known strategies.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But if you said he was a strategy specialist\u8230? yesterday's match didn't look tactical at all. It looked more like a "traveler-style" match\u8212?grabbing anything usable in the environment and improvising.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, I guess Teacher Johan's style is\u8230? dragging everyone down to a 'baby' level and beating them with his teaching experience! Yep, that's it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Satisfied with his conclusion, the staffer published the report online.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With the high heat around the championship, even small news sparked discussion\u8212?let alone something official from the League.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Damn, that summary of Teacher Johan's style? It's {\i
{\b
spot on}}."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"LOL! Bump this post! Bump it!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Teacher Johan's tactic: drag everyone to 'baby level' and beat them with superior teaching? {\i
{\b
Genius!}}"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Give that staffer a promotion!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes! Promote them now!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Meanwhile, the League also posted the matchups for the top 64 moving into the top 32.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Next opponent is\u8230? Piers?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing his next opponent, Johan raised an eyebrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He knew of Piers\u8212?Marnie's older brother, Spikemuth's Gym Leader in Galar, a rock singer dubbed "Melancholy Piers."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though a Gym Leader, his strength was not to be underestimated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Galar didn't have Elite Fours; its League was managed by the Champion and League President, so Gym Leaders were unusually strong, with fierce competition.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Like Kabut, who Johan had beaten at the Lily of the Valley Conference\u8212?he lost his Gym Leader post due to one such competition.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Galar {\i
had} Elites, Piers might've been a top candidate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Notably, Piers didn't use Dynamax.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Galar's League President Rose tried to integrate Dynamax into Gym battles to boost economic interest, but Spikemuth's Dynamax energy well had dried up\u8212?no more Dynamax available.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As such, Rose gave up on Spikemuth. No revenue, no interest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, under pressure, Piers stayed on as Gym Leader and, through his charisma and music, helped support the town.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thus, he not only rejected Dynamax but actively opposed it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was one of the few strong trainers in Galar who didn't rely on Dynamax.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And even so, in the Galar Champion's Cup, he beat Kabut and nearly beat "Son of the Storm" Raihan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Raihan himself highly regarded Piers' strength.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And now, in the Youth Master World Championship, where Dynamax wasn't allowed, Piers' strength was near-equal to Raihan's.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
