{\b
{\qc
555: A New Profession\u8212?Commentator\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a day's rest, the quarterfinals of the "Young Masters Exhibition Tournament" officially began!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan and his group arrived at the stadium.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Before they could even sit down, tournament staff approached Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Johan, you don't have a match today\u8212?would you be willing to serve as a commentator?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Commentator?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan blinked in surprise.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yesterday's commentary had been handled by Unova's Elite Four member Grimsley. It was time for him to take a break.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for asking Champion Alder... the organizers were afraid that by the time the match was over, he might still be asleep.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Other contestants who'd already lost could be considered, but... Johan was extremely popular right now, and known as the "Master of Strategy." Surely, he'd bring professional insight to the table.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ahem, it's a paid gig," the staffer added.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Say no more.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ahem, I'm just doing my part for the League. Do I {\i
look} like someone who cares about the money?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Totally not about the paycheck. Just a change of perspective for watching the matches.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With that, Johan was led to the commentator's booth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Whoa! It's Professor Johan as the commentator?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A keen-eyed spectator noticed Johan taking the seat and excitement rippled through the stands.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But while the audience was thrilled, all eyes soon turned to the first match of the day:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Cynthia vs. Lucian.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under the vibrant energy of the host, the two Sinnoh trainers entered the battlefield.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Clack, clack\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucian, with pale purple hair, a burgundy suit, brown shoes, and a scholarly air, walked out with a book in hand. He looked composed and serious.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He adjusted his glasses and smiled gently at Cynthia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan immediately leaned into the mic, "Let me translate Lucian's smile for everyone\u8212?it means 'please go easy on me.'"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucian nearly tripped. He wiped sweat from his brow awkwardly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"C'mon, Professor Johan! We're close, but do you really have to interpret {\i
that}?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pfft\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Best commentary ever!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is what real analysis sounds like! Everyone else, take notes!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the other side\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Clack, clack\u8212?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia's golden hair cascaded like sunlight, her elegant face radiant with confidence. Wearing a sleek black trench coat, she walked out like royalty.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And here we have Cynthia's smile," Johan continued, "which translates to: 'No problem at all.'"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Professor Johan is hilarious!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Right on point! He's a psychologist\u8212?he's reading them like books!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia smiled up at Johan in the booth\u8212?her grin seemed to deepen slightly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The referee signaled the battle was about to begin, and both trainers readied their Pok\u233? Balls.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The host, worried about losing their job to Johan, quickly jumped back in:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Both trainers are in position! The battle is about to ignite!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lucian's first Pok\u233?mon is out\u8212?it's Bronzong!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And Cynthia's opening choice is... Garchomp!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia started with {\i
Garchomp}?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Johan hadn't seen that coming.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar floated out of Johan's shadow and plopped beside him, pretending to adjust a bowtie.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Commentary? Please\u8212?he was made for this.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Garchomp, time to dance!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"GARRR\u8212?!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Garchomp snarled, sweeping its deadly blades across the field and locking eyes with the booth for a moment\u8212?terrifying.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucian kept a poker face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Come on! Gengar was the one taunting\u8212?you don't need to glare at {\i
us}!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The referee's flag dropped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Bronzong, use Trick Room!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Garchomp, Dragon Dive!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Classic openers\u8212?Trick Room's eerie glow began warping the battlefield.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Garchomp took flight before it could activate, roaring through the sky like a comet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Here it comes!" Johan clenched the mic. "Tear it all down, Garchomp!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the stunned silence of the crowd, Garchomp {\i
shredded} the Trick Room field.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's {\i
not} supposed to happen\u8212?but this is Pok\u233?mon battle!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With that line, Johan excused all the times he had pulled equally bizarre stunts in battle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The game isn't about perfect logic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If it were just number crunching, we'd all be playing simulations.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But in Pok\u233?mon battles, there's room for:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Type disadvantage victories\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Standing up when you should be KO'd\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dodging when it should be impossible\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That last-second counterattack\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's the thrill.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So\u8212?Cynthia, charge!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And the result?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Cynthia defeated Lucian decisively.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucian was more of a cerebral, academy-style tactician.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When you've got enough power, strategy can dominate raw aggression.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But when power is close?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The hot-blooded fighters can flip the board.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Especially against {\i
Cynthia's} unreasonable Garchomp.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As Lucian later said: "She tore up my Trick Room\u8212?how the hell am I supposed to fight that?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Neither trainer used Mega Evolution, meaning Cynthia still had hidden cards.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though the tournament was global, there were subtle regional rivalries.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Fans naturally cheered more for contestants from their own regions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lucian lost, but at least Cynthia didn't reveal too many tricks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Today had four matches:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia vs. Lucian\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon vs. Drasna\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Caitlin vs. Acerola\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven vs. Malva\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon may have abandoned the "Everything revolves around Gigantamax Charizard" strategy, but "Everything revolves around {\i
regular} Charizard" was still on the table.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Drasna, while powerful, didn't have enough to compete.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon wasn't a mono-type trainer\u8212?against Drasna's Ghosts, he had plenty of tools.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Like Aegislash.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And Dragapult, the so-called "True Giratina."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for Caitlin vs. Acerola?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Caitlin was Psychic, Acerola was Ghost\u8212?ghost had the type edge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But unlike Marshal, Caitlin wasn't completely walled. She had options.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And being a literal psychic didn't hurt. She advanced to the Top 8.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then came {\b
Steven vs. Malva.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Malva was Kalos' future Fire Elite Four\u8212?on paper, she had the type advantage.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Steven didn't just run Steel-types. He was all about Steel-Ground-Rock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Combined with his sheer strength, it wasn't even close.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tomorrow's matches?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Way more unpredictable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Lance vs. Wallace}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Flint vs. Rika}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Lorelei vs. Diantha}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Johan vs. Raihan}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Facing Raihan, huh?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar practiced his vocals with Meloetta.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sat on the porch, calculating expenses.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar waddled up to him. The bench was taller than it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It leapt, clung to the bench edge, and struggled to climb up\u8212?finally flopping into Johan's lap.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's up?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan switched the screen to tournament matchups.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar opened its mouth and dropped a half-fist-sized brown stone\u8212?Earth Plate fragment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wait, what?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was a {\i
chunk} missing!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It bit into a Plate?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You {\i
ate} it? Or absorbed it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji!" Larvitar made a gesture like turning gears, then stood tall, arms akimbo.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course it absorbed it! Duh!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan's expression twitched.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This kid... it {\i
ate} a {\i
Plate fragment}?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Does that make it a {\i
walking fragment} now?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What happens when a full Plate appears?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still\u8212?looking at its proud little face, Johan couldn't scold it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Good job, Larvitar."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe he should send the little guy into the match tomorrow?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Raihan was called the "Child of Weather," a master of sun, sandstorm, and rain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe Larvitar could seize the field?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If not, there was always Ninetales as backup.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Wanna give it a shot tomorrow?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar's eyes sparkled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Power!!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing that, Johan figured he better slap an Everstone on it. The last thing he needed was spontaneous evolution.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Aside from the Plate fragment, Larvitar still had the Land Stone from Landorus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If it could absorb one, it could definitely handle the other.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Once it did... its power would be terrifying.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe it's not so bad if it never flies?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan froze.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Am I crazy? Why would I think something like that?!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tomorrow\u8212?Top 8, day two!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
