{\b
{\qc
556: Johan vs. Raihan \u8211? Battle of the Weather?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Lance vs. Wallace!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was the first time since Johan began watching the "Young Masters World Championship" that he witnessed a battle between two future Champions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance needed no introduction. Though his Champion path in Kanto was blocked by "that one obstacle," once the Dragon King returned to Johto, he officially became its Champion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for Wallace\u8212?true, Steven handed the title over to him, but one couldn't just hand the Champion title to anyone. Wallace {\i
earned} it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So, this battle was bound to be exciting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Honestly, Lance's strength was undeniable. He may have "debuted early," but this wasn't a game or an anime\u8212?this was the {\i
real} Pok\u233?mon world. His roster wasn't just Pok\u233?mon with "dragon" in their names.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In addition to Dragonite, Charizard, Gyarados (the red one), and Aerodactyl, he also had Salamence and Altaria\u8212?both dragon types.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Okay, calling him the "Flying-type Champion" wasn't wrong.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wallace, on the other hand, ran a team of water-types\u8212?none of which were pseudo-legendaries. So in pure power, Lance had the edge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Plus, Wallace had one "flaw." Not really a flaw, but\u8230? his battling style leaned heavily toward {\i
grace}. Everything\u8212?moves, posture, expression\u8212?was stunning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It worked well against weaker opponents. But against Lance? That obsession with beauty dulled his edge in real battle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the end, Lance took the win.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia summarized it succinctly: "Lance simply had more battle experience."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yes\u8212?{\i
Cynthia} was today's commentator. Since she had already finished her match and was hugely popular, the organizers brought her in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After the Lance vs. Wallace battle ended, it was Flint vs. Rika.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Fire vs. Ground\u8212?advantage: Rika.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Up next, let's welcome from the Paldea region\u8212?Rika!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under the spotlight, Rika strode out, hands in pockets and smiling gently. She was tall, poised, and... another one with mass appeal.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And now, from the Sinnoh region\u8212?Flint!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint walked out with the same hands-in-pockets swagger, but with a totally different vibe: chaotic and scrappy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His fiery, aggressive battle style had earned him the nickname\u8212?{\i
"The Flame-Fro'd Wild Card!"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Miss Cynthia, can you comment on these two?" the host asked expertly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia smiled and nodded. As the two prepared, she said:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Miss Rika\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She gazed at the poised figure and continued:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Her battle style reminds me of Bertha of the Elite Four. She's incredibly strong."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bertha! One of the rare Ground-type Elite Four members, known for calm and precise strategy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And as for Flint\u8212?" Cynthia glanced at the overly familiar face and smirked. "Watch out for his Infernape."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint, who was eagerly waiting for praise, nearly choked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
High praise for Rika. For him? Just "watch out for Infernape"?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, Cynthia's words made it clear\u8212?Flint's Infernape had left a strong impression.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Trainers, prepare for battle!" the referee signaled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Go, Magmortar!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint led with a pure Fire-type.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rika smiled gently and threw out her Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Whiscash!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Water-Ground\u8212?Whiscash!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The type match was brutal. Whiscash hard-counters Magmortar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Normally, Flint might tense up against such an opponent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But in battle mode?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
He didn't care who he faced.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His expression said it all: {\i
Bring it on.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Magmortar, Fire Blast!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Whiscash, Earthquake!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They clashed immediately\u8212?classic Flint.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As expected, Magmortar was defeated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Flint was unfazed and kept going!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Next came Arcanine, who lowered Whiscash's Attack with Intimidate, set up Sunny Day, then launched a Solar Beam to take Whiscash down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Reckless? Maybe. Dumb? Not quite.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan might've withdrawn Arcanine to reuse Intimidate later\u8212?but that wasn't Flint's style.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And surprisingly, Rika's battle tempo started shifting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint's relentless aggression forced her to respond in kind.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Eventually, Flint traded Arcanine and Rapidash to eliminate Rika's Camerupt.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That left him with just one Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And of course, it was Infernape.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rika countered with her ace\u8212?Clodsire!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cute. Dopey-looking. But tough.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She'd clearly researched Flint and knew Infernape was his strongest Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So\u8212?she went straight for her trump card: Terastallization!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The first {\i
Terastallization} of the tournament!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rika raised her radiant Tera Orb. Sparkling dust and mysterious energy filled the arena. She hurled the orb toward Clodsire.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Clink\u8212?clink\u8212?clink!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Crystals formed around Clodsire, enveloping it in brilliant shards.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When the energy settled, Clodsire's entire body gleamed like a gemstone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A massive crystal resembling the {\i
Earth} floated above its head\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Tera Type: Ground!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The crowd went wild. It was gorgeous!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Wallace's eyes sparkled\u8212?{\i
perfect} for Contest style!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hahahaha\u8212?now {\i
that's} what I'm talking about!" Flint grinned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Infernape, show them what we're made of\u8212?Flare Blitz!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint's eyes lit up like fire, and Infernape responded, blazing toward Clodsire.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The crowd roared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Would Infernape's sheer power win out, or would Tera Clodsire stand tall?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
