{\qc
574: Gengar the \u8220?Invincible\u8221? Influencer\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan had defeated Steven and clinched the "Master vs. Student" battle, securing his spot in the finals!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The match instantly became the hottest topic online.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Most of the discussion centered around Ceruledge and Armarouge's form switching.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At first, viewers were already amazed by the fact that Ceruledge and Armarouge could switch forms freely\u8212?but then Johan showcased something even more shocking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ceruledge could wield both sword and cannon simultaneously?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cannon for range, sword for melee!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Swordsmen fear ranged casters, and casters fear being rushed\u8212?yet Ceruledge could do both, a total combat powerhouse.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After Ceruledge first showed off form switching, Charcadet's popularity had surged. Now, with this new hybrid form, the hype was even more explosive.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Many trainers from Paldea were now begging Johan to please write a book\u8212?no, publish a research paper, because everyone was drooling over his techniques.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Aside from Ceruledge, Urshifu, who had mastered both Single Strike and Rapid Strike Styles, was another hot topic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not because people expected to chase after Kubfu like they did Charcadet\u8212?it's a legendary Pok\u233?mon, after all, only obtainable from Master Mustard on the Isle of Armor.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Instead, the buzz came from Leon's phone call\u8212?especially his use of "Little Jojo" as a nickname.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for the Mega Metagross vs. Mega Gengar clash?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was, hands down, the most intense and exciting moment of the entire match.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This proved one thing clearly:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mega Evolution is still the dominant power-up method in high-level matches.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yes, Z-Moves and Terastallization exist. But compared to Mega Evolution, both have their limitations.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Z-Moves only power up one move, offering unique effects but limited use.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Terastallization alters or boosts typing\u8212?great for counterplay, but Tera Orbs require huge energy input. Outside Paldea and Blueberry Academy, there's no way to recharge them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Mega Evolution, however, boosts stats, typing, and abilities, providing broad and dynamic enhancements.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moreover, Mega Evolution's power ceiling and floor are determined by the trainer's bond with their Pok\u233?mon. For trainers passionate about battling, that emotional connection matters just as much as raw power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It's perfect for trainers\u8212?and Pok\u233?mon\u8212?who excel under pressure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, Mega Evolution has a major drawback: very few Pok\u233?mon can use it. Unlike Z-Moves and Terastallization, which are more universally applicable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dynamax/Gigantamax, in contrast, applies to all Pok\u233?mon and offers solid boosts\u8212?but it only lasts three turns, and can only be triggered in Galar's special Power Spots.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As of now, there's been no known case of combining multiple power-ups.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No Mega Evolution + Z-Move. No Mega + Tera.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The reason? It would physically overwhelm the trainer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even Mega Evolution alone already puts huge strain on most trainers. Many can barely sustain it even with the right Mega Stone and Key Stone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Add another power-up on top? The trainer might collapse before the Pok\u233?mon does.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And the Pok\u233?mon would also face major physical and mental burdens.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Post-Match, Lunchtime.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gengar."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan stopped the purple chubby shadow trying to sneak off, tiptoeing exaggeratedly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah\u8230??"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar awkwardly turned around, scratching its head and forcing a smile\u8212?pretending not to know what Johan wanted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan didn't say a word. He crossed his arms, sat back in his chair, and smiled knowingly, humming through his nose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That smile terrified Gengar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar glanced left, right, avoiding eye contact.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under the pressure of Johan's silent stare, Gengar cracked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, it raised a hand and pointed skyward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Look! A UFO!}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cha?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Where? Roto?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tyrunt, Tinkaton, and Dragonite all got fooled, turning toward the window.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom even readied its camera to film the "UFO."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8230?There was no UFO.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And Gengar tried to use the distraction to escape.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He casually grabbed Rotom and clicked a snapshot of the empty space in front of him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
CLICK\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On Rotom's screen: a photo of Gengar posing with a peace sign.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roto\u8230??"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom was utterly confused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the same time, Johan's other hand latched onto Gengar's head spike.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar blinked\u8212?then forced a sheepish grin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Trying to run?" Johan chuckled scornfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~ Ka-kaah~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar frantically waved its hands.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\i
Run? Me? No way! I was just really excited by the UFO\u8230?}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But Johan's stare silenced him again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar raised both hands: {\i
I surrender.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, with a roll of its tongue, it pulled out the DNA Splicers that Shaga had entrusted to Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan just smiled\u8212?he already knew Gengar had it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar reluctantly rolled out a pitch-black stone\u8212?the orb Alder had secretly given it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's this?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan took the orb, curious, and let go of Gengar's horn.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar slumped, ears drooping, nervously fidgeting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Originally, the DNA Splicers had no reaction when Gengar studied them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But with the black orb, the Splicers began to respond\u8212?and Gengar started "learning" things from it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't tell me it's a Dragon Stone?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nearby, Dragonite perked up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the games, Dragon Stones were the dormant forms of Zekrom and Reshiram.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In Black/White 1, there were no DNA Splicers\u8212?just the "Light Stone" and "Dark Stone."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
These functioned similarly to Splicers.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Could this be Zekrom's Dark Stone?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If so, Alder must've retrieved it from a museum or from Dragonspiral Tower.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Either way, it was black and resonated with the Splicers\u8212?most likely Zekrom's stone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"How did you learn from it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar perked up, pulling out its phone, showing Johan a picture.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Onscreen: a massive head eavesdropping.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Digital Pet Giratina!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giratina blinked as it realized Gengar had exposed it\u8212?slowly turned to stare at Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A chill ran down its spine.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
[NOT MY FAULT.]\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The screen flickered, then went black. Giratina vanished.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: "\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
You little traitor\u8230? you're not done stirring up trouble in Sinnoh, and now you're poking around Unova?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Giratina, the "Screen-Peeping Dragon," lived up to its name.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Still, Gengar hadn't learned anything dangerous, so Johan didn't press.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kids\u8212?Pok\u233?mon included\u8212?deserve some secrets, as long as they're not harmful.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Maybe Gengar had just wanted to surprise him with a cool new skill?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright. Go play."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Confirmed Gengar had gained a new skill\u8212?good enough.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar ran off gleefully, likely to message Giratina and explain its betrayal.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan rubbed his chin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He used to worry Gengar might be negatively influenced by Giratina\u8230?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But now it seemed like Gengar was influencing Giratina instead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"After all, when lives connect, something always grows from it\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In its own way, Gengar's "influence" might be another form of invincibility.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Later That Evening.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
CLICK\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Teacher."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven had arrived for dinner at Johan's place.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Behind him, Metagross carried bags of groceries with all four claws, maximizing efficiency.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Steven, hand the bags to Rotom. Find a seat."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Understood."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ro-Rotom?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"GONG-GONG\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rotom looked at the massive grocery load\u8212?then at itself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8230?How?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just then, a voice from the kitchen: "Garchomp, give him a hand."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"GARHHH\u8212?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Garchomp, who had been resting on the floor, got up with a sigh and helped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven noticed Cynthia leaning against the kitchen door.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why is Cynthia at the kitchen door?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On the couch, Lucian said nothing. Flint, bruised and bandaged, motioned toward a sign on the door.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven looked:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gengar and Cynthia: Not Allowed Inside!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"COUGH!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven nearly choked on his water.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Only Johan would dare post something like that.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the kitchen, Johan hummed to Meloetta's classical tune, commanding Rotom and chatting with Cynthia.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He missed the Indeedee siblings\u8212?prep work was easier with them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Against Lance, Ice-types are important," Johan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He and Cynthia were planning for her battle tomorrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You and Lorelei both said that," Cynthia sipped her Moomoo Milk tea.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Lorelei, huh?" Johan chuckled. "Of course. It's the Dodo Bird."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Somehow, "Dodo Bird" had become Lance's nickname among their circle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No one knew how it started, but Johan claimed innocence.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Everyone had nicknames.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lance: "Dodo Bird"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Lorelei: "Old Lady"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Flint: "Pyro-Puff"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia: "Boss Lady"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Leon: "Mr. Commercial"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan: {\i
None of this is my fault.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Your Glaceon will be key."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia's Glaceon was strong\u8212?she'd trained it seriously even as an Eevee.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After all, her screen name was "[Eevee Eats Cabbage]," showing her deep love for Eevee.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Still," Johan added, "If you get a chance, try to catch a Fairy-type."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia wasn't a mono-type trainer, but she lacked a Fairy-type in her roster.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Fairy, like Steel, Ghost, Dark, and Normal, offered immunity matchups\u8212?great against specific opponents.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Steven had Mawile, for instance. Give it a Mega Stone, and it becomes a "Dragon Slayer."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia's eyes lit up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Any suggestions?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She'd been considering it\u8212?but hadn't found the right opportunity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ice Ninetales?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She liked it, but\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're not Lorelei," Johan said. "No need to counter Lance so directly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Alolan Ninetales had great synergy\u8212?Fairy + Ice plus Snow Warning\u8212?but Cynthia didn't use snow synergy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Also, she already had Glaceon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan thought for a moment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Togekiss."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Togekiss?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fairy/Flying. Great support or pivot. And 'Serene Grace' is common."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cynthia considered it\u8212?imagining a cheerful little Togepi\u8212?then smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sounds fun."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
