"It's fine, Ninetales. It's just filled with Terastallization energy."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing this, Ninetales nodded thoughtfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
When it came to unknown, untrusted powers... it believed caution was necessary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For a while, it would keep a close eye on this Tera Orb to prevent any unexpected changes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar bit its finger.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tera Orb... if it's an orb, can it be eaten?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No, you can't eat it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan sighed and lightly tapped Larvitar's head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Theoretically, Terastallization crystals could be considered a type of crystal, and crystals... could be viewed as a kind of mineral, like diamonds, which were listed in Larvitar's diet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The power utilized in Terastallization belonged to the legendary Pok\u233?mon Terapagos.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Terapagos, a Pok\u233?mon that lived two million years ago, could transform energy into hard crystals. The Paldea region utilized this power to achieve Terastallization.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
