614: Regice & Johan: This Was Worth It\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"REGI!!!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The enormous roar echoed across the small island, a terrifying aura wrapped in frost sweeping everywhere. The ice titan Regice, standing at least seven or eight meters tall, had all seven lights on its face flashing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Don't stand so tall, crouch down a bit."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, a voice came from the shadow at Regice's feet, with a hint of resignation in the tone.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing this, Regice immediately stopped its howling and obediently crouched down, trying to maintain eye level with the human at its feet, though this was almost impossible to achieve.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At this moment, the area around the small island was completely covered in a hazy frost mist, preventing the International Police and League Police outside from seeing what was happening inside. If they could see, their jaws would certainly drop.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The previously raging Regice, who seemed to control all the cold in the world, was now so docilely crouching on the ground that it looked somewhat comical.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moreover, if anyone could understand Regice's "expression" right now, they would definitely notice that its gaze was exceptionally clear.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clearly obedient.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be honest, Regice didn't want to be like this, but the human before it was somewhat inhuman. It had lost count of how many times it had recovered its condition.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Plus, all of his Pok\u233?mon were like they were on steroids, hitting it with attacks while going "Ku ku" at it, using all sorts of moves without repeating, and somehow coordinating with each other quite well.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Especially that little one with the V-shape on its head that sat on the human's shoulder.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It looked harmless and was always smiling, with a "I'm so worried about you" expression, and then each time it would energize Regice, allowing it to recover, only to continue being tormented.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The key point was...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While its body's energy was restored, the mental impact hadn't improved at all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Regice now felt physically fine, but mentally extremely fatigued, somewhat wanting to sleep...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Actually...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Regice could have continued resisting, but as it gradually regained clarity, it increasingly sensed the aura of Regigigas from this human.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was the aura of their "creator," along with a friendly aura from the human. This was the main reason why Regice had become so obedient now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And the person standing beside Regice's feet was, of course, Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan glanced at his phone and sighed helplessly, "This coffee is completely cold."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Calculating the time, even with the recent rise in temperature, the coffee prepared by Gardevoir must have gone completely cold by now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This is what happens when you try to show off unnecessarily. If you fail, you only embarrass yourself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To think he'd try to warm coffee while taking down Regice...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan looked at the now docile Regice and said using his aura power:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You need to compensate me."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Regi?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Regice's lights flashed back and forth, as if a Psyduck-style question mark appeared above its head.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Compensate?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Wait, I'm the victim here...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Tell me, how did you wake up?" Johan found a relatively clean ice block nearby, brushed off the snow, and sat down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To be fair, in the special episodes, Steven had expended considerable effort to awaken the three titans sleeping in the Hoenn region.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although this world must have significant differences from the special episodes Johan knew, he didn't believe that a simple ruin exploration team could easily awaken Regice and make it so angry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Regi..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Regice's lights flashed again. It didn't know what had happened either.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It just felt like it had a strange dream, dreaming that a large number of meteorites fell from the sky, boundless fury was released in the sky, the earth began to sink, and all their previous efforts were destroyed in an instant.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, tensing up in the dream, it woke up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A dream?" Johan looked puzzled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And what kind of strange dream was this?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A large number of meteorites falling...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Was it referring to the meteorite incident?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or maybe...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Unfortunately, although Johan could construct dreams through hypnosis, he was completely clueless about interpreting the meaning of dreams.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In any case, Regice had a nightmare and then jolted itself awake?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As for the League's ruin exploration team, was it purely bad luck?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It feels like it's foretelling something..." Johan gently rubbed his chin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At this moment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Larvitar cautiously walked to Regice's feet and tapped its icy pillar-like foot a couple of times with its small hand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yoji!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Time to eat!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
