616: Preparing a Little 'Surprise' for the Llama\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
July 1st, evening, the sun slanting westward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Twinleaf Town.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ding dong\u8212?Ding dong\u8212?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The towering Space-Time Towers played a melodious tune that echoed throughout Twinleaf Town, announcing the coming sunset.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At this moment, a dark figure stood atop the twin towers, casting a long shadow in the setting sun.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Darkrai's body flowed like clouds, with a faint light flickering deep in its azure eyes, carrying a trace of confusion and a hint of gravity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Something was about to happen, something big!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the guardian of Twinleaf Town, Darkrai, who was once the first to sense the anomalies in time and space, once again detected a disturbance in the space-time continuum.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Could those two be fighting again?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hmm?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Just as the thought arose, Darkrai sensed a familiar aura entering the Sinnoh region.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was all too familiar with this aura.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although sensing this aura often accompanied some not-so-good events, the Pok\u233? Blocks that person brought were truly delicious...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Moreover, through confrontations with some powerful beings, Darkrai could feel that its strength, which hadn't changed in decades, had improved somewhat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was probably what that guy often said... when life encounters life, something is always born.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is it Dialga or Palkia this time?" Darkrai felt a subtle rise of fighting spirit within.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was no longer the same being that had to face the Space-Time Dragon duo alone!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A black mist surged from its body as Darkrai rode the shadows of the Space-Time Towers, soaring on the evening breeze toward the direction of that aura.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Be it Dialga or Palkia...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"As long as it's not Arceus, I'll crush them all!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a long howl, Darkrai disappeared into the shadows of Twinleaf Town.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Night fell.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Treading on the pristine snow, Johan arrived at Snowpoint City in the Sinnoh region.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Waiting for him there, besides Lucian who had come for work, were several familiar faces.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The current probationary Elite Four members of the Sinnoh region, Flint and Aaron.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Teacher Johan!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They were all quite familiar with each other, but having not met for over a month since parting in Unova, they appeared rather enthusiastic.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After briefly exchanging greetings, Lucian said:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The boss is still on Mt. Coronet. She supposedly discovered some hidden mysterious ruins and should be here soon."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As he spoke, he glanced at the time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan nodded, "I know."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although one was in Sinnoh and the other in Hoenn after parting in Unova, they had maintained contact.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After returning to Sinnoh, Cynthia had taken her Pok\u233?mon to Mt. Coronet for training.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the summit of Mt. Coronet, the coldest and harshest environment in the entire Sinnoh region, wild Pok\u233?mon were few, but whenever one appeared, it was usually extremely powerful.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Battling against nature and powerful wild Pok\u233?mon\u8212?this was Cynthia's current goal and direction.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Of course, there were rumors of ancient ruins at the mysterious summit of Mt. Coronet, which was also one of the things Cynthia, as a mythology scholar, wanted to pursue and explore.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's go see Regigigas first," Johan said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So, the group headed to Snowpoint Temple.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Although night had fallen, because Regigigas's presence was so important, Sinnoh League staff had already set up a cordon outside Snowpoint Temple under Lucian's arrangement, and brightened the lights.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From a distance, one could see the ten-meter-tall Regigigas sitting in the snow, staring blankly, motionless.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since Regigigas hadn't shown any hostility or done anything out of line, the League didn't dare make too many moves.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Outside the cordon, Johan encountered another familiar face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Pyramid King of the Hoenn Battle Frontier, Brandon!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He seemed to be discussing something with the Snowpoint Temple Shrine Maiden.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Mr. Brandon?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah, Teacher Johan, you've arrived." Brandon and the Shrine Maiden also noticed Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As the owner of the three Regi titans and someone with a keen interest in ruins and historical matters, Brandon had immediately flown in on his Battle Pyramid upon learning of Regigigas's awakening in Snowpoint Temple.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Snowpoint Temple Shrine Maiden visibly relaxed upon seeing Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Last time, when Regigigas awakened, it was this Teacher Johan who had pacified it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Shrine Maiden said: "After awakening, Regigigas just sat there motionless. We couldn't communicate with it, so..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She had already tried to communicate with Regigigas but to no avail.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is it possible," Johan glanced at the obedient giant, "that it's just awake but not fully awake?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hmm?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Both the Shrine Maiden and Brandon were taken aback.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'll go check."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Saying this, Johan walked alone toward the cordon. Just as he was about to present his "International Police Inspector" credentials, the staff had already lifted the cordon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Teacher Johan!" The person seemed somewhat excited.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Thank you," Johan expressed his gratitude.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Feeling that my face is more effective than my ID, he thought as he entered the restricted area.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar floated out from the shadows, gazing up and down at the giant before them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Regigigas."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan approached Regigigas, feeling a pressure entirely different from Regice, and attempted communication using his aura power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
However, Regigigas remained motionless, with only its signal lights flashing at an extremely slow pace. Otherwise, Johan would have thought it was still asleep.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After a brief contemplation, he gave Gengar a look.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gengar immediately understood, opening its mouth to produce a box of Pok\u233? Blocks which it handed to Johan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ka-kaah~~(\u969?`)_\u19988?~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
