In front of him, Regieleki, less than 1.5 meters tall - more accurately, only 1.2 meters - hung its head low, its signal lights flashing embarrassedly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"...So, without my permission, don't randomly charge Rotom in the future!" Johan said seriously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Regi... Regieleki..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Regieleki nodded honestly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It didn't know either - it had just felt Rotom increase its electrical output earlier and thought it was trying to do something, so it helped out. Who knew...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Draaa~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dragonite smiled foolishly nearby, patting Regieleki's shoulder to indicate it was fine.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan was in great shape and couldn't be seriously hurt by a fall. Rotom-Bike's quality was excellent too, and if worst came to worst, Tinkaton could help repair it. No big problem.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eleki..." Regieleki cautiously glanced at Johan and nodded again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Johan knew Regieleki hadn't done it intentionally, but he still needed to give proper warnings. Otherwise... this time it was just a bicycle, but next time if it was a car or airplane, wouldn't that... make them fly even faster?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
